  "raw": {
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Seed-Analyst-III_R20168": {
      "title": "Seed Analyst III",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-05\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Seed Analyst III Job Group: Merit Required Minimum Qualifications: • Registered Seed Technologists (RST) and/or AOSA Certified (Purity and Germination) Analyst with a minimum of four years of experience testing a wide range of species; or Degree in Biological Sciences, Botany, Plant Sciences, or a related field from which one has acquired an extensive knowledge in all areas of seed analysis or equivalent post-secondary education. Job Description: The Seed Science Center at Iowa State University is seeking an experienced Seed Analyst III to join our seed testing laboratory team. This position combines advanced technical seed testing with responsibility for coordinating laboratory activities, providing technical guidance to other analysts, and resolving complex testing challenges. The successful candidate will apply specialized knowledge and independent judgment across a wide range of crop species while contributing to method development, quality assurance, and continuous improvement.   The Seed Science Center and Seed Lab are internationally recognized for excellence in seed testing, research, training, accuracy, timely results, and customer service.   What You'll Do Perform specialized seed quality testing and analysis on a wide range of agricultural, vegetable, flower, tree, native, and specialty seed species in accordance with applicable industry rules, regulatory requirements, and laboratory procedures. Identify, evaluate, and classify seeds, seedlings, and other botanical materials within assigned areas of expertise, using technical references, laboratory collections, and professional judgment to resolve complex or unusual findings. Interpret seed testing rules and regulatory requirements to determine appropriate testing methods, classifications, and reporting procedures, exercising independent judgment when established procedures do not address specific testing needs. Evaluate testing results, investigate discrepancies, and determine when additional examination or retesting is necessary to ensure technical accuracy and reliability. Coordinate daily laboratory workflow by prioritizing samples, assigning and monitoring work, and maintaining testing schedules and turnaround times. Provide technical guidance, training, and direction to laboratory staff and student employees; verify technical competency and support consistent application of testing procedures and quality standards. Lead or contribute to the development, evaluation, and implementation of new or revised testing methods, procedures, and laboratory workflows. Support laboratory quality assurance and accreditation activities, including audits, proficiency testing, corrective actions, equipment calibration, and maintenance of procedures and quality records. Maintain laboratory resources and participate in professional development, technical organizations, and Seed Science Center educational and outreach activities.   Preferred Qualifications Registered Seed Technologist (RST) or AOSA Certified Seed Analyst in Purity or Germination. Significant experience performing specialized seed testing and interpreting applicable testing rules and procedures. Experience independently performing complex seed testing, interpreting technical standards, and resolving non-routine testing issues. Experience coordinating laboratory activities, training other analysts, or providing technical guidance and oversight.   Why Join Us? The Seed Science Center brings together faculty, staff, and students from across disciplines including agronomy, plant pathology, horticulture, and engineering, creating a collaborative environment recognized worldwide for leadership in seed science and technology. The Seed Lab has served seed companies, farmers, and researchers across the United States and internationally for more than 100 years. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: 12 Original Posting Date: November 5, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 15, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20168 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Seed-Analyst-II_R20167": {
      "title": "Seed Analyst II",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-05\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Seed Analyst II Job Group: Merit Required Minimum Qualifications: • Two years experience in seed analysis, which includes one year as a Seed Analyst I or equivalent; or Any combination of post high school education and work experience totaling two years from which one can acquire a working knowledge of seed laws, the “Rules for Testing Seeds” and methods and problems associated with analysis of seeds for labeling purposes. Job Description: The Seed Science Center at Iowa State University is seeking a Seed Analyst II to join our seed testing laboratory team. This position offers the opportunity to work with a wide range of agricultural, vegetable, flower, native, and specialty crop seeds, applying biological knowledge and analytical skills to evaluate seed quality. The successful candidate will perform specialized seed testing, contribute to laboratory quality assurance and method improvements, and help train other laboratory staff and student employees. This is a hands-on technical position with opportunities to develop expertise in the specialized field of seed science.   The Seed Science Center and Seed Lab are internationally recognized for excellence in seed testing, research, training, accuracy, timely results, and customer service.   What You'll Do Perform seed quality testing on a wide variety of agricultural, vegetable, flower, tree, native, and specialty crop seeds in accordance with applicable industry standards and laboratory procedures. Independently evaluate tests, recognize abnormal test results or inconsistencies, and exercise technical judgment to identify when additional examinations or testing may be necessary, consulting with senior analysts as appropriate. Prepare testing materials and conditions, monitor laboratory equipment and environments, and maintain accurate testing records and data in laboratory information systems. Manage assigned testing workloads, monitor sample progress and turnaround times, and assist with daily laboratory workflow and priorities. Provide technical guidance and training to other laboratory staff and student employees on testing methods, evaluation techniques, and laboratory procedures. Communicate routine technical information to customers and Customer Care staff regarding testing options, sample requirements, procedures, and results. Participate in the evaluation and implementation of new or revised testing methods and recommend improvements to laboratory procedures, equipment, and workflows. Support laboratory quality assurance activities, including procedure documentation, audits, proficiency testing, equipment calibration, and corrective actions. Contribute to educational and professional outreach through workshops, short courses, laboratory demonstrations, and participation in relevant professional organizations and industry activities.   Preferred Qualifications Education or experience in biology, botany, agronomy, horticulture, or a related field. Experience performing laboratory testing, biological evaluations, or other detailed technical work. Experience maintaining accurate records and interpreting technical information.   Why Join Us? The Seed Science Center brings together faculty, staff, and students from across disciplines including agronomy, plant pathology, horticulture, and engineering, creating a collaborative environment recognized worldwide for leadership in seed science and technology. The Seed Lab has served seed companies, farmers, and researchers across the United States and internationally for more than 100 years. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: 08 Original Posting Date: November 5, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 15, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20167 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Postdoctoral-Research-Associate---Acoustic-emission-monitoring-in-analog-models_R20182": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate – Acoustic emission monitoring in analog models",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-04\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Postdoctoral Research Associate – Acoustic emission monitoring in analog models Appointment Type: Post Doc/Trainee Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Earth, Atmosphere, and Climate within the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences at Iowa State University is seeking a Postdoctoral Research Associate to focus on acoustic emission monitoring of multiphase deformation experiments. The successful candidate will develop an acoustic monitoring system for an existing ring shear apparatus to monitor the failure of brittle clasts embedded in a fluid during deformation. These experiments will quantify brittle failure in space and time within a semi-brittle material and connect local deformation mechanisms to large-scale bulk deformation. The results have the potential to inform future treatment of semi-brittle materials in numerical models and other large-scale simulation applications. The successful candidate must be able to work independently while also collaborating effectively across disciplines and institutions. This project is a collaboration between Iowa State University and the Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT). Strong oral and written communication skills are required. This is a full-time research position with an initial one-year appointment and the possibility of renewal for a second year. Required Minimum Qualifications: PhD in geosciences, physics, engineering, or related fields.  Experience with acoustic emission/ultrasonic/seismic monitoring and data processing.   Experience with development of experimental setups. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with analog modelling. Experience in geophysics or structural geology. Department/Program & College Description: The Department of the Earth, Atmosphere, and Climate is staffed by 17 faculty and has strengths in climate and paleoclimate, microscale and mesoscale meteorology, hydrology, solid-earth processes, geochemistry, and geoscience education.  Undergraduate programs in climate science, earth science, geology, and meteorology serve approximately 200 undergraduate majors. About 30 M.S. and Ph.D. students are enrolled in the geology and earth science and meteorology graduate programs. Generous support for the Department is provided by an active group of alumni and friends. The Geology Program runs a multi-use field station in northwest Wyoming with a 60-year tradition of providing immersive education for students from across the country. Departmental research facilities include state-of-the-art laboratories in stable isotope geochemistry, analogue tectonic modeling, and biogeochemistry.  University research facilities include a Linux computing cluster with over 330 compute nodes and over 38,000 CPU cores, over 200 GPUs, 200 TB of memory, 2PB of high-speed data storage, and high-speed networking. The Meteorology program is co-located with the Iowa Environmental Mesonet and its administrator, giving faculty and students direct access to this well-known archive of weather and climate data.  Department Unit/Website: https://earth-atmosphere-climate.iastate.edu/   Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter One peer-reviewed publication authored by the candidate. Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Proposed Start Date: February 1, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: Post Docs Original Posting Date: November 4, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 25, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20182 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Postdoctoral-Research-Associate---Catalysis-and-Electrochemical-Conversion-of-Biomass_R20183": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate – Catalysis and Electrochemical Conversion of Biomass",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-04\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Postdoctoral Research Associate – Catalysis and Electrochemical Conversion of Biomass Appointment Type: Post Doc/Trainee Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Chemical and Biological Engineering at Iowa State University is seeking a Postdoctoral Research Associate to join a multidisciplinary, milestone-driven research program focused on the conversion of lignocellulosic biomass into chemicals and fuels. The successful candidate will join the research group of Professor Tessonnier. The Postdoctoral Research Associate will design, synthesize, and characterize heterogeneous catalysts and electrocatalysts, including metal alloys, non-precious metal catalysts, and mixed metal oxides. The successful candidate will investigate relationships between catalyst composition, structure, activity, selectivity, and stability. Responsibilities include developing and implementing GC and GC-MS analytical methods (FID, TCD, and MS detectors) to identify and quantify reaction products, including lignin-derived phenolic compounds in aqueous mixtures and permanent gases. The candidate will evaluate catalysts in batch, flow, and electrochemical reactor systems. The postdoctoral researcher will work closely with graduate students, postdoctoral researchers, faculty collaborators, and a national laboratory partner. Additional responsibilities include maintaining shared instrumentation; training and mentoring graduate and undergraduate researchers; preparing technical reports and presentations; contributing to project milestones and deliverables; and publishing research findings in peer-reviewed journals. Required Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in Chemical Engineering, Chemistry, Materials Science and Engineering, or a closely related field, completed before the start date. Demonstrated hands-on experience in the synthesis of inorganic or hybrid materials, including metal and metal-alloy nanoparticles, metal oxide and mixed-oxide catalysts, and supported catalysts, with the ability to control composition, structure, and surface properties. Experience with materials characterization techniques and advanced data analysis, including X-ray diffraction (XRD), X-ray photoelectron spectroscopy (XPS), electron microscopy, physisorption and chemisorption methods, and vibrational spectroscopy. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with gas chromatography (GC) and GC-MS analysis of organic compounds, including method development, calibration, and quantification. Experience analyzing lignin-derived or other phenolic compounds, or organic compounds in aqueous samples, is preferred. Experience in heterogeneous catalysis or electrocatalysis, including catalyst evaluation in batch or flow reactors and electrochemical techniques such as voltammetry, impedance spectroscopy, and bulk electrolysis. Experience operating, maintaining, and troubleshooting analytical instruments, with an interest in data-driven or automated experimentation. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively in written reports, oral presentations, manuscripts, and interdisciplinary team discussions; mentor students; maintain accurate laboratory records; and meet project milestones. Department/Program & College Description: The Department of Chemical and Biological Engineering at Iowa State University is a nationally recognized program with strengths in catalysis, renewable energy, biorenewables, advanced materials, biomedical engineering, and computational modeling. The department fosters a collaborative and interdisciplinary research environment supported by state-of-the-art facilities and strong partnerships with industry, government laboratories, and academic institutions. Department Unit/Website: Department of Chemical and Biological Engineering – College of Engineering, Iowa State University Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Proposed Start Date: December 16, 2026 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: Post Docs Original Posting Date: November 4, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 11, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20183 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Outreach-and-Partnerships-Coordinator_R20141": {
      "title": "Outreach and Partnerships Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-04\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Outreach and Partnerships Coordinator Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 2 years of related experience Special Required Qualifications Valid U.S. Driver's License Job Description: The Institute for Design Research and Outreach (IDRO) in the College of Design is seeking an Outreach and Partnerships Coordinator (Program Specialist II) to oversee the day-to-day operations of the college’s community and partner engagement programs.   Success in this role requires strong project management and coordination skills, the ability to balance multiple projects and competing priorities, and a proactive, organized approach to completing tasks. The position also requires applying technical skills to community and local government issues, including analyzing trends, interpreting survey data, evaluating project goals, and using findings to inform recommendations and measure outcomes.   Examples of Duties: Coordinate day-to-day community engagement programs, including developing timelines, organizing events, tracking deliverables, and ensuring activities align with program goals. Collaborate with faculty, staff, students, and external partners to coordinate program activities, support project implementation, and advance community engagement initiatives. Provide technical assistance through site visits, workshops, reports, presentations, database development, and outreach materials to support project activities and partner needs. Identify and recruit community partners, including local governments, elected officials, nonprofit organizations, and private-sector representatives, while maintaining effective working relationships. Assist with grant applications, funding opportunities, program development, and the expansion of community partnerships and outreach initiatives. Monitor project progress, analyze data and survey results, evaluate program outcomes, and document impact to inform reporting and continuous improvement. Coordinate follow-up activities with partners, faculty, and students to support project implementation, strengthen relationships, and achieve program objectives. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in planning, design, community development, public administration, or a related field. Experience in community engagement, partnership development, and stakeholder relationship management. Strong facilitation and presentation skills, including the ability to support and coordinate meetings, workshops, and group discussions. Excellent written communication skills, including the ability to prepare professional correspondence to elected officials, organize complex information, and present ideas clearly and effectively. Familiarity with Iowa local governments, elected officials, nonprofit organizations, and community-based partnerships. The Institute for Design Research and Outreach (IDRO) encompasses the research, extension, and outreach missions of the College of Design. Broadly defined, IDRO’s overall mission is to stimulate and support research, extension, and outreach efforts in areas of strength and relevance to the design disciplines.   The institute promotes interdisciplinary design research, facilitates communication with design professionals and the public, and responds to the needs of the people of Iowa in areas associated with the design disciplines. Projects often are conducted collaboratively, and individual faculty may be involved in several different programs at the same time. Through IDRO, faculty and students work together with citizen groups, businesses, communities, nonprofit organizations and government agencies in addressing problems to improve the quality of our built environment and our lives.   Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. The following application materials are required: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS807 Original Posting Date: November 4, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 11, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20141 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Postdoctoral-Research-Associate---Plant-Breeding--Genomics--and-Phenomics_R20109": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate - Plant Breeding, Genomics, and Phenomics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-04\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Postdoctoral Research Associate - Plant Breeding, Genomics, and Phenomics Appointment Type: Post Doc/Trainee Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Postdoctoral Research Associate will contribute to multidisciplinary research and crop improvement programs focused on breeding, genomics, and phenomics. This position offers advanced training and professional development opportunities to prepare the successful candidate for an independent research career in academia, government, or industry. The successful candidate will conduct field, greenhouse, laboratory, and computational research supporting crop breeding and cultivar development efforts. Responsibilities include designing and implementing experiments; collecting and analyzing data related to plant genetics, genomics, phenomics, physiology, pathology, and entomology; supporting breeding activities from planting through harvest and post-harvest seed processing; and applying statistical and quantitative methods to research data. Additional responsibilities include publishing research findings in peer-reviewed journals, contributing to grant proposals and technical reports, mentoring graduate and undergraduate students, and participating in collaborative interdisciplinary research projects. The position provides opportunities to gain experience in breeding, genomics, and phenomics while working closely with Dr. Arti Singh and collaborating with researchers across multiple disciplines. Required Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in Agronomy, Breeding, genomics, phenomics or related fields. Preferred Qualifications: Experience publishing scientific manuscripts in peer-reviewed journals relevant to plant breeding, genetics, genomics, phenomics, or related disciplines. Experience conducting field and laboratory experiments in a crop breeding program. Experience working in a mung bean breeding program. FAA Remote Pilot Certificate (Part 107). Department/Program & College Description: The College of Agriculture and Life Sciences is one of the world’s leading institutions of agriculture, with more than 160 years of leadership in science, education and extension. The college educates future leaders, conducts mission-oriented research and shares new knowledge for the betterment of Iowa and the world. The college is one of eight colleges at Iowa State University, which is one of the most influential land grant universities in the nation. Department Unit/Website: Agronomy | College of Agriculture and Life Sciences Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Proposed Start Date: December 15, 2026 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: Post Docs Original Posting Date: November 4, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 12, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20109 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Research-Scientist-I---Poultry_R20169": {
      "title": "Research Scientist I - Poultry",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-03\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Research Scientist I - Poultry Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree Job Description: The Department of Animal Science at Iowa State University is seeking an early-career Research Scientist I to coordinate and support animal science research activities. This position will oversee animal research studies, coordinate laboratory operations, and ensure research activities are conducted in accordance with approved protocols, established procedures, and regulatory requirements. The successful candidate will also provide technical guidance and training to students and research personnel while supporting the quality, accuracy, and integrity of research outcomes. What You'll Do Coordinate and oversee animal research studies, including scheduling and managing the use of animals, facilities, equipment, and other research resources. Ensure research activities follow approved experimental protocols, animal welfare standards, standard operating procedures, biosafety requirements, and applicable regulatory guidelines. Coordinate data collection and the collection, processing, handling, and storage of biological samples to maintain research quality and integrity. Identify and resolve operational, technical, or protocol-related issues that may affect animal welfare, research outcomes, or study timelines. Prepare study reports and maintain required research, regulatory, and compliance documentation in accordance with institutional and sponsor requirements. Perform and oversee chemical analyses of research samples in the nutrition laboratory, ensuring adherence to established methodologies, laboratory procedures, and quality control standards. Coordinate laboratory workflows, including scheduling and prioritizing equipment use, managing sample analysis activities, and supporting the implementation of research methodologies. Train and provide technical guidance to undergraduate and graduate students, postdoctoral scholars, hourly employees, and research staff on laboratory procedures, equipment operation, research protocols, and safety practices. Monitor research activities and personnel to ensure compliance with applicable regulations and promote a safe, organized, and compliant research environment. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Animal Science, Poultry Science, or a related field . Experience handling and working with poultry in a research or production setting. Experience collecting, processing, and managing biological samples. Experience working in a traditional laboratory setting, performing routine laboratory procedures and chemical or biological analyses. Experience following laboratory and animal research safety procedures, including compliance with established protocols, standard operating procedures, and applicable regulatory requirements. Experience coordinating research activities, including developing schedules, prioritizing tasks, and managing resources to ensure studies and laboratory work are completed within established timelines. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. This is a term position that may have opportunity for renewal. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular with Term Appointment (Fixed Term) Proposed End Date or Length of Term: January 3, 2028 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS807 Original Posting Date: November 3, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 10, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20169 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Social-Media-Specialist-I_R20173": {
      "title": "Social Media Specialist I",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-03\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Social Media Specialist I Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree Job Description: The Ivy College of Business is hiring a Social Media Specialist I to create day-to-day content and develop comprehensive strategies to support college objectives on social media. Under the supervision of the college’s Graphic Designer, this individual will work directly with the college's marketing and communications team, which includes the Director of Marketing and Communications, Graphic Designer, Event Planner, Web Manager, as well as marketing and photography interns.    The successful candidate will be skilled with social media content management platforms and analytics, stay organized, and deliver timely, creative content (text, image, and video) based on audience insight. The successful candidate will also foster positive and collaborative relationships with internal and external constituents.    Example of Duties: Develops and manages social media strategies and campaigns. Creates and publishes daily content, including text, graphics, photos, and short-form videos. Builds brand awareness, increases engagement, and grows social media audiences. Promotes the Ivy College of Business, its people, events, and accomplishments. Monitors platform trends, best practices, and digital accessibility standards. Plans and manages paid social media campaigns within established budgets. Monitors campaign performance, engagement, and analytics. Recommends content and strategy improvements based on results. Prepares monthly and annual performance reports and shares insights with leadership. Monitors social media activity and responds to comments, questions, and feedback. Identifies opportunities to increase engagement with key audiences and stakeholders. Establishes, manages, and monitors college-affiliated social media accounts. Provides guidance and expertise on social media strategies, platform requirements, and best practices. Conducts social listening and competitor research to identify trends and opportunities.   Preferred Qualifications: Experience managing and maintaining social media accounts across multiple platforms. Experience developing, implementing, and managing paid social media advertising campaigns. Ability to interpret social media metrics and analytics, prepare performance reports, and use data to inform and guide content and marketing strategies. Experience creating engaging digital content, including photography, videography, and short-form video. Strong written and verbal communication skills, including experience with professional correspondence with faculty and staff, caption writing, and developing audience-focused social media content.   Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position.   Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS806 Original Posting Date: November 3, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 10, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20173 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Administrative-Assistant-II_R20165": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant II",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-03\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Administrative Assistant II Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent and 3 years of related experience Job Description: The Graduate College at Iowa State University is seeking an organized and service-oriented Administrative Assistant II to support the Ronald E. McNair Postbaccalaureate Achievement Program. This position plays an important role in the day-to-day administration of the program, providing support to students, prospective participants, alumni, faculty, and university partners. Responsibilities include coordinating program activities and events, supporting student recruitment and engagement, managing financial and travel transactions, maintaining program records, and assisting with data collection and reporting. The successful candidate will be an effective communicator who enjoys working with students, managing multiple priorities, and contributing to a program focused on supporting students in their pursuit of graduate education.   What You'll Do Serve as a primary administrative contact for the McNair Program, providing information and support to students, prospective participants, alumni, faculty, and university partners. Coordinate program events and activities, including planning, scheduling, communications, logistics, and on-site support. Support student recruitment and the application process by preparing recruitment materials, monitoring applications, and communicating with prospective participants. Maintain accurate and confidential participant and alumni records, databases, and communication lists. Develop and distribute program newsletters, announcements, and social media content. Support student success and engagement by monitoring academic progress, communicating graduate school application requirements to graduating students, and participating in program activities and weekly classes. Process financial transactions and provide business operations support, including purchasing, vouchers, reimbursements, catering, conference registrations, and other program expenditures. Coordinate travel arrangements for staff and students, including transportation, lodging, authorizations, and reimbursements. Travel with students to regional or national conferences as needed to provide logistical and program support. Collect, maintain, and analyze program data; assist with participant outcome tracking, report preparation, program assessment, and documentation required for institutional reporting and external funding agencies.   Preferred Qualifications Experience providing administrative support and customer service to multiple stakeholders in an office environment. Experience coordinating meetings, events, travel, or complex schedules involving multiple participants. Demonstrated experience providing confidential administrative support. Experience managing records, tracking deadlines, and coordinating multiple administrative processes simultaneously. Expertise with Microsoft Office Suite, particularly Excel spreadsheets, Outlook email and calendars, Word documents, Power Point presentations, and Teams.   This role offers a rare opportunity to build lasting, meaningful relationships with students across every college at Iowa State. The McNair Program is a close-knit community where staff and Scholars work closely and stay connected long after graduation. You will support students as they apply to a wide range of graduate programs and celebrate with them as they enter top institutions across the country. Many alumni return to share updates about their graduate school journeys and early careers, reflecting the strong sense of support and impact the program creates. For someone who values long-term student development and the chance to make a tangible difference in individual academic trajectories, this position is uniquely rewarding.   The successful candidate will join a productive team of professionals who are fully engaged with the students we serve.   Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position.   This is a term position that may have opportunity for renewal. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular with Term Appointment (Fixed Term) Proposed End Date or Length of Term: September 30, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS806 Original Posting Date: November 3, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 11, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20165 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
