    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Postdoc-Research-Associate---Veterinary-Pathology_R20067": {
      "title": "Postdoc Research Associate - Veterinary Pathology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-03\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Postdoc Research Associate - Veterinary Pathology Appointment Type: Post Doc/Trainee Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Veterinary Pathology at Iowa State University is seeking a highly motivated Postdoctoral Research Associate to support interdisciplinary research focused on prion biology, transmissible spongiform encephalopathies, and disease-associated protein misfolding. The successful candidate will contribute to the development, optimization, and evaluation of innovative methods for the isolation, recovery, and detection of disease-associated proteins in complex biological samples. This position involves designing and conducting laboratory experiments, developing antibody-based and biochemical assays, evaluating protein capture and detection approaches, and analyzing quantitative research data. The researcher will work with tissues, biological fluids, and other potentially infectious materials while adhering to established biosafety and containment protocols. Additional responsibilities include maintaining accurate research records, preparing protocols and reports, contributing to scientific publications and presentations, and collaborating on the evaluation of emerging diagnostic and detection technologies. The position offers the opportunity to work within a multidisciplinary research environment alongside scientists in veterinary medicine, biomedical sciences, and engineering, while developing independent research skills and contributing to impactful research conducted at both Iowa State University and the National Animal Disease Center. Required Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in Biochemistry, Molecular Biology, Microbiology, Biomedical Sciences, or a closely related field, completed by the anticipated start date. Research experience in protein biochemistry, immunological assays, or related molecular and cellular laboratory methods. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with prion biology, transmissible spongiform encephalopathies, or other protein misfolding disorders. Experience developing, optimizing, or validating immunoassays and other protein detection methods. Experience with protein purification, affinity capture, magnetic bead methods, or related biochemical techniques. Experience working with infectious materials under established biosafety procedures. Record of peer-reviewed publications and effective interdisciplinary collaboration. Department/Program & College Description: Veterinary pathology provides a critical link between the basic and clinical sciences. Our faculty fill essential roles in teaching veterinary and graduate students, diagnosis of animal diseases, and scientific research. Department Unit/Website: Veterinary Pathology - Veterinary Pathology Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a federal security background check and authorization to access a federal research facility. The selected candidate must maintain the required access authorization and complete all required biosafety, prion-handling, and security training. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Proposed Start Date: December 1, 2026 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: Post Docs Original Posting Date: October 21, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 12, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20067 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Ames-National-Laboratory-Scientist-I_R20179": {
      "title": "Ames National Laboratory Scientist I",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-02\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Ames National Laboratory Scientist I Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: PhD or equivalent combination of education and experience Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The successful candidate will serve as the computational lead within an integrated discovery platform. You will architect the digital frameworks, spanning graph neural networks, molecular representations, thermodynamic equilibrium modeling, and multi-agent LLM systems, that interpret complex analytical data, predict extractant-metal selectivity, and drive AI-guided open-loop and closed-loop experimental studies through direct interaction with autonomous robotic laboratories for critical materials separation. Skills and abilities necessary for this position include a strong fundamental grasp of coordination chemistry, solution thermodynamics, and aqueous electrolyte equilibria. The candidate must possess advanced programming proficiency in Python, cheminformatics libraries (specifically RDKit), and scientific machine learning frameworks (such as PyTorch Geometric). Furthermore, the role requires hands-on experience developing LLM-based agentic workflows, navigating Linux-based HPC cluster environments, interfacing with autonomous robotic labs for both open-loop and closed-loop studies, and working collaboratively in multi-institutional teams to translate physical sciences into computational workflows. This position is a 1-year term appointment. Preferred Qualifications: Experience running aqueous equilibrium engines, specifically PHREEQC or phreeqpy, with familiarity in non-ideal electrolyte models (Pitzer equations, Bromley, or e-NRTL). Prior exposure to wet-chemical laboratory environments handling mineral acids, metal salt solutions, and organic solvent diluents. Experience interfacing with autonomous robotic labs or automated liquid handlers for AI-guided open-loop and closed-loop experimental studies. Familiarity with interpreting datasets from analytical instrumentation (ICP-MS, ICP-OES, UV-Vis spectrophotometry, ATR-FTIR). Basic familiarity with OpenCV, YOLOv8, or simple image-segmentation tools. Exposure to real-world hydrometallurgical feedstocks (acid rock drainage, zinc roaster residues, bauxite red mud). Experience in drafting research proposals or participating in grant writing. Department/Program & College Description: Would you like to continue your scientific career at a U.S. National Laboratory that conducts world-renowned research? Would you enjoy working on a beautiful university campus in a mid-sized city location that regularly ranks as one of the U.S. Best Places to Live? If you answered yes to any of these questions, you should consider a career with Ames National Laboratory! Ames National Laboratory is a U.S. Department of Energy federally contracted National Laboratory located in Ames, Iowa, on the campus of Iowa State University. We are dedicated to translating foundational science through applied research to create technological innovations. We create materials, inspire minds to solve problems, and address some of the most challenging issues facing our world today. We promote and believe in a culture of civility and shared ownership in support of the Laboratory's collective success. Employees with appointment at Ames National Laboratory are subject to particular restrictions related to participation in Foreign Government Sponsored or Affiliated Activities, as defined and detailed in United States Department of Energy Order 486.1A. You will be asked to disclose any such participation during the recruitment phase for review by Ames National Laboratory.   Employment is contingent upon satisfying applicable requirements of Ames National Laboratory’s federal sponsor, the United States Department of Energy, and ISU requirements. These may include background checks and eligibility determinations related to access of facilities, information, or projects. This position requires the incumbent to obtain and maintain government access authorization for the duration of the appointment.  Department Unit/Website (if applicable): www.ameslab.gov Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter List of Professional References Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular with Term Appointment (Fixed Term) Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS810 Original Posting Date: November 2, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 15, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20179 Employees with appointment at Ames National Laboratory are subject to particular restrictions related to participation in Foreign Government Sponsored or Affiliated Activities, as defined and detailed in United States Department of Energy Order 486.1A. You will be asked to disclose any such participation during the recruitment phase for review by Ames National Laboratory.   Employment is contingent upon satisfying applicable requirements of Ames National Laboratory’s federal sponsor, the United States Department of Energy, and ISU requirements. These may include background checks and eligibility determinations related to access of facilities, information, or projects. This position requires the incumbent to obtain and maintain government access authorization for the duration of the appointment.  Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Storekeeper-II_R20178": {
      "title": "Storekeeper II",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-02\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Storekeeper II Job Group: Merit Required Minimum Qualifications: • One year of work experience in storekeeping, accounting, business administration or job related work, or Any combination of such experience and post high school education that totals one year. • Possession of appropriate drivers license as required. Job Description: Under general supervision, operates a small storeroom, or is in charge of one or more functions of a large storeroom operation. Provides functional supervision to storeroom personnel as required.   Characteristic Duties and Responsibilities   • Receives, stores and issues equipment, materials, supplies, foodstuffs, etc., according to established methods. • Stores special stock items requiring treatment which may deviate from established storekeeping methods in assigning space and identification. • Issues items which require knowledge of specific areas of supply operation and good knowledge of stock characterized by susceptibility to spontaneous combustion, toxicity, fragility, rapid deterioration, contamination, ease of physical damage. • Performs tasks independently in connection with checking and tallying special or technical items of supply. • Verifies stock against shipping authorizations for agreement as to quantities, descriptions, sizes, conditions and conformance to purchase orders. • Searches manufacturers’ catalogs, technical bulletins, nomenclature lists, etc. to identify special items; seeks advice of operating personnel to insure compliance with purchase orders for unusual orders. • Applies storekeeping procedures and methods in arranging space, conducting inventory, estimating needs, and maintaining and preparing records and reports as directed. • Makes minor adjustments or repairs to items carried in stock. • Drives, loads, and unloads a delivery truck periodically. • Assist faculty and staff in setting up and operating equipment for lectures, regular laboratory work, or special demonstrations.   Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities   • Knowledge of storeroom methods and procedures. • Knowledge of the characteristics, uses and proper handling/storage techniques of items supplied. • Knowledge of proper lifting and bending techniques. • Ability to interpret and follow oral and written instructions. • Ability to prepare and maintain stock records, reports, and inventories. • Ability to perform basic arithmetic functions involving addition, subtraction, multiplication, and division. • Ability to communicate effectively with coworkers and constituents. • Ability to work independently. • Ability to provide functional supervision. • Ability to work with computerized inventory control system. Keep ISU Dining moving from the warehouse to the table! As a Storekeeper II , you’ll play a key role in receiving, storing, inventorying, and delivering food, supplies, equipment, and other materials across ISU Dining locations. You’ll operate delivery vehicles and pallet jacks, load and unload materials, verify deliveries, complete transfer documentation, distribute products, and coordinate with delivery-site staff to ensure items are safely and accurately placed. You’ll also move furniture and equipment between Dining locations and serve as a resource for delivery logistics.    You’ll maintain inventory across coolers, freezers, and dry storage areas, ensuring proper stock rotation, receiving temperatures, product quality, and accurate records. You’ll fulfill orders and requisitions, conduct inventory counts, use tablet and inventory systems, complete Quality Assurance logs, and maintain clean, safe, and organized storage areas. The role also includes supporting and training student staff, assisting with equipment maintenance, coordinating vendor returns, and obtaining and maintaining ServSafe and forklift certifications. Some items may weigh up to 100 pounds.    Preferred Qualifications Experience in food service, warehouse, storeroom, receiving, or distribution operations.  Experience receiving, storing, rotating, and issuing food, supplies, or inventory.  Experience operating forklifts, pallet jacks, or other material-handling equipment.  Experience using computerized inventory, purchasing, or warehouse management systems.  Knowledge of food safety, sanitation, quality assurance, temperature monitoring, and FIFO inventory practices.    About the Department ISU Dining’s Foodstores Logistics team keeps dining operations running smoothly by receiving, storing, managing, and distributing the food, supplies, and equipment needed across campus dining locations. The team plays an essential behind-the-scenes role in ensuring products are available, properly handled, and delivered safely and efficiently to support the Cyclone dining experience.  Department Website: https://dining.iastate.edu/ Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: 06 Original Posting Date: November 2, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 12, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20178 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Term-Faculty-for-Management-and-Entrepreneurship_R20172": {
      "title": "Term Faculty for Management and Entrepreneurship",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-02\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Term Faculty for Management and Entrepreneurship Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Management and Entrepreneurship in the Ivy College of Business at Iowa State University is seeking two faculty members to teach Management and/or Entrepreneurship courses beginning January 2027 with an initial term of one year. The position will be at the rank of Lecturer or Assistant Teaching Professor and come with the possibility of both renewal and increased FTE. The teaching assignments will be between one and four sections and may include a variety of classes taught face-to-face and online. ISU is a residential campus so, even if some teaching is online, Iowa residency and regular time on campus throughout the semester is required. The possible courses include: MGMT 3710 – Organizational Behavior MGMT 3720 – Ethical and Responsible Management MGMT 3810 – Managing Family Businesses MGMT 4710 – Introduction to Human Resource Management MGMT 4730 – Evidence-Based Decision Making in Human Resource Management MGMT 4780 – Strategic Management ENTSP 3100 – Entrepreneurship and Innovation ENTSP 3130 – Feasibility Analysis for New Ventures ENTSP 3200 – Corporate Entrepreneurship ENTSP 4100 – Social Entrepreneurship The Department of Management and Entrepreneurship is a vibrant, supportive, and productive group of 40 faculty members (19 tenure-track and 21 term) currently chaired by Chad Murphy. With research interests spanning the areas of HR, OB, Strategy, Entrepreneurship, and Healthcare Management, they have published research in a wide variety of top journals, including the Academy of Management Journal , Academy of Management Review , Journal of Applied Psychology, Personnel Psychology, Organizational Behavior and Human Decision Processes, Journal of Management , Organization Science , Strategic Management Journal , and Journal of Business Venturing . The department offers undergraduate degrees in Human Resource Management, Management, Entrepreneurship, Healthcare Management, and International Business. The department also offers a Masters in Entrepreneurship and hosts PhD programs in Management as well as Entrepreneurship. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Required Minimum Qualifications: Masters degree in a business discipline or field related to the possible courses listed above Previous teaching experience in a corporate or academic setting Recent or continuing professional engagement as required for AACSB accreditation   Preferred Qualifications: Experience with ISU’s learning management system, Canvas Experience teaching online courses ABD or Ph.D. in a business discipline or field related to the possible courses listed above   Department/Program & College Description: The Ivy College of Business at Iowa State University, established in 1984, furthers Iowa State University’s land-grant ideals by training students to be knowledgeable and ethical communicators, leaders, collaborators, and problem solvers through impactful research, innovative teaching, and community engagement. With the largest undergraduate business program in the state of Iowa and nationally ranked graduate programs, the Ivy College of Business is home to over 5000 students with a strong growth trajectory. We pride ourselves on our high ethical standards and our drive to promote an environment where all individuals may succeed academically, professionally, and personally. Each member of our community is committed to the college’s mission to link theory with practice for tomorrow’s business leaders. The college offers undergraduate, graduate, and Ph.D. programs and is accredited by the Association to Advance Collegiate Schools of Business (AACSB International). Less than five percent of business schools worldwide receive this accreditation. Department Unit/Website: https://www.ivybusiness.iastate.edu/management/ Proposed Start Date: January 1, 2027 Proposed End Date or Length of Term: December 31, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of Application/Cover Letter 3) Contact Information for Three References For full guaranteed consideration, please apply on or before  November 15, 2026 . For questions about the position, please contact the department chair Chad Murphy (chmurphy@iastate.edu). If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: November 2, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20172 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Postdoc-Research-Associate---Bee-Ecology-and-Conservation-in-Farmland_R20145": {
      "title": "Postdoc Research Associate - Bee Ecology and Conservation in Farmland",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-02\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Postdoc Research Associate - Bee Ecology and Conservation in Farmland Appointment Type: Post Doc/Trainee Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Ecology, Evolution, and Organismal Biology at Iowa State University invites applications for a Postdoctoral Scholar to join a USDA-NIFA-funded research project investigating how reconstructed native habitat within agricultural landscapes affects managed and wild bees. This is a full-time Postdoctoral Scholar position located at Iowa State University in Ames, Iowa. The initial appointment is for one year, with the possibility of renewal. Funding may be available for up to three years, contingent upon satisfactory performance and continued project funding. The position includes Iowa State University benefits. The anticipated start date is between January 2027 and May 2027. The successful candidate will work with Professors Amy Toth (direct supervisor), Lisa Schulte Moore, and Matthew O'Neal, along with an interdisciplinary team at Iowa State University on the project, \"Evaluating Benefits of Reconstructed Habitat in Farmland Across Bee Species and Landscapes.\" The overarching goal of the project is to determine when and where prairie strips and other reconstructed habitats provide net benefits to bee communities in intensively farmed landscapes. Research activities integrate field ecology, pollinator health, landscape ecology, pesticide exposure, floral resource assessment, and the management of honey bee and bumble bee colonies. This multi-year project involves extensive fieldwork at Iowa farms utilizing prairie strips within corn-soybean production systems. The Postdoctoral Scholar will be expected to: Travel to field sites and collect ecological and bee health data on wild bees, managed bumble bees, and honey bees. Assist with the management and monitoring of honey bee and bumble bee colonies used in the study. Analyze data; prepare manuscripts for peer-reviewed publication; and present research findings at scientific conferences. Collaborate with project investigators, research staff, graduate and undergraduate students, farmer cooperators, and other project partners. Assist with plant surveys, floral resource measurements, including the use of drone imagery, and pollen sampling and analysis. Contribute to interdisciplinary research efforts focused on pollinator conservation in agricultural landscapes. This position provides substantial opportunities for intellectual leadership. The successful candidate will be encouraged to contribute to research planning, mentor students and junior researchers, and develop professional skills relevant to future careers in ecology, entomology, conservation science, and related disciplines. Required Minimum Qualifications: PhD in biology, entomology, ecology, or a closely related field by the appointment start date.   Prior research experience relevant to the goals and activities of this project. Possession of a valid driver's license and meeting the University's Fleet Safety Program requirements. Preferred Qualifications: Experience conducting ecological or entomological field research, especially related to Hymenoptera.   Experience with plant and/or bee identification.   Experience with beekeeping or honey bee research.   Department/Program & College Description: The Department of Ecology, Evolution, and Organismal Biology (EEOB) at Iowa State University is dedicated to advancing understanding of the natural world through research, teaching, and outreach. EEOB explores the interactions among organisms and their environments, the diversity of life, evolutionary processes, and the structure and function of living organisms. Faculty, staff, and students conduct innovative research addressing critical challenges in ecology, conservation, biodiversity, evolutionary biology, and environmental sustainability while preparing the next generation of scientists and leaders. Department Unit/Website: Department of Ecology, Evolution, and Organismal Biology (EEOB) Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Proposed Start Date: January 15, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: Post Docs Original Posting Date: October 26, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 15, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20145 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Postdoctoral-Research-Associate---Theoretical-Nuclear-Physics-and-Quantum-Computing_R20105": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate - Theoretical Nuclear Physics and Quantum Computing",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-02\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Postdoctoral Research Associate - Theoretical Nuclear Physics and Quantum Computing Appointment Type: Post Doc/Trainee Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Postdoctoral Research Associate will conduct theoretical nuclear physics research with an emphasis on ab initio Hamiltonian methods and their applications to quantum computing. The successful candidate will develop and apply advanced computational approaches in light-front quantized field theory or microscopic nuclear structure theory to investigate fundamental properties of atomic nuclei and strongly interacting quantum systems. This position is expected to be funded for one year, with the possibility of renewal contingent upon the availability of funding. Responsibilities include performing independent and collaborative research, developing innovative theoretical and computational techniques, publishing results in peer-reviewed journals, presenting findings at scientific conferences, and contributing to research proposals and interdisciplinary collaborations. The position offers opportunities to work at the intersection of nuclear physics, quantum information science, and high-performance computing. Required Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in Theoretical Nuclear Physics, Particle Physics, or a closely related field by the position start date. Experience in ab initio nuclear theory or Hamiltonian light-front field theory. Demonstrated record of scholarly achievement, including publications in peer-reviewed scientific journals. Preferred Qualifications: Experience using high-performance computing (HPC). Experience with quantum computing. Department/Program & College Description: The Department of Physics and Astronomy at Iowa State University is dedicated to advancing the understanding of the universe through excellence in research, education, and innovation. The department maintains nationally recognized theoretical and experimental research programs in astrophysics, condensed matter physics, high-energy physics, and nuclear physics, providing a collaborative and intellectually stimulating environment for discovery. Faculty, postdoctoral researchers, and students work together to address fundamental scientific questions using advanced computational, experimental, and analytical approaches. Department Unit/Website: Department of Physics and Astronomy Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Proposed Start Date: December 2, 2026 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: Post Docs Original Posting Date: October 19, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 9, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20105 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
