    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Postdoctoral-Research-Associate---Poultry-Disease-Diagnostics-and-Epidemiology_R20166": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate - Poultry Disease Diagnostics and Epidemiology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-02\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Postdoctoral Research Associate - Poultry Disease Diagnostics and Epidemiology Appointment Type: Post Doc/Trainee Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Postdoctoral Research Associate will lead and support research focused on advancing poultry disease diagnostics, molecular epidemiology, and pathogen surveillance. This position is responsible for designing and conducting research projects utilizing real-time PCR, sequence typing, and next-generation sequencing technologies to evaluate, develop, and improve diagnostic assays for poultry diseases. The individual will investigate disease transmission patterns, differentiate primary and secondary pathogens, and contribute to the understanding of disease emergence and spread within poultry populations. The position will also provide technical leadership within the laboratory, including training and supervising students and staff, maintaining laboratory operations, and ensuring the quality and integrity of research activities. The successful candidate will collaborate with multidisciplinary research teams, analyze and interpret complex data, publish findings in peer-reviewed journals, assist with grant development, and present research outcomes at regional, national, and international scientific meetings. This position offers an opportunity to contribute to innovative research that supports poultry health, disease prevention, and the advancement of diagnostic technologies for the poultry industry. Required Minimum Qualifications: Completed Ph.D. in Poultry Medicine or a closely related field with a focus on poultry infectious diseases by the start date of employment. Preferred Qualifications: Experience developing and validating molecular diagnostic assays. Clinical diagnostic experience in poultry or veterinary diagnostic laboratories. Expertise in virology, microbiology, phylogenetics, sequence typing, and molecular epidemiology. Experience with next-generation sequencing and bioinformatics analyses. Strong publication record demonstrated through peer-reviewed scientific publications and presentations. Department/Program & College Description: At VDPAM, we lead the future of food animal and population medicine. As a global center of excellence, we are recognized for our expertise, valued for our collaborative partnerships, and trusted to deliver innovative, science-driven solutions to the most pressing challenges in animal health and food production. We advance our vision by empowering current and future veterinarians, scientists, and industry stakeholders through exceptional education, groundbreaking research, and world-class clinical and diagnostic services. Every day, we work to elevate animal health, enhance productivity and welfare, strengthen food safety, and support a sustainable global food system. Department Unit/Website: Veterinary Diagnostic and Production Animal Medicine - Veterinary Diagnostic and Production Animal Medicine Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Proposed Start Date: December 1, 2026 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: Post Docs Original Posting Date: November 2, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 9, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20166 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Resident---Equine-Internal-Medicine_R20162": {
      "title": "Resident – Equine Internal Medicine",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-02\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Resident – Equine Internal Medicine Appointment Type: Post Doc/Trainee Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Veterinary Clinical Sciences, in conjunction with the Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center, offers a three-year residency program in Equine Internal Medicine designed to prepare residents for board certification through the American College of Veterinary Internal Medicine (ACVIM). The program consists of 156 weeks of supervised clinical training and educational experiences under the guidance of ACVIM Large Animal Internal Medicine diplomates. Residents will participate in advanced equine patient care, clinical teaching, and scholarly activities while developing the knowledge and skills necessary for specialty certification. Required Minimum Qualifications: Doctor of Veterinary Medicine (DVM) degree and eligible for veterinary licensure. Completion of a one-year veterinary internship by the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated interest in Large Animal Internal Medicine. Experience teaching or mentoring veterinary students. Department/Program & College Description: The Department of Veterinary Clinical Sciences within Iowa State University's College of Veterinary Medicine is dedicated to excellence in veterinary education, clinical service, and research. Faculty, residents, and staff work collaboratively to advance animal health through specialty clinical care, innovative research, and the training of future veterinary professionals. Department Unit/Website: Veterinary Clinical Sciences - Veterinary Clinical Sciences Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Proposed Start Date: July 15, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: Post Docs Original Posting Date: November 2, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 9, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20162 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
