    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Animal-Caretaker-I_R20160": {
      "title": "Animal Caretaker I",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-30\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Animal Caretaker I Job Group: Merit Required Minimum Qualifications: • Ability to read, write, and follow instructions. • Possession of a valid state or commercial driver's license, as required. Job Description: Job Profile Description: The College of Veterinary Medicine at Iowa State University is seeking a Large Animal Caretaker to support the daily operations of our large animal facilities. This position is key to ensuring our facilities remain clean, safe, and fully supportive of teaching, research, and clinical activities. You will work with a variety of large animals, including horses, cattle, swine, and small ruminants such as sheep and goats .   What You’ll Do: Provide care for large animals , including feeding, watering, grooming, and monitoring health through daily observation. Assist with veterinary procedures and animal restraint during clinical treatments and educational demonstrations. Maintain animal facilities , ensuring enclosures, equipment, and environments are clean and sanitary while following biosecurity protocols. Transport animals and supplies within the facility and assist with facility upkeep and minor repairs. Monitor and report on animal health status, including any signs of illness, injury, or stress, to supervisors and veterinary staff.   Work Environment & Schedule Full-time position with rotating shifts. You’ll work on-site, caring for animals in various weather conditions and physical environments. Shift: Overnight: 4, 10-hour days (8pm-7am) * On call and rotating weekends   Why Join Us Be part of a team supporting teaching, research, and clinical care in veterinary medicine Gain hands-on experience working with large animals Contribute to a mission focused on animal health, safety, and welfare Training provided for candidates eager to learn   About the College of Veterinary Medicine: The Iowa State University College of Veterinary Medicine is at the forefront of veterinary education, clinical care, and research. As part of our team, you’ll work in a cutting-edge environment where animal health, student education, and scientific advancements are prioritized. Join us in making a meaningful impact on the welfare of animals and the future of veterinary medicine. Preferred Qualifications: Experience handling large animals/livestock. Experience working in a research, educational, or veterinary setting. Experience or familiarity with cleaning and disinfecting animal housing areas and maintaining sanitary environments. Experience maintaining records related to animal care, feeding schedules, health monitoring, or inventory management. Department Unit/Website: https://vetmed.iastate.edu/vmc/large-animal/ Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: 7611a Original Posting Date: October 30, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 13, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20160 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Electrician-II_R19974": {
      "title": "Electrician II",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-30\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Electrician II Job Group: Merit Required Minimum Qualifications: • Requires State of Iowa Class A Journeyman Electrician license with at least four years as an apprentice plus two years of experience as a journeyman electrician; or State of Iowa Class B Journeyman Electrician license with eight years in the electrical trade in maintenance or construction. • Must possess a valid driver’s license and meet University’s Fleet Safety Program. Job Description: Under general supervision, applies knowledge, skills and abilities at the journey level to install and repair electrical systems and equipment (generally less than 600V). Demonstrates Journeyman Electrician qualifications, training, experience and technical knowledge. Responsible for the coordination and accomplishment of maintenance, operations and modifications. Performs the duties peculiar to, and normally required in, the trade of electrician, following recognized procedures and techniques for such work. Utilizes special tools, equipment, and processes (such as insulation testers, thermal imaging cameras and Thermal/Infrared (TIR) Predictive Testing procedures) to collect, perform initial diagnostics, and respond to data through established guidelines for preventive and predictive maintenance to ensure equipment reliability. About the department – Utility Services Utility Services is a 24-hour, 365-day-a-year operation dedicated to meeting the energy needs of the Iowa State University community. The department operates and maintains four energy production facilities, as well as an extensive network of utility distribution systems that serve the entire Iowa State campus. Through a commitment to operational excellence, safety, and sustainability, Utility Services works to provide reliable, economical, and environmentally responsible utility services that support the university's teaching, research, and outreach mission. Its primary goal is to safely deliver dependable utility services while continuously advancing sustainability and efficiency across campus operations. Copy and paste the link below to learn more about our team! https://www.fpm.iastate.edu/utilities/energy_production_facilities.asp About the role: Maintain and repair campus site lighting and low-voltage power distribution systems. Install conduit, cable, switchboards, panels, and circuit breakers. Perform maintenance and installation of variable frequency drives, campus mass warning signals, traffic/pedestrian control signals, utility electric meters, and mechanical flow meters. Utilize utility locating equipment to identify and troubleshoot underground infrastructure. Assist Utility High Voltage staff with cable pulls, switch replacements, and vault maintenance. Read and interpret schematics, drawings, and instruction books. Communicate effectively, professionally, and positively with colleagues and campus community members. You will receive training to use utility locating equipment for the identification and troubleshooting of underground infrastructure Install and maintain motor starters and motor control centers. Perform maintenance on circuit breakers protecting circuits that range from 120V to 15,000V. Other duties as assigned. Characteristic Duties and Responsibilities • Performs all duties listed under Electrician I. • Installs, maintains, troubleshoots, repairs and replaces 600 volts and less electrical distribution systems and related equipment, including but not limited to main panel board control systems, programmable controls, solid state control systems, step up and down transformers, current and potential transformers, protective field devices, line monitoring equipment and VFD’s. • Installs, maintains, troubleshoots and repairs control systems including lighting, programmable controllers, and building heating and cooling system programmable controllers. • Performs preventive maintenance on electrical equipment systems and control systems. • As required, will commission 600 volts and less electrical distribution systems and related equipment, and control systems. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities • Knowledge of the occupational hazards and safety precautions of the trade. • Knowledge of safety precautions mandated by OSHA, NFPA, NEC and the EPA. • Demonstrates all knowledge, skills, and abilities listed under Electrician I. • Knowledge of electrical control systems, including variable frequency drives. • Ability to use and interpret specialty tools and equipment used to troubleshoot electrical equipment and systems. • Ability to plan and perform work involving the installation, modification, troubleshooting and repair of new and existing control systems and related equipment. • Ability to work in all types of environmental conditions or in areas where there is exposure to excessive noise, dirt, and fumes and at elevated heights from ladders, scaffolds, or hydraulic lifts. Preferred Qualifications -Experience working with Variable Frequency Drives (VFDs), including troubleshooting and installation -Experience with commercial/industrial and three-phase electrical systems -Familiarity with Building Automation Systems (e.g., Metasys) -Experience using electrical system testing and diagnostic tools such as insulation testers, thermal imaging, or power analyzers Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: 5070a Original Posting Date: September 23, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 23, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R19974 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Building-Systems-Specialist-II_R20135": {
      "title": "Building Systems Specialist II",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-30\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Building Systems Specialist II Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 2 years of related experience or an equivalent combination of education and experience totaling 6 years Job Description: The Building System Specialist II at Iowa State University is responsible for managing, maintaining, and optimizing building automation systems to ensure efficient, reliable, and sustainable operation of university facilities. This position provides technical expertise in system programming, commissioning, troubleshooting, performance evaluation, and continuous improvement while coordinating daily operations, contractors, and campus customer needs. The role also ensures compliance with applicable safety regulations, supports the development of new university facilities, and advances Facilities Planning and Management’s mission to provide safe, efficient, and effective building systems across campus. About the Department: Facilities Planning & Management (FP&M) is an organization that is dedicated to the maintenance and enhancement of Iowa State University, one of the nation’s leading educational and agricultural institutes. But more importantly, FP&M is dedicated to their employees and enhancing the lives of each team member through opportunities both professionally and personally. FP&M is one of the largest departments on campus and currently employs over 450 full-time employees and students combined. Preferred Qualifications -Knowledge of HVAC systems -Metasys control programming experience -Experience working with NAE/SNE supervisory engines Example of Duties • Investigates and tests building systems. • Writes and tests program modifications, creates templates and procedures, and develops key performance indicators. • Implements measures to improve the efficiency of building systems and meet targeted performance. • Evaluates the performance of building systems. • Documents results of commissioning effort including building automation system architecture, operation sequences, standardizing procedures, operator training, etc. Level Guidelines • Intermediate-level position with solid professional and/or technical skills working under general supervision to achieve goals • Applies broad, working knowledge of the principles of the field to moderately complex, difficult, and varied problems and issues • Exercises judgment within defined procedures and practices to determine appropriate action and resolve problems • Responds to a broad range of inquiries and requests • May provide training and/or direction to lower-level staff • May lead projects of moderate scope and complexity • Provides guidance to students Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS809 Original Posting Date: October 30, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 12, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20135 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Department-of-Interior-Design---Assistant-Professor_R20159": {
      "title": "Department of Interior Design - Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-30\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Department of Interior Design - Assistant Professor Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Interior Design in the College of Design at Iowa State University (ISU) invites applicants for the position of a tenure-track Assistant Professor with an anticipated start date on August 16, 2027. We seek exceptional candidates with commensurate experience and a proven track record with nationally, or the potential for, nationally and internationally recognized scholarship.   The department seeks an enthusiastic and dedicated design educator with innovative, creative, and emerging approaches to design pedagogy and research. Successful candidates will demonstrate an understanding of contemporary topics in interior design and related fields, informed by diverse and forward-thinking perspectives. We seek educators who create and foster design excellence and value interdisciplinary collaboration. This role requires maintaining an active record of creative research and/or scholarship in interior design related areas, with a focus on how these explorations inform and shape the future of design education and the profession. We especially seek individuals with experience and knowledge in low-impact, environmentally responsible design and interior lighting design, as well as interest in critical and ethical use of emerging technologies, including artificial intelligence. Applicants will also be expected to contribute to advancing initiatives that align with the department’s core values and its mission of examining how design can support a holistic approach to individual well-being.    Candidates will have the opportunity to teach design studios, seminars, and lecture courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels and mentor graduate students.  Additionally, participation in service activities within the department, college, university, and the broader ISU community is expected.  Candidates should possess strong communication skills, a commitment to teaching excellence, and exhibit the potential for long-term scholarship in supporting the mission of the department, college, and university.   The Department of Interior Design is committed to sustaining a collegial, positive, and productive environment for each individual and the collective benefit of all. All faculty members are expected to exhibit and convey good citizenship within department, college, and university activities, and maintain the highest standards of integrity and ethical behavior.   Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position.   Required Minimum Qualifications: Terminal Degree in Interior Design/Interior Architecture or Design-Related Discipline (Ph.D., M.F.A., M. Arch., or equivalent) At least one degree in Interior Design/Interior Architecture   Preferred Qualifications: NCIDQ certified or ability to become qualified within one year of appointment. Demonstrated evidence or potential for national and/or international scholarship. Evidence of teaching experience or professional practice and management across the program curricula. Experience with relevant industry-standard software (e.g., Revit, AutoCAD, Adobe Suite, SketchUp, Unreal Engine). LEED, WELL, EDAC, CAPS certification, or other relevant certification(s).   Department/Program & College Description: The Department of Interior Design is a vibrant program in the College of Design at Iowa State University, along with Architecture, Industrial Design, Graphic Design, Art and Visual Culture, Landscape Architecture, and Urban Planning and Development. The Department of Interior Design is a CIDA accredited program that offers a Bachelor of Fine Arts in Interior Design (BFA).  The Department also offers a Master of Arts in Interior Design (MA), a Master of Fine Arts in Interior Design (MFA), and an interdisciplinary double degree with the Department of Architecture (MA-MArch). The department also offers experiential learning in immersive study abroad programs, encourages  professional internships, and pursues student outreach projects in support of the Land Grant mission.  There are many interdisciplinary opportunities, and strategic collaborations with other highly ranked colleges and departments.   More than 200 undergraduate students, 15 graduate students, and 12 faculty members make up the Department of Interior Design, united by a shared commitment to excellence. Over the past decade, ISU interior design students have won multiple national and international awards, and students have participated in several Venice Biennale sessions. The department is recognized for its development of interdisciplinary collaborations.   Department Unit/Website: For more information about our department’s design program, see https://www.design.iastate.edu/interior-design/   Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. However, to receive full consideration, applications should be received by January 31, 2027 . All interested, qualified persons must apply for this position online at jobs.iastate.edu to Job Requisition Number R20159 .   The following documents are required to be submitted in PDF format:   1) Letter of application that briefly discusses how the candidate meets each of the preferred qualifications 2) A curriculum vitae (include a list of courses taught, if available) 3) Contact information for at least three references, including name, email address, phone number, and other pertinent information. References will not be contacted until the campus interview phase. 4) Other documents, as relevant: Teaching philosophy (1-2 pages) Statement of research/creative scholarship (1-2 pages) Portfolio of creative work and student work (up to 20 samples)   Inquiries regarding this position may be directed to Hamed Yekita, Chair of the Search Committee, at yekita@iastate.edu . Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: October 30, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20159 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Assistant-Athletics-Director-for-Sports-Nutrition_R20111": {
      "title": "Assistant Athletics Director for Sports Nutrition",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-30\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Athletics Director for Sports Nutrition Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s and 5 years of related experience. Registered dietitian with the Commission on Dietetic Registration (CDR). Must have and maintain licensure as a Licensed Dietitian in the State of Iowa. Job Description: The Iowa State University Athletics Department invites applications for a dynamic and experienced Assistant Athletics Director for Sports Nutrition.  This position will serve as a key leader, shaping departmental operations and nutritional strategies that fuel Cyclone student-athletes. This role offers the opportunity to continue building and enhancing a high-performing nutrition program supported by industry-leading facilities and infrastructure, lead a dedicated staff, and directly impact competitive success through evidence-based performance nutrition.   What you’ll do Lead business operations for Performance Nutrition, including strategic planning, forecasting, education, annual reports, and fiscal oversight of an annual budget of approximately $4 million. Ensure strong financial controls and compliance with guidelines. Serve on the Sports Medicine, Performance, and Welfare leadership team. Work closely with internal and external partners and stakeholders to maximize student‑athlete potential through nutrition fostering positive, collegial, and collaborative relationships. Direct meal planning and scheduling for the Stark Performance Center Nutrition Center, catered meals, post‑competition recovery strategies ,and fueling stations. Serve as the liaison between ISU and the nutrition center vendor. Supervise full‑time staff members and student interns, fostering a collaborative, service‑oriented team culture that builds a culture of trust, confidence, and confidentiality with the student-athletes. Maintain comprehensive nutrition programs tailored by sport and individuals including disordered eating planning that enhance athletic performance and support student‑athlete wellness. Provide confidential, individualized dietetic assessments and counseling to student‑athletes and teams. Oversee sports nutrition education. Play an integral role in recruiting presentations. Establish and foster a working relationship with Iowa State's nationally recognized Department of Food Science and Nutrition to provide clinical experience and supervision for future sport dietitians. Ensure all duties are performed in accordance with NCAA, Big 12 Conference, and university policies. The ideal candidate will possess proven experience in sports dietetics, along with strong leadership, operations management, and budget planning skills. This position requires a strong customer service focus, excellent communication and presentation skills, the ability to solve problems and exercise sound judgment, and a commitment to multiculturalism and working with a diverse student body. Some evening and weekend work is required to provide consultation to student-athletes, coaches or prospect families. This position serves at the pleasure of university administration and is exempt from certain P&S policies. Preferred Qualifications Board Certified Specialist in Sports Dietetics (CSSD). Related master’s degree. Documented experience in administrative oversight of sports nutrition department, or equivalent. Experience managing the budget for a large collegiate sports nutrition department and dining center. Experience providing sports nutrition counseling, educational programming, and meal planning for athletes and teams.  Experience counseling disordered eating/eating disorders. Expertise working with nutritional supplement programs for athletes.  About ISU Athletics As an NCAA Football Bowl Subdivision athletics program and a founding member of the Big 12 Conference, Iowa State University sponsors 18 intercollegiate athletics teams and supports 450 student-athletes in their pursuit of academic and athletic excellence. ISU Athletics employs over 250 talented and dedicated full-time staff members, more than 500 temporary and student employees, and multiple auxiliary partners who collaboratively work within a culture to support and enhance the experiences of Cyclone student-athletes and their loyal fan base. Iowa State student-athletes have produced 10-consecutive years of record-setting Graduation Success Rate scores in the classroom, while athletically, the Cyclones have captured 19 national team championships, 140 national individual titles and 162 conference team championships in its rich history.   www.cyclones.com   Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an on-going basis without sponsorship.   Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume Contact information for 3 references Cover Letter (optional) Why Choose Iowa State University ? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. This position serves at the pleasure of university administration and is exempt from certain P&S policies. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS810 Original Posting Date: October 30, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 12, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20111 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Budget-and-Finance-Specialist-II_R20148": {
      "title": "Budget and Finance Specialist II",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-29\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Budget and Finance Specialist II Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 2 years of related experience Job Description: The Ivy College of Business is hiring a Budget and Finance Specialist II to support the financial operations and budget needs of assigned departments and college units.   The successful candidate will provide excellent customer service, stay organized, and manage competing priorities. They will produce accurate, timely financial reports, respond promptly to enquiries, pay close attention to detail, and maintain audit readiness. They will also proactively share updates and follow up on outstanding requests to keep internal partners informed.   Examples of Duties: Manage and monitor departmental budgets and expenditure. Review and approve financial transactions for policy compliance. Investigate irregular transactions and support year-end financial closing. Coordinate financial activities related to vendor payments, contracts, grants, and foundation accounts. Process student hiring, separations, and tuition award approvals. Maintain accurate financial documentation and records. Prepare and present timely, accurate budget and financial reports to department leadership. Monitor grant balances and review purchasing card transactions. Ensure compliance with university financial policies and procedures. Coordinate financial activities across departments. Review audit reports and communicate policy updates. Improve financial processes and procedures. Provide financial training and guidance to faculty, staff, and students. Develop and communicate financial policies and instructional materials. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in finance, accounting, or a related field. Experience managing departmental budgets, monitoring expenditure, and preparing financial reports. Knowledge of financial policies, procedures, internal controls, and compliance requirements. Ability to interpret and communicate financial information while providing guidance, training, and support to faculty, staff, and leadership. This is an onsite position located in Ames, IA. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. The following application materials are required: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS808 Original Posting Date: October 29, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 8, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20148 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Assistant-Teaching-Professor-of-Communication-Studies_R20158": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor of Communication Studies",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-29\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Teaching Professor of Communication Studies Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: The Communication Studies program, in the Department of Psychology in the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences at Iowa State University in Ames, Iowa, invites applications for an in-person term faculty position at the rank of Assistant Teaching Professor. This is a part-time (75% appointment) position with a standard teaching load of six courses per academic year, in person and online.   Responsibilities include teaching professional communication, leadership, training and development, organizational communication, and other courses as needed based on the candidate's expertise.   The position is a 9-month appointment with an initial term of three years, beginning August 16, 2027. Renewal for additional three-year terms is contingent upon performance and departmental needs.   Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position.   Required Minimum Qualifications : MA in Communication Studies or a closely related area by the time of appointment Record of excellence in teaching Communication Studies courses at the university level   Preferred Qualifications :  Experience teaching professional communication, leadership, training and development, and/or organizational communication PhD in Communication Studies or a closely related area by the time of appointment Record of excellence in teaching Communication Studies courses at the university level Demonstrated commitment to serving strategic program initiatives Department/Program & College Description : Communication Studies at Iowa State University is housed in the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences and offers an undergraduate major and minor. Consistent with the university’s land-grant mission, the program is committed to excellence in undergraduate education and the advancement of the understanding of human communication through teaching, practice, and research. In keeping with the land grant mission of Iowa State University, faculty share their expertise in the classroom, throughout the university, and with the broader community.   Faculty value collegiality and evidence-based teaching practices, and Iowa State supports a collaborative and student-centered teaching environment with strong instructional resources and professional development opportunities.   Iowa State University is located in Ames, Iowa, a vibrant community of over 66,000 residents, approximately 30 minutes north of Des Moines. Ames was ranked the #5 Best College Town in America (Best College Reviews, 2022), #15 on the Top 100 Best Places to Live (Livability.com, 2020), and the healthiest city in the State of Iowa (USA Today, 2020). Ames has 38 parks, 55 miles of bike and pedestrian trails, golf courses, lakes, and an aquatics center for outdoor recreation. Additional information about the city of Ames is available at: https://www.cityofames.org/About-Ames   Department Unit/Website : https://comst.las.iastate.edu/ Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Proposed End Date or Length of Term: May 15, 2030 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Part time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of Application/Cover Letter 3) Evidence of teaching effectiveness Teaching Statement (1-2 pages) describing the applicant’s teaching experience in communication courses and instructional philosophy Copies of at least two years of teaching evaluations 4) Contact Information for Three References For guaranteed consideration, please apply by December 1, 2026. The position will remain open until filled. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Original Posting Date: October 29, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20158 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Data-Analyst-I_R20155": {
      "title": "Part-time Data Management and Reporting Analyst",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-29\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Part-time Data Management and Reporting Analyst Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree Job Description: The Seed Science Center at Iowa State University is seeking a Part-Time Data Management and Reporting Analyst to support operational reporting, data quality, and program assessment. In this role, you’ll turn data from multiple systems into useful information that helps leaders evaluate performance, make informed decisions, and identify opportunities for improvement. This is a part-time position at 50% FTE, averaging approximately 20 hours per week, with flexibility in scheduling work hours. What You’ll Do Analyze operational data to identify trends in sample volumes, testing activities, customer service, turnaround times, revenue, workload distribution, and program performance. Develop recurring and ad hoc reports, dashboards, visualizations, and performance metrics to support decision-making and operational improvements. Collect, organize, clean, validate, and maintain data from multiple systems to ensure accuracy, consistency, and completeness. Investigate data discrepancies, resolve reporting issues, and collaborate with information technology staff on system updates and improvements. Maintain documentation of data definitions, reporting methods, business rules, and data quality standards. Support accreditation reviews, annual reporting, program assessment, and evaluation of organizational goals and performance measures. Participate in user testing and validation of system updates and reporting modifications. Help staff access, interpret, and use reports and data resources; develop training materials and user documentation as needed. Follow established data governance practices and FAIR data principles to ensure data is findable, accessible, interoperable, and reusable. Provide basic support for reporting systems and business applications and assist student employees or project participants as assigned.   Preferred Qualifications Experience analyzing data to identify trends, patterns, or operational performance measures. Experience developing reports, dashboards, or data visualizations using Excel, Power BI, Tableau, or similar tools. Experience collecting, cleaning, validating, and maintaining datasets from multiple sources. Experience using databases, reporting systems, or business applications to retrieve, organize, or manage data. Experience documenting data definitions, reporting procedures, or data quality standards. Experience communicating analytical findings or providing training and technical assistance to help others use data and reporting tools. MS SQL and MS Visual Studio experience. Why Join Us? The Seed Science Center is a preeminent institution in American agriculture with a longstanding history of supporting the seed industry through research, education, testing, and outreach. You'll join a close-knit team of approximately 30 employees who value collaboration, build strong working relationships, and create a welcoming environment. This is an opportunity to contribute to meaningful work while becoming part of a team that takes pride in its work and enjoys connecting through shared activities. About the Opportunity The candidate will be hired as a Data Analyst I. This is a term position that may have an opportunity for renewal. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. How to Apply Please submit a resume or CV and a cover letter describing your relevant experience in data management, reporting, data analysis, and related systems or tools. For guaranteed consideration, please apply on or before November 5 th , 2026. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular with Term Appointment (Fixed Term) Proposed End Date or Length of Term: February 28, 2029 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Part time Pay Grade: PS807 Original Posting Date: October 29, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 8, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20155 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Deputy-Athletics-Director---Chief-Revenue-Officer--CRO-_R20143": {
      "title": "Deputy Athletics Director - Chief Revenue Officer (CRO)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-28\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Deputy Athletics Director - Chief Revenue Officer (CRO) Appointment Type: Contract Job Description: Iowa State Athletics seeks an innovative and results-driven executive to serve as Deputy Athletics Director and Chief Revenue Officer to help position the department for continued success in an evolving collegiate athletics environment. Reporting directly to the Director of Athletics, this position serves as a member of the executive staff and provides strategic leadership for Iowa State Athletics’ revenue generation and external-facing operations. The position oversees strategic communications, marketing and fan experience, communications, digital media, licensing, Cyclone Sports Properties, creative services, broadcast/television, and will serve as a sport administrator. Working closely with the Director of Athletics and executive staff, the CRO develops integrated strategies to grow commercial revenue, maximize CYTown monetization, strengthen the Iowa State brand, expand fan engagement, and enhance the experience of student-athletes, fans, alumni, and corporate partners. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Executive Leadership: Serves on the executive staff and advises the Director of Athletics on revenue strategy, brand positioning, external communications, fan engagement, and commercial partnerships. Establishes goals, budgets, performance measures, and cross-functional priorities for assigned units; recruits, develops, and evaluates staff. Collaborates with the ISU Foundation, University Marketing, and other campus partners to align messaging, relationships, and institutional priorities. Areas of Direct Responsibility: Revenue Generation: Leads integrated commercial revenue strategy, including sponsorship, multimedia rights, licensing, digital platforms, and new revenue opportunities, including CYTown-related commercial opportunities; coordinates with leaders responsible for ticketing, premium seating, fundraising, and other revenue streams. Strategic Communications: Directs long-range external communications strategy, institutional messaging, reputation management, and coordinated communications on major department initiatives. Marketing & Fan Experience: Oversees marketing campaigns, attendance and engagement initiatives, promotions, game presentation, and the overall fan experience across athletics venues. Communications: Provides leadership for athletics communications, media relations, public information, storytelling, and crisis communications in coordination with university partners. Digital Media: Oversees digital content strategy, athletics websites, social media channels, audience development, and digital engagement and monetization opportunities. Licensing: Leads athletics licensing strategy, brand usage, merchandise-related partnerships, and licensing revenue in coordination with university stakeholders and licensees. CYTown Monetization: Leads athletics-related commercial strategy and revenue opportunities associated with CYTown, including sponsorships, naming rights, advertising, event programming, experiential activations, and other partnership opportunities; collaborates with university leadership, project stakeholders, and Cyclone Sports Properties to coordinate inventory, agreements, activation, and long-term revenue performance. Cyclone Sports Properties: Provides executive oversight of the multimedia rights relationship, including sponsorship sales strategy, inventory, activation, partner servicing, contractual performance, and revenue goals. Creative Services: Oversees creative direction, graphic design, video production, photography, and consistent visual identity across departmental platforms and campaigns. Broadcast/TV: Provides strategic oversight of athletics broadcasting, television production, live event coverage, and related distribution and content partnerships. Sport Administration: Serves as sport administrator for assigned programs, supporting head coaches, student-athlete experience, competitive planning, budget oversight, and alignment with departmental priorities. Other Duties: Performs other duties as assigned by the Director of Athletics.   Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree. Progressive leadership experience in intercollegiate athletics, sports business, or a related field, including oversight of revenue or external operations. Demonstrated success in revenue generation, strategic leadership, marketing, communications, media, or commercial partnerships.   Preferred Qualifications: Executive-level leadership experience in intercollegiate athletics. Experience overseeing multimedia rights, brand and communications, digital content, broadcast operations, or multiple external units. Master's degree in business, sport management, communications, marketing, or a related field.   About ISU Athletics: As a proud member of the Big 12 Conference, Iowa State University Athletics sponsors 18 NCAA Division I varsity sports and is committed to providing a transformational student-athlete experience centered on competitive excellence, academic achievement, leadership development, health and well-being, and personal growth. Iowa State student-athletes have produced 10-consecutive years of record-setting Graduation Success Rate scores in the classroom, while athletically, the Cyclones have captured numerous national team championships, national individual titles, and conference team championships in its rich history.  ISU Athletics employs over 250 talented and dedicated full-time staff members, more than 500 hourly and student employees, and multiple auxiliary partners who collaboratively work within a culture to support and enhance the experiences of Cyclone student-athletes and our amazing fan base, while advancing the mission and strategic priorities of Iowa State University. www.cyclones.com   Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an on-going basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume Cover letter Contact Information for references   Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program   If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Proposed Start Date: November 16, 2026 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: Contract Original Posting Date: October 23, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 6, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20143 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Groundskeeper-I_R20150": {
      "title": "Groundskeeper I",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-27\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Groundskeeper I Job Group: Merit Required Minimum Qualifications: • One year of experience in operating the machinery and tools used in groundskeeping work or any combination of related experience and education from which comparable knowledge and ability can be acquired which totals one year. Special Required Qualifications Valid U.S. Driver's License Job Description: The Facilities Planning and Management Department at Iowa State University is seeking a dedicated Groundskeeper I to join our team. This position plays a vital role in maintaining the university's grounds, ensuring they remain attractive and well-kept throughout all seasons. Under direct supervision, the Groundskeeper I will operate and maintain power equipment, trucks, and light machinery, as well as perform a variety of landscaping tasks such as mowing, trimming, and planting. Seasonal maintenance, including leaf removal and snow clearing, is also a key part of the role. Working collaboratively with the groundskeeping team, this position helps uphold the beauty and safety of the campus.  Preferred Qualifications Mowing experience Grading experience Planting experience Tree and shrub maintenance experience Commercial Drivers License (CDL), Class B with air brake, motor vehicle inspector certification The position follows a schedule of Monday through Friday, 6:00 a.m. – 2:30 p.m. Join us and contribute to keeping Iowa State University’s campus looking its best year-round!  Characteristic Duties and Responsibilities   • Operates tractors with attachments such as mowers, tillers, post hole diggers and snow plows to landscape and maintain grounds including lawn areas, sidewalks, parking lots and streets. • Maintains attachments and makes minor emergency repairs. • Operates and maintains power and hand mowing equipment. • Assists in the cultivation and care of shrubs, trees and flowers as directed. • Operates trucks and other transportation equipment as required. • Responds to calls for emergency service, including snow removal, as required.   Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities   • Ability to understand and follow oral and written instructions and specifications. • Ability to safely operate and maintain equipment and hand/power tools. • Ability to apply various groundskeeping techniques to different work situations. • Ability to lift. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: 5731a Original Posting Date: October 27, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 7, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20150 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Admissions-II_R20144": {
      "title": "Admissions II",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Admissions II Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 2 years of related experience Job Description: The Office of Enrollment Services at Iowa State University is dedicated to fulfilling the university’s land-grant mission by attracting, recruiting, orienting, enrolling, and retaining students to meet institutional enrollment goals. We are seeking qualified candidates for the Admissions II – Enrollment Advisor position. This role plays a vital part in supporting prospective and current students as they navigate the enrollment process by providing high-quality support related to admissions and financial aid through phone, e-mail, and in-person interactions. The successful candidate will manage incoming communication, advise on admissions and financial aid processes, handle escalated inquiries, and connect students with appropriate campus resources. Key Responsibilities Counsel and guide prospective and current students through the full enrollment process. Provide accurate and timely customer service via phone, email, and in-person communication. Manage high-volume inquiries with professionalism, efficiency, and a positive attitude. Advise on admissions requirements, application status, financial aid processes, and action items. Utilize Workday Student, Salesforce, and other systems to research and resolve student questions. Navigate moderate to complex inquiries with accuracy and escalate issues when appropriate. Interpret and apply admissions and financial aid policies, procedures, and compliance requirements. Track and document communications in CRM systems to ensure consistent and accurate follow-up. Make outbound calls to assist students in completing admissions and financial aid steps. Schedule appointments and assist students during office visits and campus events. Provide basic technical support and direct students to ITS when needed. Communicate in a clear, friendly, and professional manner aligned with university standards. Identify inquiry trends and share insights to support improved communication and processes. Participate in individual and group training, proactively addressing knowledge gaps. Support admissions and enrollment events such as campus visits, Admitted Student Day, and Destination Iowa State. About the Office of Enrollment Services The Office of Enrollment Services at Iowa State University is committed to supporting students through exceptional service, personalized guidance, and innovative outreach. Our team works collaboratively to ensure an engaging, student-centered admissions experience that reflects the university’s values of integrity, hard work, and excellence. By joining our office, you will contribute to meaningful work that supports student success and helps shape the future of Iowa State University! Example of Duties • Provides information and guidance to prospective students and their families regarding university programs, student life, upcoming deadlines, and admission policies and procedures. • Counsels and advises prospective, current, and former students, parents, faculty and staff concerning financial aid, admission policies, procedures, application materials and transfer credit issues. • Opportunity to represent the University at on-campus recruitment and orientation events. • Provides status updates regarding eligibility, scholarships, and applications. • Counsels students and families at the generalist level on financial aid including eligibility, application procedures, aid programs, and costs. • Works closely with student employees and assists with overseeing work of student employees. • Opportunity to assist with training and development of student employees. Preferred Qualifications: Experience working in higher education student services. Experience with systems such as: Workday Student, Salesforce (or other CRM systems), and Navigate. Experience in a high-volume customer service role, including handling complex or sensitive inquiries with professionalism and care. Background in interpreting policies, regulations, or compliance guidelines. Experience engaging with various populations such as: students, families, counselors, campus partners, and community partners. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS806 Original Posting Date: October 26, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 9, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20144 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Assistant-Professor--Land-Use---Resilience-Planning_R20147": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor: Land-Use & Resilience Planning",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor: Land-Use & Resilience Planning Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: Iowa State University Extension and Outreach Community and Economic Development (CED)in partnership with the Department of Urban Planning and Development (UPD) in the College of Design, invites applications for a 12-month tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Land-Use & Resilience Planning.   We seek a scholar and educator whose research and teaching focus on how communities can use land-use planning to address changing conditions in Iowa, manage natural resources, and build long-term community resilience. The successful candidate will contribute to UPD's teaching and research mission while developing an applied extension and outreach program through CED that responds to the needs of Iowa communities.   With a joint appointment in UPD and CED, the candidate will work with local governments, regional organizations, state agencies, community organizations, and other partners. The successful candidate will translate research and planning knowledge into practical tools, programs, technical assistance, and educational resources. A start-up package will be available to initiate research and statewide engagement.   About ISU Extension and Outreach, Community and Economic Development Iowa State University Extension and Outreach Community and Economic Development (CED) works with communities across Iowa to strengthen local economies, leadership, and quality of life. CED connects university expertise with community needs through applied research, education, technical assistance, and partnerships in areas such as community planning, economic development, housing, and local governance. Website: https://www.extension.iastate.edu/communities/programs-and-services   Department of Urban Planning and Development The Department of Urban Planning and Development (UPD) at Iowa State University prepares students to address the complex challenges facing cities, towns, and regions. Through teaching, research, and community engagement, UPD faculty focus on areas such as land-use planning, housing, transportation, community and economic development, environmental resilience, local governance and planning technologies, with a strong emphasis on applying planning knowledge to real-world community needs. Please visit the departmental website for more information: https://www.design.iastate.edu/academics/departments/upd/ .   Areas of Interest We welcome candidates whose scholarship and practice address one or more of the following areas: land-use planning; land-use law and regulation; planning for rural, regional and community resilience; natural-resource and watershed planning; or economic development.   Candidates whose work connects multiple areas and demonstrates the application of planning knowledge to community challenges are particularly encouraged to apply. The position provides an opportunity to integrate research, teaching, and community engagement around some of the most consequential challenges facing urban and rural communities in Iowa.     Position Responsibilities The successful candidate will contribute to Iowa State University’s land grant mission and the teaching, research, extension, and service imperatives of the Department of Urban Planning and Development, the College of Design, and ISU Extension and Outreach.     The successful candidate will teach undergraduate and graduate courses in areas such as land-use planning, planning law, community resilience, and natural resources and watershed planning, as well as contribute to innovative planning courses and studios consistent with departmental needs and aligned with the work program of ISU Extension and Outreach.   A major component of this position will be developing an applied research and extension program focused on land-use planning and resilience in Iowa communities. The future faculty member will be expected to pursue external funding; disseminate scholarship through appropriate academic, extension, and professional venues; translate research to community needs and for public audiences; develop interdisciplinary collaborations within and beyond Iowa State University; establish a leadership role in statewide land use matters; and engage communities throughout Iowa.   Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position.   Required Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. degree in urban and regional planning, environmental planning, geography, law, policy, public administration, or a closely related field by the start date.   Preferred Qualifications: Evidence of research or scholarly potential related to land-use planning and resilience. Evidence of the ability to contribute to undergraduate and graduate teaching in planning. Experience with community-engaged research or applied planning practice. Ability to translate research into practical tools, programs, or decision-support resources for communities and practitioners. Experience working with local governments, residents, regional organizations, extension systems, public agencies, or community-based organizations. Evidence of or potential for developing an externally funded research program. Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: Candidates should submit: 1. Letter of application describing their interest in the position and alignment with its teaching, research and extension responsibilities. 2. Curriculum vitae. 3. Community engagement philosophy statement. 4. Teaching statement describing teaching philosophy and experience. 5. Contact information for three professional references. Guaranteed consideration date is December 15, 2026 and application reviews will continue until the position is filled. The anticipated start date is August 16, 2027 . Questions about the position may be directed to Dr. Carlton Basmajian , Search Committee Chair, at carlton@iastate.edu . Questions about the application process may be directed to employment@iastate.edu or 515-294-4800. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: October 26, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20147 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Clinical-or-Tenure-Track---Assistant-Associate-Full-Professor-Small-Animal-Emergency-and-Critical-Care-Medicine_R20140": {
      "title": "Clinical or Tenure Track – Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Small Animal Emergency and Critical Care Medicine",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Clinical or Tenure Track – Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Small Animal Emergency and Critical Care Medicine Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The College of Veterinary Medicine at Iowa State University (ISU), located in Ames, Iowa, is seeking qualified applicants for a full-time, clinical or tenure track faculty appointment in the area of Small Animal Emergency and Critical Care Medicine in the Department of Veterinary Clinical Sciences (VCS) at the Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center (LVMC). The LVMC is a state-of-the-art teaching hospital providing specialized care for companion and large animals throughout Iowa and surrounding states. The candidate will join a department with over 50 diverse faculty and staff members, allied in teaching, research, and clinical efforts relevant to companion animals, equids, and other large animals . The successful candidate will provide clinical service and teaching at the Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center (LVMC). The primary focus for all aspects of the position will be on veterinary emergency and critical care for patients in the Hixson-Lied Small Animal Hospital. Clinical duties may include weekend and after-hours obligations which are divided among all ECC faculty. Supervision and instruction of interns and residents, instruction of clinical-year students, and primary case supervision is expected, in addition to participation in and contribution to weekly resident boards review and journal clubs. The successful candidate will also have a collegial, collaborative attitude and willingness to participate in all levels of technician, student, and house officer education. Remaining effort may include participation in research, scholarship, and traditional didactic and laboratory teaching. Appointment rank will be determined based on the qualifications, documented experience, and interests of the selected candidate. The successful candidate will join a program currently supported by four small animal ACVECC diplomates, six residents, one ECC specialty intern, nine rotating interns, and three large animal ACVECC diplomates as well as registered veterinary technicians; including two VTS-ECC .  The emergency and critical care department is a young yet established service that is continuing to experience steady growth. Centered in the State of Iowa, just 30 minutes from the capital, Des Moines, the LVMC serves a large geographic region (Iowa and surrounding states), providing a diverse and challenging caseload that allows the ECC service to practice cutting edge medicine. Services and technology supporting the ECC service include but are not limited to digital radiography, point of care ultrasound, advanced imaging (1.5T MRI, 32-Slice CT), interventional radiology, mechanical ventilation (Servo-u, and Servo-i), high velocity nasal insufflation (three Vapotherm units), therapeutic plasma exchange (Amicus device), multi-parameter monitoring systems, an in-house blood bank, VCM, and three pharmacists with compounding capability. Continuous renal replacement therapy (Prismaflex) is also available with the goal of onboarding hemoperfusion capabilities in the future. The successful candidate will share oversight of the ICU, Critical Care Service and the Emergency Service with the other ECC faculty members. The 43-cage ICU is currently managed in an open style with all services providing primary care, utilizing a collaborative approach to maximize case management. The 24/7 Emergency Service sees approximately 5,000 cases/year, including first opinion cases as well as referrals. The LVMC is AAHA accredited, a VetCOT Level 2 trauma center and a Level I VECCS certified facility.   Ames, Iowa is often found at the top of lists for best college towns and most livable cities in the US. A low cost of living and friendly midwestern hospitality help maintain a small-town feel, with easy access to college sports, the arts, and countless parks and outdoor activities.   Required Minimum Qualifications: DVM or equivalent degree. Successful completion of an American College of Veterinary Emergency and Critical Care (ACVECC) or European College of Veterinary Emergency Care (ECVECC) residency. Individuals in their final year of residency training are also encouraged to apply and will be considered. Eligible for a State of Iowa Veterinary License on or before first day of employment. Eligible to register under the state Controlled Substances Act with the Iowa Board of Pharmacy upon employment. In addition, positions at the following ranks will require: CLINICAL ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR: Must have experience in academia and a record of contributions of an appropriate magnitude and quality in the clinical specialty. There should be evidence of promise for further academic development and contributions to their field.  CLINICAL PROFESSOR : Must have substantial academic experience and contributions to their professional field. TENURE track : Must hold credentials in a specialty field (i.e. DACVECC)   Preferred Qualifications: ACVECC/ECVECC diplomate Demonstrated experience in didactic and clinical teaching of veterinary students. Experience in modern, veterinary emergency and critical care practices and standards of care. Demonstrated experience and willingness to train interns Demonstrated experience and willingness to train residents for successful completion of the ACVECC certifying exam. A record of, or notable potential of, scholarship production through manuscript publication/preparation, preparation/success in granting activity, an advanced academic degree (MS or PhD), or national scholarly, clinical, or educational presentations.   Department/Program & College Description: The LVMC is a state-of-the-art facility designed to provide specialized care and comprehensive medical and surgical services for companion, exotic, and large animals throughout Iowa and surrounding states. Our clinicians, residents, interns, technicians, staff, and senior veterinary students work collaboratively to provide 24-hour, high-quality care to animal patients.   Department Unit/Website: www.vetmed.iastate.edu/vcs ; https://vetmed.iastate.edu/vmc Proposed Start Date: June 1, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of Application/Cover Letter 3) Contact Information for Three (3) external to Iowa State References If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. For full guaranteed consideration, please apply on or before November 23, 2026. This position is open until filled. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: October 26, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20140 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Digital-Scholarship-Librarian-II_R20004": {
      "title": "Digital Scholarship Librarian II",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Digital Scholarship Librarian II Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree and 2 years of related experience Job Description: The Iowa State University Library is seeking applications for a Digital Scholarship Librarian II. Housed in the Digital Scholarship and Initiatives department, this position provides leadership and expertise in digital scholarship, supporting the creation, discovery, access, and sustainable stewardship of research outputs in an evolving technological landscape.   The role applies expertise in web and open-source technologies, data, and emerging technologies such as AI to develop digital scholarship projects and strengthen digital research methods in support of student learning and faculty research.   The successful candidate will demonstrate strong collaboration and communication skills, a commitment to user-centered approaches to technology, and the ability to work both independently and as part of a team in a rapidly evolving digital environment. Example of Duties: Develop and support digital scholarship projects involving static web technology, web-based storytelling, digital collections, open access research, and open educational resources. Enhance the Digital Scholarship and Initiatives department's digital infrastructure to improve the discoverability, accessibility, and sustainability of its digital projects and platforms. Support and expand open access initiatives by enhancing the discoverability and reach of research outputs and archival material in the institutional repository and digital collections. Provide instruction and outreach in areas such as AI literacy, web technologies, and computational and data-informed research methods. Contribute to external partnerships and initiatives that strengthen the library's role in research and teaching. The library is committed to supporting all librarians through mentoring, training, and professional development opportunities to foster success and growth in their work. The Digital Scholarship Librarian will be supported in the pursuit of continued learning relevant to their position and encouraged to share their skills with their colleagues at ISU and beyond. Preferred Qualifications: Experience working with digital scholarship tools and technologies, including web development technologies and platforms, data-focused approaches, digital collections, or institutional repositories. Ability to teach and support research using digital methods, AI and digital literacy concepts, and emerging technologies. Demonstrated experience using HTML, CSS, JavaScript, Git/GitHub, or related web development technologies. Experience supporting the discoverability and access of digital projects through metadata and structured data, APIs, or user-centered design. Strong collaboration, communication, and problem-solving skills, with the ability to work effectively with a wide range of collaborators, learn new technologies, and address technical challenges creatively. This posting will be open until filled. However, to receive full consideration, please apply before November 9th, 2026. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS808 Original Posting Date: October 26, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20004 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Assistant-Director-Student-Recruitment_R20121": {
      "title": "Assistant Director Student Recruitment",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Director Student Recruitment Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 5 years of related experience Job Description: Lead Strategic Student Recruitment at Iowa State University The College of Agriculture and Life Sciences (CALS) at Iowa State University is seeking an Assistant Director for Student Recruitment to lead undergraduate recruitment strategy and advance enrollment growth. Reporting directly to the Associate Dean for Academic Innovation, this highly visible role will use data, team leadership, and strategic partnerships to strengthen enrollment outcomes across CALS academic programs.   Why This Role Matters CALS academic departments bring a range of strengths, priorities, and opportunities for student recruitment. You'll have the opportunity to shape college-wide recruitment strategy, lead an energetic, collaborative team, and work with academic departments and campus leaders to develop approaches that connect more students with CALS programs.   Success in this role depends on building relationships, sharing insights, and turning ideas into action to advance shared recruitment goals.   What You'll Do Develop and implement undergraduate recruitment strategies aligned with university and college enrollment priorities. Analyze recruitment trends, conversion rates, and enrollment outcomes to identify opportunities, set goals, and improve student yield across academic programs. Lead, coach, and develop the CALS recruitment team, fostering collaboration, accountability, and continuous improvement. Oversee recruitment planning, budgeting, staffing, and performance management to align resources with college priorities. Build partnerships with department leaders, faculty, staff, Admissions, Marketing, Extension, and external organizations to coordinate recruitment efforts and expand outreach. Present recruitment data, strategies, and recommendations to college leadership to inform decisions and resource allocation. Lead recruitment events, campus visits, admitted-student experiences, and outreach initiatives that showcase CALS programs to prospective students. Guide scholarship strategy by evaluating fund utilization and outcomes and advising leadership on investment priorities that support recruitment, enrollment, and student success. Collaborate with campus partners to support prospective students through recruitment and transition to Iowa State and contribute to student retention and success.   The Leader We Are Looking For Strategic thinking and analytical skills to interpret enrollment trends and translate insights into effective recruitment strategies. Leadership and team development skills to guide staff, establish priorities, and foster accountability and collaboration. Communication and relationship-building skills to engage stakeholders, influence decisions, and build productive partnerships. Planning and resource management skills to align recruitment activities and resources with college priorities. Adaptability and initiative to address departmental needs, respond to enrollment challenges, and identify opportunities for improvement. Preferred Qualifications : Experience leading, supervising, or developing teams, including setting priorities, guiding performance, and supporting team effectiveness. Experience developing or implementing strategies related to student recruitment, enrollment, admissions, or student engagement. Experience using data and performance metrics to inform strategic decisions and improve outcomes. Experience building partnerships with academic departments, faculty, staff, or external stakeholders. Experience presenting data, recommendations, or strategic plans to support planning, resource allocation, or organizational priorities. About Us The College of Agriculture and Life Sciences at Iowa State University offers nationally recognized academic programs, impactful research, and extensive Extension outreach. CALS prepares students to address challenges in agriculture, food systems, natural resources, health, and community development. You'll join a collaborative college community where strong partnerships help students discover pathways to meaningful careers. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS809 Original Posting Date: October 26, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 8, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20121 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Micro-Credential-Program-Specialist-II_R20079": {
      "title": "Micro-Credential Program Specialist II",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Micro-Credential Program Specialist II Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 2 years of related experience Job Description: The Center for Excellence in Teaching and Learning is currently accepting applications for a Micro-Credential Program Specialist II. This position plays a critical role in advancing Iowa State University's expanding micro-credential initiative by supporting the development, implementation, administration, and continuous improvement of non-credit and credit-bearing micro-credentials and digital badges. This position serves as a central resource for faculty, staff, and program partners, coordinating project workflows, managing digital credential operations through the Accredible platform, supporting communications and outreach efforts, and maintaining program data and reporting processes. The successful candidate will collaborate with stakeholders across the university to facilitate micro-credential development and approval processes, administer digital credentials, create and maintain program resources and training materials, support marketing and promotional initiatives, and analyze program metrics to inform decision-making and program enhancement. This position requires strong organizational, communication, project coordination, and technology management skills, along with the ability to manage multiple priorities in a collaborative environment. Some key responsibilities include: Coordinate micro-credential proposals, development projects, approvals, revisions, and implementation activities. Administer and maintain the university's digital credentialing platform, including digital badge and micro-credential issuance. Partner with faculty, staff, and university stakeholders to support program development and operations. Create and maintain program communications, training resources, web content, and outreach materials. Conduct workforce and industry research to inform micro-credential development and alignment with in-demand skills. Track, analyze, and report program performance data, learner engagement, and credential outcomes. Identify opportunities to improve processes, workflows, and operational efficiencies. Represent the micro-credential program through presentations, workshops, meetings, and various outreach activities. The ideal candidate is a detail-oriented and highly organized professional who enjoys managing projects, supporting technology-enabled initiatives, working collaboratively with various stakeholders, and leveraging data to drive continuous improvement. They are comfortable balancing multiple priorities while providing exceptional service and support in a dynamic higher education environment. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with project management and workflow tools to coordinate processes Experience with developing promotional materials or other program communications using Adobe Creative Suite Understanding of workforce development, skills-based hiring, labor market research and trends Familiarity with Micro-credentialing and digital badging Previous experience working in a higher education setting For more information about Micro-Credentials and what we do, please visit: Micro-Credentials – CELT This is 2-year fixed term position. Potential renewal contingent on future funding. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Please Note: To receive full consideration, applications should be received by November 8, 2026. Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular with Term Appointment (Fixed Term) Proposed End Date or Length of Term: January 3, 2029 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS807 Original Posting Date: October 26, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20079 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Open-Term-Faculty-Position-in-Civil-Construction-and-Environmental-Engineering_R20126": {
      "title": "Open Term Faculty Position in Civil Construction and Environmental Engineering",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Open Term Faculty Position in Civil Construction and Environmental Engineering Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Civil, Construction and Environmental Engineering (CCEE), in the College of Engineering at Iowa State University ( www.ccee.iastate.edu ) invites applications for term faculty position(s) involving in-person instruction in construction engineering, geotechnical engineering, and/or structural engineering. Candidates must have the qualifications and ability to teach courses in at least two of these three areas. Appointments may be made at the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Teaching Professor or Professor of Practice, based on relevant industry and teaching experience, demonstrated accomplishments, and applicability toward department standards. Responsibilities include preparing and delivering lectures; developing course materials, homework, laboratory assignments, quizzes, examinations, and projects; evaluating student work and assigning grades; maintaining office hours; and meeting with students to support their learning. Successful candidates will collaborate with other faculty as needed to coordinate instruction and support course delivery. Grading support may be available depending on class size and availability of resources. Additional responsibilities include departmental and university service, such as serving on committees, attending meetings, and advising student organizations or competition teams. This position is described as a full-time equivalent (1.0 FTE), nine-month appointment. Appointment rank will depend on applicant qualifications. The initial term is expected to be three years, with the possibility of renewal. Term Faculty members are not tenure-eligible, but faculty members may be considered for advancement in rank in accordance with applicable policies. Candidates should demonstrate a strong record of achievement in teaching, professional engineering practice, or both in construction engineering, civil engineering, or a closely related discipline. Successful candidates will have excellent communication skills and share Iowa State University’s commitment to excellence and its Principles of Community.   Required Minimum Qualifications: Candidates for this position must hold a Bachelor’s degree in civil, construction, or architectural engineering or a related degree and have at least 5 years of relevant experience.  Candidates must demonstrate relevant industry or educational experience qualifying them to teach in a minimum of two of the three identified areas. Candidates at Associate or Full Teaching Professor rank are required to meet department standards for appointment to the rank.   Preferred Qualifications: Evidence of an impactful career in related professional practice outside of traditional academic roles. Previous teaching experience. Strong communication skills. Professional engineering licensure in the United States, or the ability to become licensed. Ability to teach in all three areas of interest (construction engineering, geotechnical engineering, and structural engineering)   Department/Program & College Description: The CCEE Department offers B.S. degree programs in civil engineering, civil engineering with environmental emphasis, construction engineering, and environmental engineering, plus M.S., MEng, and Ph.D. graduate degree programs in civil engineering and maintains externally funded research of more than $21 million annually. CCEE is committed to faculty, staff and students who can enrich University objectives in the areas of research, teaching, and service.   Department Unit/Website: https://www.ccee.iastate.edu/   Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Proposed End Date or Length of Term: May 15, 2030 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: Applications will begin to be reviewed on November 22, 2026, with full consideration given to applications received by that date. The posting will remain open until the position is filled. All interested, qualified people must apply for this position online at jobs.iastate.edu . The following documents are required to be submitted as four separate PDF files (one for each required item numbered below):  1) Letter of application/cover letter that briefly discusses how you, the candidate, meet each of the required and preferred qualifications 2) Resume or Curriculum Vitae 3) Two-page statement explaining your qualifications to teach courses in construction, geotechnical, or structures and how you would bring your experience into the courses 4) Contact information for at least three references, including name, mailing address, email address, phone number, and other pertinent information Direct questions to cceesearch@iastate.edu . Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: October 23, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20126 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Custodian-I---Department-of-Residence_R19111": {
      "title": "Custodian I - Department of Residence",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Custodian I - Department of Residence Job Group: Merit Required Minimum Qualifications: • Ability to read, write, and follow instructions. Job Description: Are you ready to embark on a custodial role that’s steady, meaningful, and rooted in community? Iowa State University is seeking a dependable and motivated applicants to join the Department of Residence as a Custodian I . You’ll have the opportunity to become a valued member of our campus community; supporting the spaces where students live, study, and connect. As one of the largest non-academic departments on campus, the Department of Residence employs more than 400 staff members who work together to create a supportive learning and social environment for students. In this role, you’ll be at the forefront of maintaining campus buildings and common areas, helping ensure spaces are clean, welcoming, and ready for daily use. Each day brings a mix of routine and variety, offering hands-on work that makes a visible difference. If you’re looking for reliable work, strong benefits, and a team-oriented environment, we encourage you to apply. What You’ll Do Perform general cleaning throughout residence hall buildings, including common areas, restrooms, offices, and other assigned spaces Maintain floors using a variety of methods such as vacuuming, mopping, scrubbing, stripping, and waxing Clean and disinfect bathrooms, fixtures, furniture, and high-touch surfaces Restock supplies such as soap, paper towels, and toilet paper in assigned areas Collect and remove trash and recycling throughout the building Move furniture and equipment as needed to support cleaning and daily operations Assist with basic upkeep such as changing light bulbs and reporting maintenance concerns Support conferences and events by handling linens, room setup, and cleanup as needed Perform limited exterior duties such as clearing entrances, sidewalks, and nearby areas What You’ll Get Insurance benefits beginning on your first day, with timely enrollment. Retirement benefits with strong university contributions. Paid vacation, sick leave, and holiday pay. Tuition reimbursement available after one year of employment. A collaborative, service-oriented workplace dedicated to supporting students. Preferred Qualifications Prior custodial, janitorial, or commercial cleaning experience Experience operating commercial cleaning equipment Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: 0003a Original Posting Date: April 29, 2026 Posting Close Date: December 13, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R19111 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
