    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/TRIO-Pre-College-Programs-Director_R20101": {
      "title": "TRIO Pre-College Programs Director",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-19\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: TRIO Pre-College Programs Director Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 5 years of related experience Special Required Qualifications Master's degree Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: Interested in leading programs that help students prepare for college, achieve academic success, and pursue their future goals? Enjoy building partnerships with schools, families, communities, and campus stakeholders to create positive student outcomes? If so, the Division of Student Affairs at Iowa State University is seeking a TRIO Pre-College Programs Director to provide leadership and oversight for the Talent Search and Upward Bound programs! This position is responsible for program administration, staff leadership, grant management, student success initiatives, and community partnerships that support college access and educational achievement. This position will be classified as a Manager Programs. What You'll Do: Provide overall leadership, strategic direction, and administrative oversight for the Talent Search and Upward Bound programs, ensuring alignment with program goals, federal TRIO requirements, and institutional priorities. Supervise, mentor, and evaluate professional and student staff, fostering a collaborative and student-centered team culture. Lead program planning, implementation, and assessment efforts designed to support college access, academic success, high school completion, and postsecondary enrollment for program participants. Oversee program budgets, resource allocation, and fiscal operations to ensure responsible stewardship of grant-funded resources. Ensure compliance with federal regulations, grant requirements, reporting standards, and university policies and procedures. Develop and maintain partnerships with K-12 schools, community organizations, campus departments, and other stakeholders to enhance program effectiveness and participant outcomes. Direct the collection, analysis, and reporting of program data, using assessment results and performance metrics to inform decision-making and continuous improvement efforts. Lead grant administration activities, including preparing annual performance reports, monitoring progress toward objectives, and coordinating grant renewal and funding initiatives. Represent the programs through outreach, recruitment activities, presentations, meetings, and community engagement efforts. Support participant recruitment, retention, and engagement strategies while promoting a supportive environment for students. Collaborate with internal and external partners to identify opportunities for program growth, innovation, and expanded student support services. Provide leadership and support for initiatives that enhance educational opportunities and student success while contributing to the continued growth and effectiveness of the TRIO programs. The successful candidate will demonstrate progressive leadership and supervisory experience, with the ability to effectively oversee multiple federally funded programs concurrently. They will possess a strong background in project administration, including grant management, budget oversight, and adherence to funding requirements. Preferred Qualifications: Doctorate (PhD) preferred in counseling, student services, education, or a closely related field. Experience working with federally funded TRIO programs or other college access and pre-college programs. Demonstrated experience building partnerships with K-12 schools, school districts, community organizations, and educational stakeholders. Experience planning, implementing, and assessing programs that support educational access, academic success, and postsecondary enrollment, including the use of program data and performance metrics to inform decision-making and continuous improvement. Grant writing experience, including proposal development and compliance with funding guidelines. About TRIO Talent Search and Upward Bound at Iowa State University: Iowa State University TRIO Talent Search is a college preparatory program funded by the U.S. Department of Education. The goal of Talent Search is to increase the likelihood that participants graduate from high school and enroll in college. Talent Search provides students with academic enrichment, financial aid resources, career exploration and advising through monthly school visits. Talent Search advisors work with school counselors and teachers to identify qualified youth who have the potential for success in college. To learn more about Talent Search, please visit TRIO Talent Search . Upward Bound is a federally funded college preparatory program for high school students. It primarily serves students from income-eligible families and those whose parents do not hold a bachelor's degree. Key features and goals of the Upward Bound program include: academic support, college and career preparation, enrichment activities, developing life skills, and a summer residential program. The long-term goal of Upward Bound is to increase the rate at which participants not only enroll in, but also graduate from, institutions of higher education. To learn more about Upward Bound, please visit TRIO Upward Bound . Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. This posting will be open until filled. However, to receive full consideration, applications need to be submitted before November 2nd, 2026. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS809 Original Posting Date: October 19, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20101 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Dewitt-IA/Program-Specialist-I---LEAP--Part-Time-_R20078": {
      "title": "Program Specialist I - LEAP (Part-Time)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-19\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Program Specialist I - LEAP (Part-Time) Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree Special Required Qualifications Valid U.S. Driver's License Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: Are you looking for a benefits-eligible role that supports your well-being while making a difference? Do you want to see the real-world impact of your work on individuals and the broader community? If so, Iowa State University Extension and Outreach is seeking qualified candidates for a Program Specialist I with the Leveraging Activities and Partnerships to Address Obesity (Iowa LEAP) project team! This individual will support Clinton County and will be located at the Clinton County Extension office in DeWitt, Iowa. What You'll Do: Coordinate and manage day-to-day activities of the Iowa LEAP project in Clinton County. Lead coalition meetings and subgroup planning sessions. Conduct community assessments (e.g., Walkability Audits, Food Service Guidelines). Develop and execute local communication campaigns. Build and maintain relationships with local partners to support community health initiatives. Collaborate with stakeholders to implement nutrition and physical activity strategies. Collect and report program data for monthly and annual CDC reporting. Participate in statewide training, technical assistance, and Extension events. This is a fixed-term position with an end date of 9/29/2027, with the opportunity for renewal. This is a part-time position (20 hours/week) that offers schedule flexibility. Local travel will be involved in this role. Preferred Qualifications : Bachelor’s degree or above in Public Health, Nutrition, or related field. Experience working with multi-level nutrition, food, or physical activity system initiatives. Experience collecting and retrieving data to prepare program reports. Experience planning/coordinating events. About Iowa LEAP with Extension and Outreach: Iowa State University Extension and Outreach received funds from the Center for Disease Control and Prevention to work in Iowa counties where 40% or more of adults have obesity. Six Iowa counties are working with local leaders to increase access to healthy food and safe, accessible places to be physically active. Extension offices in Muscatine, Cedar, Franklin, Crawford, Clinton, and West Pottawattamie are leading the way in making the healthy choice easy. To learn more, please visit LEAP . This posting will be open until filled. However, to receive full consideration, applications need to be submitted before November 2nd, 2026. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular with Term Appointment (Fixed Term) Proposed End Date or Length of Term: September 29, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Part time Pay Grade: PS806 Original Posting Date: October 19, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20078 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Professor-and-Chair---Department-of-Economics_R20103": {
      "title": "Professor and Chair - Department of Economics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-19\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Professor and Chair - Department of Economics Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Economics at Iowa State University seeks nominations and applications for the position of Professor and Chair. The department is jointly administered by the College of Agriculture and Life Sciences (CALS) and the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences (LAS), offering a distinctive environment that integrates agricultural economics and general economics within a single academic unit. The department is recognized for excellence in teaching, research, extension, outreach, and service, and supports undergraduate programs in Agricultural Business, Economics, and Business Economics, as well as graduate programs in Economics and Agricultural Economics. The Chair serves as the chief academic and administrative officer of the department and provides strategic leadership to advance the department's missions of teaching, research, extension, outreach, and service. The Chair is responsible for promoting excellence across all mission areas; facilitating strategic hiring; supporting the success and development of faculty, staff, and students; stewarding financial and human resources; and enhancing the department's visibility and impact locally, nationally, and internationally. As leader of a jointly administered department, the Chair reports to the Dean of CALS and the Dean of LAS and serves as a collaborative member of both college leadership teams. The Chair works closely with faculty, staff, students, alumni, industry partners, community stakeholders, and university administrators to advance the department's strategic priorities and contribute to the missions of Iowa State University and both colleges. The initial Chair appointment is for five years and is subject to review in accordance with university policy. The Chair serves in an at-will administrative appointment and reports jointly to the Dean of the College of Agriculture and Life Sciences and the Dean of the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences. The appointment is expected to be a 9-month faculty appointment with summer salary provided while serving as Chair. The anticipated workload distribution is approximately 80-85% administration and leadership and 15-20% scholarly, teaching, research, extension, outreach, and/or service activities. Responsibilities may be adjusted based on departmental and institutional needs. Responsibilities include:   Strategic Leadership Provide collaborative, strategic, and innovative leadership with a demonstrated commitment that advances the department's mission and strategic priorities. Lead departmental planning and continuous improvement efforts that position the department for long-term success. Foster a culture of excellence, innovation, accountability, and collegiality across all mission areas. Serve as an active and collaborative member of both CALS and LAS leadership teams. Faculty and Staff Development Recruit, retain, mentor, develop, and evaluate an outstanding faculty and staff. Support faculty success in teaching, research, extension, outreach, and service. Provide leadership for promotion and tenure, post-tenure review, faculty advancement, annual evaluations, and professional development initiatives. Foster an environment in which faculty and staff are supported, engaged, and accountable for achieving departmental goals. Research, Extension, and Outreach Leadership Advance the department's research enterprise and scholarly reputation. Support faculty and graduate students in securing extramural funding and developing impactful research programs. Ensure appropriate stewardship of Agriculture Experiment Station activities and compliance with associated reporting requirements. Promote excellence in extension and outreach programming and strengthen engagement with stakeholders throughout Iowa and beyond. Encourage interdisciplinary collaboration within the department, across colleges, and with external partners. Academic Programs and Student Success Promote excellence and innovation in undergraduate and graduate education. Support the development and continuous improvement of relevant, rigorous, and responsive academic programs. Champion student recruitment, retention, mentoring, and success. Foster a culture that values effective teaching, student learning, and graduate education. Fiscal and Operational Management Ensure effective stewardship of departmental financial, personnel, and physical resources. Provide sound fiscal leadership and maintain compliance with university and college policies and procedures. Allocate resources strategically in support of departmental priorities and goals. Ensure efficient and effective departmental operations. Governance and External Engagement Maintain and support effective departmental governance processes. Communicate clearly and effectively with faculty, staff, students, college leadership, and other stakeholders. Represent and advocate for the department within the university and to external constituencies. Build and strengthen relationships with alumni, industry leaders, professional organizations, public agencies, and other partners. Promote the department's strengths, accomplishments, and impact at local, state, national, and international levels. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position . Required Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in Economics, Agricultural Economics, or a closely related discipline. Established record of scholarship, teaching, and service sufficient to qualify for appointment with tenure at the rank of Professor at Iowa State University.   Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated leadership experience in an academic, research, administrative, or organizational setting. Strategic planning and organizational leadership. Budget and fiscal management. Recruitment, development, evaluation, and retention of faculty and staff. Undergraduate and graduate program development and student success initiatives. Research leadership, including extramural funding and graduate student mentoring. Extension, outreach, policy engagement, or public scholarship. Building interdisciplinary collaborations and partnerships. Record of effectiveness in collaboration, communication, and relationship building. Working effectively with industry, government, nonprofit organizations, alumni, and other stakeholders. Leading organizations with multiple constituencies and complex administrative relationships. Working effectively within a system of shared governance and consultative academic decision-making.   Department/Program & College Description: The Department of Economics is one of Iowa State University's oldest and most distinguished academic units. The department is among a select group of economics departments nationally that combines agricultural economics and general economics within a single department. It is home to approximately 33 faculty members and 7 staff members and serves approximately ~450 undergraduate students and ~55 graduate. Faculty conduct nationally and internationally recognized research spanning several fields in economics, agricultural economics, and environmental and resource economics. Through its research, teaching, extension, and outreach programs, the department addresses critical economic challenges facing Iowa, the nation, and the world. The university is committed to continued investment in the department, including strategic investments in faculty and academic programs.   Department Unit/Website: https://www.econ.iastate.edu Proposed Start Date: July 1, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on \"Apply\" and complete the Employment Application. To guarantee full consideration, applications should be received by 12/05/2026 . All interested, qualified persons must apply for this position by submitted or attaching the following: 1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of interest and Statement of Purpose 3) Names and contact information for at least three professional references. References may be contacted to provide letters of recommendation and/or participate in a reference conversation via phone. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: October 19, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20103 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Graphic-Design-Assistant-II_R20091": {
      "title": "Graphic Design Assistant II",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Graphic Design Assistant II Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent and 2 years of related experience Job Description: Printing Services is seeking a Prepress & Print Design Technician II (Graphic Design Assistant II) to join our creative, fast-paced printing environment. This position combines graphic design, prepress, variable-data production, department marketing, and webstore support, including the development of dynamic product templates for online ordering. You’ll work on a wide variety of print, wide-format, mailing, and creative projects from concept through production. Working within established workflows and guidelines, you’ll independently resolve prepress issues and collaborate with customers, customer relations staff, and production teams to ensure files are accurate, consistent, and properly prepared for efficient downstream production. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in a printing services environment Experience working in a higher education environment Experience with print prepress software for digital and wide-format print production Experience with promotional and marketing materials Experience with mail list processing and variable-data printing workflows Experience with web-to-print, online ordering, or digital storefront platforms for print services About the Department: Do you enjoy a dynamic work environment where every day brings new projects and technical challenges? Are you interested in hands on work that supports meaningful communication across a large and diverse campus community? Printing Services at Iowa State University plays a critical role in supporting the university’s academic, research, and outreach missions by providing high quality print and design services. The department’s mission is to efficiently meet Iowa State’s core printing needs while delivering reliable, cost effective solutions with prompt turnaround times and top quality results. Printing Services combines technical expertise in prepress, production, and finishing with a strong focus on accuracy, accessibility, and consistency. As part of an integrated communications workflow, the department supports emerging digital print solutions, helping translate the knowledge and messaging of Iowa State University into effective visual communications for campus partners and the broader Iowa community. Team members work closely with production staff, customer-facing colleagues, and clients across campus in a collaborative, service oriented environment where precision, problem solving, and continuous improvement are valued. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Please Note: To receive full consideration, applications should be received by October 25, 2026. Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS806 Original Posting Date: October 16, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20091 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Assistant-Professor---Environmental-Engineering_R20069": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Environmental Engineering",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor - Environmental Engineering Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Civil, Construction and Environmental Engineering (CCEE) at Iowa State University (ISU) seeks candidates for a tenure-track assistant professor faculty position in environmental engineering. Applications from candidates in all areas of environmental engineering are welcome, but areas of particular interest include novel materials for environmental applications, One Health applications to environmental engineering, resource recovery, and air pollution. The successful candidate will establish and sustain an externally funded research program and complement the current research and education efforts in the CCEE Department through interdisciplinary collaboration. The candidate will teach courses at both the undergraduate and graduate levels, mentor both graduate and undergraduate students, generate a scholarly publication record, participate in technical committees and outreach activities, and exhibit a commitment to the ISU Principles of Community. Candidates should communicate well, collaborate effectively, and contribute to the mission of the department. We especially welcome candidates that can contribute to the department's ABET-accredited Environmental Engineering B.S. program. For more information about out department's engineering program, see www.ccee.iastate.edu .   Required Minimum Qualifications: Candidates for this position must hold a Ph.D. in civil engineering, environmental engineering or a closely related field. The Ph.D. must be conferred by the employment start date.   Preferred Qualifications: Agenda of research that compliments existing strengths in the department and University. Agenda of teaching that contributes to the department's degree programs, especially Environmental Engineering. A strong record of peer-reviewed publications in related technical areas. A professional engineering license or the ability to become licensed. Professional experience (e.g., academic, postdoctoral, industry) in a related field   Department/Program & College Description: The CCEE Department offers B.S. degree programs in civil engineering, civil engineering with environmental emphasis, construction engineering, and environmental engineering, plus M.S., MEng, and Ph.D. graduate degree programs in civil engineering and maintains externally funded research of more than $21 million annually. CCEE is committed to faculty, staff and students who can enrich University objectives in the areas of research, teaching, and service. Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: Applications will begin to be reviewed on November 15, 2026 with full consideration given to applications received by that date. The posting will remain open until the position is filled. All interested, qualified people must apply for this position online at jobs.iastate.edu . Please be prepared to attach the following: 1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of Application/Cover Letter 3) Contact Information for Three References 4) Other Documents: Research Statement (up to 2 pages) Teaching Statement (up to 2 pages) Please direct questions regarding the position to cceesearch@iastate.edu . If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: October 12, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20069 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Instruction-Librarian-I_R20070": {
      "title": "Instruction Librarian I",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Instruction Librarian I Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree Job Description: The Iowa State University Library invites applications for an Instruction Librarian I to join its Instruction Unit. This role will collaborate with the instruction team to coordinate and teach the undergraduate information literacy course. As part of the Research and Instruction Department, the Instruction Unit also develops and delivers workshops and instructional sessions focused on information literacy, AI literacy, and research skills. The Instruction Librarian will also contribute to the development and delivery of these instructional initiatives.   The successful candidate will have a customer-service focus, be skilled in organization and time management, possess the ability to interact effectively with library staff and the university community, and work independently as well as collaboratively in a rapidly changing, team-based environment.   The Iowa State University Library is committed to supporting librarians through mentoring, training, and professional development opportunities that foster professional growth and success. The Instruction Librarian will be encouraged and supported in pursuing continued learning relevant to their role, as well as sharing their knowledge and expertise with colleagues at Iowa State University and the broader library community.   Example of Duties: Teaching the library’s credit bearing information literacy course for undergraduate students.  Work with the instruction team to centrally coordinate the course and manage student learning accommodations. Actively participate in development of content and learning materials for the information literacy course. Ensure digital accessibility of the course learning materials. Co-manage the course’s learning management system, Canvas. Coordinate library’s LibGuides system and provide support to librarians on using LibGuides. Participate in the development of guides, tutorials, and other learning modules that support AI literacy, information literacy, and research skills. Contribute to the ongoing evaluation of instruction programs, providing recommendations for improvement.   Preferred Qualifications: Experience teaching or providing information literacy instruction. Experience delivering reference and research services in an academic or research library. Experience using course management systems, such as Canvas. Experience using instructional technologies and content creation software. Knowledge of accessibility standards and practices for creating digitally accessible learning materials. This posting will be open until filled. However, to receive full consideration, please apply before October 30th, 2026. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS807 Original Posting Date: October 15, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20070 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
