    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Research-Assistant-Professor---Electrical-and-Computer-Engineering_R18719": {
      "title": "Research Assistant Professor - Electrical and Computer Engineering",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Research Assistant Professor - Electrical and Computer Engineering Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering ( ece.iastate.edu ), in the College of Engineering at Iowa State University, invites applications for the position of Research Assistant Professor.  This is a 3-year term research faculty position that holds responsibilities primarily contributing to the research mission of the department through scholarly impact and an externally funded research program in the areas of wireless and network systems.  Specifically, besides contributing to the research, education, and innovation projects led by the Center for Wireless, Communities and Innovation ( wici.iastate.edu ), the responsibilities include mentoring graduate and undergraduate students working on research and design projects. Term Faculty hold limited-term, full or part-time, renewable appointments that are not eligible for tenure, but have the potential to be reviewed for advancement into senior ranks.  Research faculty must secure extramural funding to fully support their research program and at least 80% but no more than 90% of their salary, with the remainder salary provided by the department. Successful candidates will have experience that demonstrates exceptional ability or potential to produce scholarship, compete for and secure funding from external sources, and the capability for long-term leadership in their research field.  They will also exhibit excellent communication skills. Required Minimum Qualifications: Ph. D. in Computer Engineering, Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, or equivalent. Preferred Qualifications: Research experience and quality publications in advanced wireless and network systems (e.g., safety-critical wireless, URLLC, Open RAN, 6G/NextG); Hands-on experience with cellular network platforms (e.g., O-RAN, srsRAN, OpenAirInterface, Aether/SD-RAN), edge/cloud computing platforms (e.g., Kubernetes, OpenStack), SDN, and/or VNF; Hands-on experience in designing, developing, deploying, and/or operating field-deployed wireless, network, and/or distributed systems; Hands-on experiences in edge/cloud systems management, virtual machines/containers, Linux systems administration, shell scripting, etc; Capability of building systems prototypes based on reference publications and/or open-source software; Knowledge of wireless systems, networked/distributed systems, operating systems, virtualization, systems and network security; Programming skills: Python, C, C++, Java, Web etc. Department/Program & College Description: The Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering at Iowa State University is home to 60 faculty and is associated with 11 research centers and institutes, for instance, the Center for Wireless, Community and Innovation (WiCI). The department boasts 20 IEEE Fellows, over $15.4M in research expenditures (FY20), and one of the largest ECpE enrollments in the nation. About Iowa State University and the Ames Community Iowa State University is classified as a Carnegie Foundation Doctoral/Research University-Extensive . More than 30,000 students are enrolled and are served by over 6,200 faculty and staff. The College of Engineering consists of eight departments with annual research expenditures exceeding $105 million. Iowa State University is located in Ames, IA , a progressive community of 66,000, located approximately 30 minutes north of Des Moines , one of the fastest-growing metro areas in the Midwest, and is beaming with community pride and accolades . Iowa State University and the College of Engineering are responsive to the needs of dual-career couples and are dedicated to work-life balance through an array of flexible work policies. Department Unit/Website:   For more information about our department’s engineering programs, go to www.ece.iastate.edu . Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2026 Proposed End Date or Length of Term: May 15, 2029 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. However, to receive full consideration, applications should be received by November 15th, 2026. All interested, qualified persons must apply for this position online at jobs.iastate.edu . The following documents are required to be submitted in PDF format: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter that briefly discusses how the candidate meets each of the preferred qualifications Contact information for at least three references, including name, mailing address, email address, phone number, and other pertinent information Research statement Inquiries regarding this position may be directed to Hongwei Zhang ( hongwei@iastate.edu ) or Sara K. Harris ( skharris@iastate.edu ). Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: March 4, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R18719 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Lecturer-in-Journalism-and-Mass-Communication_R20088": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Journalism and Mass Communication",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Lecturer in Journalism and Mass Communication Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: The Greenlee School of Journalism and Communication in the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences at Iowa State University seeks a lecturer to teach JLMC 2010: Reporting and Writing for the Mass Media. The successful candidate will teach two 3-credit sections of the course, required for majors in advertising, digital storytelling, journalism, public relations, and sports media. The course develops students’ skills in reporting, interviewing, research, writing, and Associated Press style.   Required Minimum Qualifications :   Master’s degree in related field. Two years of professional experience in advertising, public relations, journalism, or sports media.   Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated teaching excellence in higher education; Demonstrated ability to mentor students and/or emerging professionals; Additional professional experience beyond the required amount in advertising, journalism, public relations, or sports media.   Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position.   Department/Program & College Description : The Greenlee School of Journalism and Communication has a dynamic ACEJMC-accredited undergraduate program and a strong master’s program. The school has undergraduate majors in advertising, journalism and mass communication, public relations, and sports media and communication, as well as a new interdisciplinary major in digital storytelling. Additional information about the school is available at www.greenlee.iastate.edu.   Department Unit/Website :  www.greenlee.iastate.edu Proposed Start Date: January 1, 2027 Proposed End Date or Length of Term: May 15, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Part time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following:\n \n1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae \n2) Letter of Application/Cover Letter \n3) Contact Information for Three References \n\nIf you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485.\n\n Why Choose ISU? \n\nIowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as:\n• Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans\n• Generous leave plans\n• Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa)\n• Life insurance and long-term disability\n• Flexible Spending Accounts\n• Various voluntary benefits and discounts\n• Employee Assistance Program\n• Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: October 14, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 15, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20088 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Senior-Psychologist_R20064": {
      "title": "Senior Psychologist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Senior Psychologist Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Doctorate Degree from an American Psychological Association (APA) or Canadian Psychological Association (CPA) accredited program or certified equivalent in counseling or clinical psychology and 1 year of related experience, which may include a doctoral internship. Licensed as a psychologist. Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: Impact Student Well-Being in a Collaborative and Supportive Environment Are you looking to make a real difference in the lives of university students while working in a dynamic and team-oriented environment? Iowa State University’s Student Counseling Services (SCS) is seeking a skilled Senior Psychologist to provide essential mental health services to students. This is a unique opportunity to contribute to the personal and academic success of students through a variety of counseling, crisis intervention, and educational programs. Why Iowa State University and SCS? Team-Oriented, Collaborative Environment At ISU’s Student Counseling Services, we value teamwork and collaboration. Our staff works closely together to provide high-quality care for students. You will be part of a dedicated team of professionals, collaborating to offer counseling, crisis support, and outreach programming aimed at improving student well-being. Engaging and Varied Work Each day brings new opportunities to support students as they navigate their college experience. From individual and group therapy to managing crises, you’ll engage in meaningful work that helps students overcome challenges and meet their personal and academic goals. As part of a center with a robust training program, you’ll also have the opportunity to provide supervision and mentorship to trainees, contributing to the development of future professionals in the field. Excellent Work-Life Balance and Benefits We understand the importance of maintaining balance in life. Iowa State University is committed to creating a workplace where your professional responsibilities are balanced with your personal needs. The university offers a flexible, supportive environment, including access to a fantastic benefits package which includes wellness programs and generous vacation time, allowing you to recharge and maintain your well-being while helping others. What We Offer: Work/Life Balance: primarily a Monday-Friday, day hours position! Generous Vacation and Sick Leave – 24 vacation days, 18 sick days, and 11 paid holidays. Excellent Health Insurance Options – including dental and vision coverage. Paid Professional Development opportunities. Retirement Plans with Employer Contributions – choose from multiple plans to secure your future. Tuition Reimbursement and Professional Development Support – grow with us! Wellness Programs and Work-Life Resources – including mental health and counseling support. Key Responsibilities: Provide individual and group therapy within a brief treatment model. Conduct intake assessments and make recommendations for appropriate services. Deliver crisis intervention and manage urgent student needs. Provide presentations and outreach programming on mental health topics for students, staff, and faculty. Provide supervision to trainees. Maintain thorough documentation of client interactions and services. Take part in crisis coverage as part of a rotating staff schedule. Why You’ll Love Living in Ames Ames, Iowa, offers an outstanding quality of life. Known for its welcoming community, Ames is home to a vibrant blend of cultural, athletic, and social events, thanks in part to Iowa State University. Whether you're attending concerts, art exhibitions, or theater performances, there's always something happening. The city also hosts a wide variety of athletic events, from Cyclone football and basketball games to other university sports that bring the community together. Plus, Ames frequently offers festivals, farmers’ markets, and university-sponsored lectures and events, ensuring there’s something for everyone. In addition to the exciting local atmosphere, Ames provides an affordable cost of living and excellent schools, making it a great place to live and thrive. Plus, with Des Moines just 30 minutes away, you’ll have easy access to everything a larger city has to offer without sacrificing the charm and convenience of a smaller town. Special Requirements: Applicants must be licensed as a psychologist before their start date. Applicants must also obtain an Iowa psychologist license within six months of the start date. For more information about our services, visit: Iowa State University Student Counseling Services . This position serves at the pleasure of university administration and is exempt from certain P&S policies. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available. This posting will be open until filled. However, to receive full consideration, applications need to be submitted before November 4th, 2026. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. This position serves at the pleasure of university administration and is exempt from certain P&S policies. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS810 Original Posting Date: October 13, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20064 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Postdoc-Research-Associate---Veterinary-Field-Services_R19565": {
      "title": "Postdoc Research Associate – Veterinary Field Services",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Postdoc Research Associate – Veterinary Field Services Appointment Type: Post Doc/Trainee Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The position emphasizes training in food animal medicine, with a substantial focus on bovine health and production systems, including both beef and dairy cattle. The selected candidate will gain production medicine–based clinical experience and have opportunities to participate in applied research activities. The primary work will be with the Veterinary Field Services unit, with opportunities to collaborate with and gain additional clinical and diagnostic experience through the ISU Food Animal and Camelid Hospital and the ISU Veterinary Diagnostic Laboratory. This position is designed to support candidates pursuing board certification as a Beef Cattle Diplomate or Food Animal Diplomate through the American Board of Veterinary Practitioners (ABVP) and to provide advanced clinical, teaching, and research experience for careers in academia, food animal practice, and veterinary clinical scholarship. Responsibilities include active participation in ambulatory food animal care through ISU Veterinary Field Services; involvement in the clinical instruction of veterinary students within the professional DVM program; participation in applied research in food animal medicine; and development of observational research studies, such as case reports and case series, to support scholarly productivity and ABVP board certification. Required Minimum Qualifications: DVM or equivalent veterinary degree by the start date of employment. Possession of, or eligibility to obtain by the start date of employment, a State of Iowa veterinary license and Category II accreditation through the USDA National Veterinary Accreditation Program (NVAP). Possession of, or eligibility to obtain by the start date of employment, U.S. Drug Enforcement Administration (DEA) registration and State of Iowa controlled substance registration. Valid U.S. driver's license and ability to meet University requirements for authorization to operate University vehicles by the start date of employment. Preferred Qualifications: One year of clinical experience in a food animal veterinary practice or comparable clinical food animal setting. Demonstrated experience working effectively with herd managers, animal care providers, and/or students at various levels of training. Department/Program & College Description: The Iowa State University College of Veterinary Medicine Food Animal and Camelid Field Services provides on-farm services to livestock producers in the general Ames area. Equipped with four fully stocked mobile veterinary trucks and eight full-time clinicians, Veterinary Field Services provides individual animal and herd health veterinary care for beef, dairy, swine, sheep, goats, and camelids (alpacas and llamas). The Field Services unit serves to educate veterinary students on farm animal medicine while providing high-quality veterinary services to local producers. Our services provide students with additional hands-on training in best practices for management of a wide variety of clinical cases to help prepare them for their future veterinary careers. Department Unit/Website: Veterinary Field Services - Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. To be guaranteed consideration, applications must be received by October 22, 2026. This is a one-year term position with the possibility of renewal. The anticipated start date is July 1, 2027 . Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Proposed Start Date: July 1, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: Post Docs Original Posting Date: July 17, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19565 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Custodian-I_R20083": {
      "title": "Custodian I",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Custodian I Job Group: Merit Required Minimum Qualifications: • Ability to read, write, and follow instructions. Job Description: The Facilities Planning & Management Department is seeking applicants for full-time Custodian I positions. Under direct supervision, performs custodial work required for the general maintenance of buildings.  ABOUT THE DEPARTMENT:    Facilities Planning & Management (FP&M) is an organization that is dedicated to the maintenance and enhancement of Iowa State University, one of the nation’s leading educational and agricultural institutes. But more importantly, FP&M is dedicated to their employees and enhancing the lives of each team member through opportunities both professionally and personally. FP&M is one of the largest departments on campus and currently employs over 450 full-time employees and students combined.  Preferred Qualifications: At least 1 year of experience in custodial work or a related field  Experience operating commercial cleaning equipment such as floor scrubbers, vacuums, or buffers  Experience using a work order or work management systems Characteristic Duties and Responsibilities • Performs cleaning in all areas of a building. • Performs cleaning of all floor areas such as vacuuming, shampooing, sweeping, mopping, stripping, scrubbing, waxing, and buffing. • Cleans and polishes all bathroom fixtures. • Cleans and washes all glass surfaces, ceilings and walls. • The use of a ladder up to 12 feet in height may be required. • Replaces light bulbs and cleans light fixtures, using a ladder as required. • Makes beds and handles both clean and soiled linens. • Refills holder of disposable items, such as soap, bathroom tissue, paper towels, etc. Cleans and disinfects beds, bedside tables, overbed tables, etc., and other equipment and areas. • Reports breakage and needed repairs. • Moves furniture, supplies and miscellaneous equipment; removes draperies and rugs periodically for cleaning; delivers supplies to various areas. • Collects trash from receptacles throughout the building and empties it into various areas. • Performs duties in the immediate exterior of building such as sweeping sidewalks, snow and ice removal at entrances, cleaning ash pits, cleaning debris from grounds and window wells, and cleaning exterior windows. • Locks and unlocks doors as required. • Assists in unloading trucks, unpacking, assembling, and moving equipment and furniture. • Picks up and returns equipment for repair by maintenance. • Delivers housekeeping supplies to designated areas. • Operates high pressure, water-cleaning apparatus to clean and disinfect rug runners, hospital equipment and showers. • Maintains inventory of linen and record of lined laundering; maintains inventory of custodial supplies, and keeps and prepares other records and reports as directed. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities • Knowledge of standard cleaning techniques and characteristics of surfaces to be cleaned, and equipment and supplies required. • Ability to move furniture and objects in preparation for cleaning; to load and unload trash receptacles; to operate safely and properly care for power machinery; to use arm muscles in hand cleaning, mopping, and scrubbing for protracted periods of time; to work on ladders. • Knowledge of proper bending and lifting techniques and ability to lift and carry 50 pounds. • Ability to work in a variety of environments including crowded public areas and high and low temperature areas. • Knowledge of the safe use if chemical cleaning agents and possible hazards relating to environmental sanitation. • Ability to communicate effectively with others. • Ability to follow oral and written instructions. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: 0003a Original Posting Date: October 13, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 23, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20083 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Assistant-Professor-in-Seed-Pathology_R19814": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Seed Pathology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor in Seed Pathology Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Plant Pathology, Entomology and Microbiology and the Seed Science Center in the College of Agriculture and Life Sciences at Iowa State University invite applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor in the area of seed pathology. We seek candidates with broad expertise in seed pathology whose research will support the development of state-of-the-art diagnostic tools that facilitate the detection of seedborne pathogens with particular emphasis on viruses, bacteria, and fungi. Candidates whose expertise encompasses the use of high-throughput sequencing and associated computational pipelines are of particular interest. The position is 65% research, 30% teaching, and 5% service. The successful candidate is expected to develop an externally funded, high-impact research program that engages students in the broad areas of plant pathology, seed pathology and bioinformatics while also participating in service to the university. ISU has extensive shared facilities for biological research, including -omics technology for genetics, genomics and microbiome studies and high-performance computing. The collaborative environment is enhanced by interdisciplinary and disciplinary graduate majors that promote cross-fertilization within labs. The successful candidate will have an office and laboratory in the Seed Science Building, which houses the Seed Science Center. The Seed Science Center is a globally recognized hub of excellence in seed testing, research, education, systems, and international programs. It is a leader in developing science to inform policy to benefit the world seed trade. The Center is home to the Seed Lab, one of the largest public testing laboratories in the U.S. that has provided accurate and professional seed testing services to growers and the seed industry for more than 130 years. The Department of Plant Pathology, Entomology and Microbiology serves as home to the ISU Plant and Insect Diagnostic Clinic, has access to numerous field research facilities, and administers a vibrant and experiential undergraduate microbiology program. Faculty have strengths in extension, teaching, and the scholarship of teaching and learning, and research across the full spectrum from fundamental to applied.   Required Minimum Qualifications: Candidates must have a Ph.D. in Plath Pathology, Plant Science or a closely related field with experience in the broad area of seed pathology   Preferred Qualifications: Evidence of strong potential for conducting innovative research in seed pathology that includes the development of diagnostic tests for pathogens Evidence for the use of high-throughput sequencing and associated computational pipelines Evidence of a strong publication record in internationally recognized journals Evidence of strong potential for research mentoring Evidence of strong potential for collaborative research Evidence of strong potential for securing extramural funding Evidence of strong potential for evidence-based, innovative teaching  Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on \"Apply\" and complete the Employment Application. The application should include: 1) Cover Letter describing the qualifications for the position (2 pages max) 2) Curriculum Vitae 3) Research Statement detailing experience and future plans (3 pages max) 4) Teaching Statement detailing philosophy, experience, and future plans (2 pages max) 5) Names and contact information for three references For guaranteed consideration, applications should be received by January 4th, 2027. Questions regarding this position should be directed to the Chair of the Search Committee, Scott Heuchelin ( scotth3@iastate.edu ), or the Chair of the Department of Plant Pathology, Entomology and Microbiology, Steven Harris ( stevenh1@iastate.edu ). Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: August 21, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R19814 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Assistant-Professor--Technology---Urban-Analytics-and-Planning_R20075": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor: Technology - Urban Analytics and Planning",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor: Technology - Urban Analytics and Planning Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Urban Planning and Development (UPD) in the College of Design at Iowa State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in technology, urban analytics and planning. We seek a scholar and educator whose research and teaching connect data and emerging technologies to contemporary urban and regional issues. The successful candidate will strengthen the department’s capacity in planning methods while developing a forward-looking research agenda that explores how emerging technologies can enhance the ways planners understand, analyze, visualize, and shape places. This work should demonstrate careful attention to the ethical and responsible use of data and technology in planning research and practice. Areas of Interest This position provides an opportunity to strengthen and modernize core departmental capacity in planning methods while building new strength in AI, urban analytics, visualization, and using technology in planning. Areas of research and teaching interest may include: urban analytics and data-driven planning, artificial intelligence and emerging technologies in planning, PlanTech and digital planning tools, quantitative planning methods, data visualization and geovisualization, emerging issues in technology and planning, and ethical and responsible applications of AI and data in planning. The position is intended to connect analytical and technological innovation with planning practice. Position Responsibilities The successful candidate will be expected to: Develop and maintain a nationally recognized program of research and scholarship, including pursuing external funding appropriate to the defined research agenda. Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in planning methods, urban analytics, technology in planning, and/or related areas. Contribute to other planning courses, studios, and other departmental curricular needs. Integrate emerging technologies and contemporary analytical methods into planning education. Mentor undergraduate and graduate students and serve on graduate thesis committees. Collaborate with faculty across the College of Design, ISU Extension and other units at Iowa State University. Contribute to departmental, college, university, and professional service.   In addition, faculty in UPD have an opportunity to work with ISU Extension and Outreach, Community and Economic Development, during the summer. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Required Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. degree in urban and regional planning, community and regional planning, geography, urban studies, or a closely related field by the time of appointment.   Preferred Qualifications: Evidence of potential for effective undergraduate and graduate teaching. Research and teaching expertise in two or more of the following: urban analytics, AI and emerging planning technologies, quantitative methods, and data visualization. Evidence of potential to develop a strong program of research and scholarship and secure external research funding. Experience with interdisciplinary, applied, or community-engaged research. Experience integrating emerging technologies into teaching and/or professional planning practice.   Department/Program & College Description: About Department of Urban Planning and Development The Department of Urban Planning and Development (UPD) at Iowa State University prepares students to address the complex challenges facing cities, towns, and regions. Through teaching, research, and community engagement, UPD faculty focus on areas such as land-use planning, housing, transportation, community and economic development, environmental resilience, local governance and planning technologies, with a strong emphasis on applying planning knowledge to real-world community needs. Please visit the departmental website for more information: https://www.design.iastate.edu/academics/departments/upd/ Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: The guaranteed consideration date is December 15, 2026 and application reviews will continue until the position is filled. The anticipated start date is August 16, 2027 . Candidates should submit: 1) Letter of application describing their interest in the position and alignment with research and teaching responsibilities. 2) Curriculum vitae. 3) Research statement describing current scholarships, future research and funding agenda. 4) Teaching statement describing teaching philosophy. 5) Contact information for three professional references. Questions about the position may be directed to Dr. Carlton Basmajian , Search Committee Chair, at carlton@iastate.edu . Questions about the application process may be directed to employment@iastate.edu or 515-294-4800. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: October 9, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20075 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Violence-Prevention-Specialist_R20032": {
      "title": "Violence Prevention Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Violence Prevention Specialist Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 3 years of related experience Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: Are you passionate about creating a holistic student experience that supports mental, physical, and emotional wellbeing? Are you interested in an opportunity where you get to engage with students and help them reach their full potential—academically and beyond? If so, Student Wellness with the Division of Student Affairs at Iowa State University is currently seeking applicants for a Violence Prevention Specialist. This individual plays a key role in advancing student health and wellbeing through strategic communication, data-informed storytelling, and health promotion initiatives. This position will be hired as a Wellness Program Specialist II. This position will focus on violence prevention education and outreach. This position includes work in areas such as sexual violence, stalking, and hazing. What You’ll Do: Develop, implement, and evaluate violence prevention and health promotion programs, initiatives, and educational campaigns Plan, facilitate, and assess trainings, workshops, presentations, and outreach efforts focused on violence prevention, consent education, bystander intervention, and student wellbeing Coordinate and support campus-wide prevention initiatives, awareness campaigns, events, and programs that foster a safe and healthy campus community Build and maintain collaborative partnerships with campus departments, student groups, community organizations, and external stakeholders to advance prevention efforts Support the implementation, assessment, and continuous improvement of university violence prevention strategies, programs, and strategic priorities Recruit, train, supervise, and support peer educators and student leaders engaged in prevention education and outreach activities Develop and disseminate educational materials, resources, digital content, and marketing strategies to increase awareness, engagement, and access to support services Collect, analyze, and report program data and assessment outcomes to measure effectiveness, demonstrate impact, and inform continuous improvement Serve on university and community committees, workgroups, and collaborative initiatives that support prevention, safety, and wellbeing goals Occasional weekend/evening hours will be involved in this role. Preferred Qualifications: Specialized training or coursework in violence prevention, sexual assault prevention, healthy relationships, etc. Certification in bystander intervention, violence prevention, trauma-informed practices, or similar prevention-focused approaches. Experience facilitating workshops, presentations and health promotion training. Experience coordinating, facilitating, and training teams; preferably focused on prevention education and outreach efforts. Experience using tools such as Smartsheet and/or Qualtrics. Department Description: Student Wellness at Iowa State University provides leadership in university strategy for health promotion and provides support programs aimed at creating a campus culture of wellbeing so that all students can thrive. Student Wellness plans, implements, and evaluates health education and prevention strategies that focus on health and wellness issues that directly affect student success, higher learning, and personal development such as: violence prevention, suicide, mental health, substance use, and more. To learn more, please visit Student Wellness . This posting will be open until filled. However, to receive full consideration, applications need to be submitted before October 23rd, 2026. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS807 Original Posting Date: October 9, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20032 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Clinical-Track-or-Tenure-Track---Assistant-Associate-Full-Professor---Anatomic-Pathology_R20034": {
      "title": "Clinical Track or Tenure Track - Assistant/Associate/Full Professor - Anatomic Pathology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-08\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Clinical Track or Tenure Track - Assistant/Associate/Full Professor - Anatomic Pathology Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Veterinary Pathology in the College of Veterinary Medicine at Iowa State University (ISU) invites applications for a full-time, clinical-track or tenure-track faculty position in Anatomic Pathology at the Assistant, Associate, or Professor level. Appointment rank and track will be based on the selected candidate’s qualifications, documented experience, and interests.  The successful candidate will join 6 ACVP Anatomic Pathologists, 3 ACVP Clinical Pathologists, 2 ACVM Veterinary Parasitologists and 1 specialist in medical education assessment.  This position has a primary commitment to teaching and professional practice. This position is devoted primarily to teaching and professional practice, with a limited portion of effort allocated to research and scholarly activities. The specific distribution of responsibilities will be established with the department chair based on departmental needs, appointment track, and the successful candidate’s qualifications and interests. The successful candidate will participate in the department’s surgical biopsy and necropsy services. The biopsy service receives submissions from the ISU Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center (LVMC) and practicing veterinarians in the surrounding region. The necropsy service evaluates diverse species submitted through the LVMC small and large animal clinics. Responsibilities include diagnostic interpretation and communication of findings to clinicians and referring veterinarians, with an emphasis on accurate, timely, and clinically useful reports. Teaching responsibilities include instruction of senior veterinary students and pathology residents through diagnostic service, including necropsy techniques, lesion recognition and interpretation, and clinicopathologic correlation. The successful candidate will also contribute to didactic and laboratory instruction in anatomic pathology and related disciplines for undergraduate, professional (DVM), and graduate students, as assigned, and participate in resident training and mentorship. The successful candidate will advance anatomic pathology through scholarship appropriate to the appointment track and assigned effort. Clinical-track scholarship may include case reports, case series, educational scholarship, and collaborative research. Tenure-track faculty are expected to contribute anatomic pathology expertise to research collaborations resulting in peer-reviewed publications. Scholarly expectations will be consistent with the position’s substantial teaching and professional practice commitment. The successful candidate will demonstrate a collegial and collaborative approach, effective communication with learners and veterinary colleagues, and commitment to student education. All faculty are expected to uphold high standards of integrity and ethics, contribute to a positive work environment, and approach clients and patients with professionalism and compassion. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position.   Required Minimum Qualifications: DVM or equivalent degree. Board certification in anatomic pathology through the American College of Veterinary Pathologists (ACVP), European College of Veterinary Pathologists (ECVP), or Japanese College of Veterinary Pathologists (JCVP). In addition to the requirements above, the following minimum qualifications apply by rank and track: Clinical Associate Professor. A graduate degree; Diplomate status in anatomic pathology in the ACVP, ECVP, or JCVP; and a minimum of five years of professional practice experience emphasizing companion animal, production animal, and equine pathology. Clinical Professor . A graduate degree; and a minimum of ten years of professional practice experience emphasizing companion animal, production animal and equine pathology.   Assistant Professor on the tenure track. A PhD.   Associate Professor on the tenure track. A PhD; a minimum of five years of professional practice experience emphasizing companion animal, production animal, and equine pathology; a record of scholarship and teaching; and experience with resident training. Professor . A PhD; and a minimum of ten years of professional practice experience emphasizing companion animal, production animal and equine pathology; a record of scholarship and teaching; and experience with resident training. Candidates for appointment at the Associate Professor and Professor level must demonstrate accomplishments in scholarship, teaching, and clinical service appropriate to the rank and appointment track.   Preferred Qualifications: Experience in diagnostic anatomic pathology, including biopsy and necropsy services involving companion animals, production animals, and horses. Experience teaching anatomic pathology in didactic, laboratory, or clinical settings. Research experience demonstrated through publications, grants, or graduate student mentorship. An MS, PhD, or equivalent graduate degree in veterinary pathology, microbiology, virology, education, or a related veterinary field, where not already required for the appointment rank.   Department/Program & College Description: The Department of Veterinary Pathology contributes to the teaching, professional practice, and research missions of the ISU College of Veterinary Medicine. Its diagnostic services support patient care through the Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center and provide opportunities for instruction of veterinary students and pathology residents. Departmental research areas include animal models of human disease, infectious diseases, carcinogenesis, toxicology, host-pathogen interactions, parasitology, educational scholarship, and comparative pathology.   The Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center provides specialized care and comprehensive medical and surgical services for companion and large animals from Iowa and surrounding states. Clinicians, residents, interns, technicians, staff, and veterinary students work collaboratively in patient care and clinical education. As the nation’s first public veterinary school, Iowa State University’s College of Veterinary Medicine has a longstanding commitment to veterinary professional practice, education, research, and service. The college works to improve the health and well-being of animals and people. Iowa State University is located in Ames, Iowa, approximately 30 minutes north of Des Moines.   Department Unit/Website: Department of Veterinary Pathology: https://vetmed.iastate.edu/vpath/ College of Veterinary Medicine: https://vetmed.iastate.edu/ Proposed Start Date: January 1, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of application addressing the required and preferred qualifications and including a statement of teaching. 3) Contact Information for Three Professional References If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. For full guaranteed consideration, please apply on or before November 08, 2026. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: October 8, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20034 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Tenure-Track-Assistant-Professor-GDCB_R20038": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Assistant Professor GDCB",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-08\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Tenure-Track Assistant Professor GDCB Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Genetics, Development and Cell Biology (GDCB) at Iowa State University seeks to hire an assistant professor to start in August 2027. The faculty member should use model organisms such as zebrafish, Drosophila and/or human cell and organoid systems to investigate the molecular mechanisms underlying the cell and developmental biology of human health and disease . Areas of interest include, but are not limited to, developmental and cell biology, cancer biology, neurobiology, stem cell biology, and related fields. Research interests that integrate modern experimental biology, including genome engineering and single cell biology, with emerging computational approaches such as artificial intelligence (AI) will be given priority. The new faculty member will also contribute to undergraduate and graduate education by teaching Biology, Genetics, or Integrated Health Sciences courses and/or developing new offerings in their area of interest that integrates AI, quantitative biology, and modern biomedical research. Required Minimum Qualifications: PhD or equivalent in biological sciences before August 16, 2027   Preferred Qualifications: Research experience aligned with position description Well-developed research plan Postdoctoral training with evidence of independent research Strong supporting publications Potential to secure external funding Potential for excellence in teaching and mentoring   Department/Program & College Description: The Department of Genetics, Development, and Cell Biology (GDCB) at Iowa State University advances life sciences through innovative research, personalized education, and interdisciplinary collaboration. We investigate the genetic, molecular and cellular foundations of life to prepare the next generation of leaders and professionals to address global challenges in biotechnology, medicine, health, food security, and sustainable agriculture. Our dynamic programs bridge scientific discovery with real-world impact, empowering all students to shape a healthier and more resilient future.   Department Unit/Website: https://www.gdcb.iastate.edu/ Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1. Cover letter 2. Curriculum Vitae (CV) 3. Research plan (no more than 3 pages) 4. Teaching statement and/or interests (1 page) 5. Names and contact information of 3-5 references If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. For full guaranteed consideration, please apply on or before December 01, 2026. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: October 8, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20038 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
