    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Assistant-Professor-of-Criminal-Justice_R20044": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Sociology and Criminal Justice in the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences at Iowa State University in Ames, Iowa invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Criminal Justice, as a 9-month position, starting August 16, 2027. The Department is particularly interested in candidates with research and/or teaching experience in the area of emerging technologies in criminal justice (e.g., artificial intelligence, digital forensics, surveillance, etc.), especially as used in policing and courts.   The successful candidate will have a strong research portfolio and demonstrated commitment to excellence in teaching. Responsibilities include teaching undergraduate and graduate criminal justice courses, with modalities as determined by the department (in-person, hybrid, or online); developing and maintaining an excellent, nationally recognized research program; contributing service to the department and the broader discipline; and pursuing external research funding.   Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position.     Required Minimum Qualifications: PhD in Criminology/Criminal Justice or a closely related discipline by the appointment start date   Preferred Qualifications: Evidence of high quality, peer-reviewed publications in criminology/criminal justice Expertise in the area of emerging technologies in criminal justice (e.g., artificial intelligence, digital forensics, surveillance, etc.). Record of highly effective undergraduate teaching in criminal justice, supported by student/peer evaluations and/or applicant statement of teaching philosophy Potential to secure external funding from federal/state agencies, private sector, and/or foundations   Department/Program & College Description: The Department’s ( http://www.soc-cj.iastate.edu/ ) current and future research, teaching, and extension scholarship is centered on creating new knowledge and preparing the next generation of scientists, teachers, professionals, and citizens to apply social science skills to societal challenges. The Department has a pedagogical mission to prepare undergraduate and graduate students with skills to launch professional careers that address the major challenges of society and engage in civic life as well-educated global citizens. The Criminal Justice program enrolls more than 400 majors and minors.    Department Unit/Website: http://www.soc-cj.iastate.edu/ Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of Application/Cover Letter that briefly discusses how the applicant aligns with each of the preferred qualifications, especially a substantive focus on emerging technologies in criminal justice; specific sections should address research (e.g., research interests and publication experience, potential for grant-funding including trainings and/or experience with previous funded projects) and teaching in criminal justice (e.g., supported by student/peer evaluations and/or applicant statement of teaching philosophy) 3) Contact Information for Three References If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. For full guaranteed consideration, please apply on or before November 1, 2026. This position is open untill filled. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: October 6, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20044 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-of-Kinesiology-and-Health_R20016": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Kinesiology and Health",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant or Associate Professor of Kinesiology and Health Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: The Department of Kinesiology and Health at Iowa State University invites applications for a tenure-track or tenured faculty position at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor, beginning August 16, 2027 . This open search welcomes applicants from any area of kinesiology and health. We seek an outstanding scholar whose research complements and extends our strengths, expands externally funded research through diverse sources, develops partnerships with industry, healthcare, or community organizations, and advances Iowa State's land-grant mission by improving health and well-being in Iowa and beyond. Candidates at the Associate Professor rank will also have opportunities to mentor early-career faculty and contribute to department leadership. The initial contract period is for up to four years with the possibility of renewal. About the Department The Department of Kinesiology and Health is one of five units in the College of Health and Human Sciences. The Department is committed to advancing the science of physical activity, human movement, and health through innovative and impactful research. Faculty maintain active research programs in exercise physiology, exercise psychology, biomechanics, neuromotor control, and physical activity and health, with departmental strengths in healthy aging, cardiovascular and brain health, skeletal muscle and space biology, immunology, occupational biomechanics, rural health, digital health, and translational intervention research across the lifespan. Studies range from cellular and molecular research to randomized controlled trials, and from community-based research to dissemination and implementation science, addressing critical questions related to health, performance, and quality of life. Indirect cost revenue from externally funded research is returned directly to principal investigators at a competitive rate. Undergraduate programs: More than 1,100 undergraduate majors, ranking in the top three for undergraduate enrollment among Iowa State's 61 academic departments. The BS in Kinesiology and Health offers options in Community and Public Health, Exercise Science, Physical Activity and Health Promotion, Physical Education Teacher Education, and Pre-Health Professions, with minors in Dance, Exercise Science, Health Promotion, and Kinesiology and Health. Graduate programs: More than 80 graduate students, with enrollment nearly doubling in recent years. Programs include the MS and PhD in Kinesiology, Master's in Athletic Training, and online Master's in Digital Health. Undergraduate research: Strong demand for research mentorship, with most students pursuing pre-health careers. Of student researchers surveyed, 86% rate their lab experience as very or extremely impactful. People and culture: The department includes 42 faculty and staff, including 13 tenure-track and tenured faculty, 17 term faculty, and 12 professional and scientific staff. A 2026 external program review recognized our collegial culture as a key strength. Facilities: The department’s 90,000-square-foot facility includes the Exercise Clinic, 15 research laboratories, and 5 teaching laboratories, with shared DEXA, cardiovascular, metabolic, and strength assessment spaces. Collaboration: Interdisciplinary teams connect department strengths with partners across campus, including the ISU Translational Research Network (U-TuRN), ISU Extension and Outreach serving all 99 Iowa counties, the Nanovaccine Institute, Center for Industrial Research and Service, Virtual Reality Applications Center, ISU Athletics, the Colleges of Veterinary Medicine and Engineering, as well as healthcare, industry, and community partners across Iowa. The successful applicant for this position will: Establish or sustain an externally funded research program drawing on federal, foundation, industry, or other sources Publish in respected peer-reviewed journals Build partnerships that expand research, funding, and student opportunities, and share research findings with practitioners and the public Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in the area of expertise Mentor graduate students and engage undergraduates in research Provide service to the department, college, university, and profession   Required Minimum Qualifications : Earned doctorate in Kinesiology or a related field by the start date Assistant Professor rank: A record of peer-reviewed publications and evidence of a research program with strong potential for external funding Associate Professor rank: A sustained record of peer-reviewed publications, extramural funding, and a nationally recognized research program sufficient to qualify for tenure at the rank of Associate Professor Preferred Qualifications :  Research that complements or extends one or more department research strengths Record of seeking funding from diverse sources, such as federal agencies, foundations, industry, or state and community partners Postdoctoral experience Experience building partnerships or translating research into practice Record of interdisciplinary collaboration Collegiate teaching and graduate mentoring experience Leadership experience in research, professional, or academic settings Department Unit/Website: https://kin.hs.iastate.edu/ Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Cover letter (up to 2 pages) addressing the required and preferred qualifications 2) Curriculum vitae 3) Research statement (2 to 3 pages) describing how your research complements and extends the department's research strengths, and your plan for external funding 4) Contact information for three professional references   For guaranteed consideration, please submit your application materials by November 9, 2026 . This position will remain open until filled.   Questions about the position may be directed to Dr. Elizabeth Stegemöller , Search Committee Chair, at esteg@iastate.edu.   Questions about the application process may be directed to employment@iastate.edu or 515-294-4800. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: October 2, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20016 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Postdoctoral-Research-Associate---Ovarian-Biology-and-Toxicology_R20036": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate - Ovarian Biology and Toxicology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Postdoctoral Research Associate - Ovarian Biology and Toxicology Appointment Type: Post Doc/Trainee Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Postdoctoral Research Associate will contribute to a collaborative research program focused on understanding the molecular and phenotypic ovarian responses to PFAS exposure. The successful candidate will conduct animal exposure studies, perform ex vivo ovary culture experiments, and collect phenotypic and biochemical data. Responsibilities include molecular analyses, ovarian follicle assessment, steroid hormone quantification, experimental design, data analysis, manuscript preparation, and training and mentoring graduate students. The position also includes maintaining detailed research records, managing laboratory sample inventories, and supporting a collaborative research environment. Required Minimum Qualifications: PhD in Reproductive Biology, Toxicology or related field.  Preferred Qualifications: Experience in ovarian biology, female reproductive biology, and/or toxicology. Experience with animal handling, exposure studies, and biological data collection. Experience performing molecular laboratory analyses, including western blotting and immunofluorescent staining. Experience with histology, ovarian follicle counting, and/or ex vivo ovary culture. Experience with statistical analysis and coding in Python or R, bioinformatic analyses, and/or proteomic analyses.     Department/Program & College Description: Our commitment is to educate and prepare students for productive and gratifying careers in animal production, veterinary medicine and the diverse areas of animal business and industry. Instruction, research and outreach programs are led by 46 faculty , many of whom are internationally recognized, with expertise in breeding and genetics, genomics, nutrition, physiology, meat science and meat processing, animal well-being and management. These programs and disciplinary focus areas include beef cattle, dairy cattle, horses, poultry, swine, sheep, companion animals, laboratory animals and zoo animals. Department Unit/Website: Department of Animal Science Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Proposed Start Date: November 16, 2026 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: Post Docs Original Posting Date: October 6, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 6, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20036 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Postdoctoral-Research-Associate---PFAS-Analytical-Chemistry_R20035": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate - PFAS Analytical Chemistry",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Postdoctoral Research Associate - PFAS Analytical Chemistry Appointment Type: Post Doc/Trainee Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Postdoctoral Research Associate will contribute to a collaborative, multidisciplinary research program focused on understanding the molecular and phenotypic ovarian responses to PFAS exposure. The successful candidate will conduct animal exposure studies, perform molecular and analytical laboratory techniques, and support the collection, analysis, and interpretation of research data. Responsibilities include PFAS quantification using HPLC-MS/MS and LC-MS/MS, molecular analyses, steroid hormone quantification, experimental design, and manuscript preparation. The position also includes maintaining detailed research records, managing laboratory sample inventories, and training and mentoring graduate students in a collaborative research environment. Required Minimum Qualifications: PhD in Reproductive Biology, Toxicology or related field.  Preferred Qualifications: Experience in analytical chemistry, including HPLC-MS/MS, LC-MS/MS, and chemical extraction techniques. Experience in PFAS research and/or toxicology. Experience with animal handling, exposure studies, and biological data collection. Experience with molecular laboratory analyses, including western blotting and immunofluorescent staining. Experience with statistical analysis and coding in Python or R. Department/Program & College Description: Our commitment is to educate and prepare students for productive and gratifying careers in animal production, veterinary medicine and the diverse areas of animal business and industry. Instruction, research and outreach programs are led by 46 faculty , many of whom are internationally recognized, with expertise in breeding and genetics, genomics, nutrition, physiology, meat science and meat processing, animal well-being and management. These programs and disciplinary focus areas include beef cattle, dairy cattle, horses, poultry, swine, sheep, companion animals, laboratory animals and zoo animals. Department Unit/Website: Department of Animal Science Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Proposed Start Date: November 16, 2026 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: Post Docs Original Posting Date: October 6, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 6, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20035 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
