    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Student-Recruiter-III_R20175": {
      "title": "Student Recruiter III",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-05\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Student Recruiter III Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 5 years of related experience Job Description: Help shape the graduate student experience at Iowa State University by connecting prospective students with opportunities to advance their education and achieve their goals. The Office of Admissions is seeking a collaborative, student-focused Student Recruiter III to lead graduate recruitment initiatives, develop strategic outreach efforts, and support a team dedicated to helping prospective graduate students navigate their path to Iowa State. In this role, you'll work closely with the Graduate College, academic programs, and campus partners to strengthen recruitment strategies, expand engagement with domestic and international students, and create meaningful experiences from initial inquiry through enrollment. The ideal candidate will bring strong leadership, communication, relationship-building, and organizational skills, along with the ability to use data and innovative approaches to improve recruitment outcomes. Key Responsibilitie s Graduate Recruitment Strategy: Collaborate with the supervisor to support the development, implementation, and evaluation of graduate recruitment strategies, including those for on-campus, online, and hybrid non-thesis master’s programs. Supervise and Develop Staff: Provide leadership and direction to recruitment staff through coaching, mentoring, performance management, employee development, and team engagement. Manage Recruitment Outreach: Oversee an assigned recruitment territory or prospect population, coordinate outreach efforts, and guide team strategies to engage prospective students from initial inquiry through enrollment. Support Prospective Graduate Students: Provide guidance on graduate programs, application requirements, admission decisions, enrollment processes, and available resources. Assist with complex inquiries and provide guidance to recruitment staff. Coordinate Recruitment Events and Visits: Lead the planning and execution of graduate recruitment events, campus and virtual visits, information sessions, and yield activities. Deliver presentations to prospective students and other audiences. Build Campus and External Partnerships: Develop and maintain relationships with the Graduate College, academic departments, scholarship representatives, international student services, educational institutions, and external recruitment partners. Lead Recruitment Communications: Develop and coordinate targeted recruitment campaigns, Salesforce Journeys, and follow-up strategies to strengthen prospective student engagement and support enrollment goals. Use Data to Drive Decisions: Analyze recruitment trends, develop dashboards, evaluate outreach effectiveness, and use enrollment data and student feedback to identify opportunities for improvement. Support Recruitment Travel and Budget Planning: Coordinate domestic and international recruitment activities, oversee team travel and event coverage, monitor recruitment spending, and evaluate recruitment outcomes. Improve Recruitment Operations: Provide guidance on recruitment systems, staff training, communication practices, and process improvements to ensure consistent, responsive, and effective service to prospective students. This position includes occasional evening and weekend commitments, as well as domestic and international travel to support recruitment activities, events, and professional development opportunities. About the Office of Admissions The Office of Admissions at Iowa State University plays an important role in welcoming future Cyclones and helping students discover the academic opportunities, resources, and experiences available at Iowa State. Through personalized outreach, recruitment events, campus visits, and partnerships across the university, the team supports prospective students throughout the admissions and enrollment journey. Working collaboratively with academic colleges, the Graduate College, and campus partners, the Office of Admissions is committed to providing a welcoming, informative, and supportive experience for students from a wide range of backgrounds and educational goals. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in higher education graduate student recruitment. Experience engaging with domestic and international student populations or supporting recruitment initiatives across different geographic markets. Experience supervising, coaching, mentoring, or providing leadership and direction to staff or teams. Experience building and maintaining collaborative relationships with academic programs, campus partners, external organizations, or other stakeholders. Experience using customer relationship management (CRM) systems, such as Salesforce, to manage prospective student engagement, communication campaigns, and follow-up activities. Experience analyzing recruitment, enrollment, or outreach data to evaluate outcomes, identify trends, and guide strategic decisions. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS809 Original Posting Date: November 5, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 26, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20175 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Facilities-Project-Manager-III_R20153": {
      "title": "Facilities Project Manager III",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-06\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Facilities Project Manager III Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 5 years of related experience Job Description: Facilities Planning and Management (FPM) at Iowa State University is seeking qualified candidates for a Facilities Project Manager III to lead the planning, design, and coordination of capital projects that support the University's teaching, research, and outreach mission. In this role, you'll manage moderate to large renovation and new construction projects, with primary responsibility for leading design phase activities. Responsibilities include managing budgets, monitoring the work of design professionals, obtaining project approvals, and serving as the primary point of contact for university clients, architects, engineers, and other professional consultants. We're looking for someone with strong project management experience and excellent communication skills who enjoys leading collaborative teams, solving complex challenges, and guiding projects from concept through construction. The ideal candidate is organized, detail-oriented, and comfortable balancing multiple priorities while working with diverse stakeholders. What You'll Do Lead and coordinate project activities for multiple moderate to large capital projects simultaneously, with primary responsibility for managing the planning and design phases. Coordinate consultant activities to ensure designs align with project goals, user needs, and university standards. Develop project budgets, manage project funds, and coordinate required approvals throughout the project lifecycle.Oversee design progress and help resolve challenges related to project scope, require ments, schedules, and stakeholder expectations. Collaborate with university construction managers to support a smooth transition from design into construction and successful project delivery. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Construction Management, Engineering, Architecture, or a related field. Experience managing the planning and design of commercial, institutional, or similarly complex building projects. Experience with large, complex, or multi-phase public sector construction projects, including procurement policies and regulations. Experience coordinating architects, engineers, design consultants, and other project stakeholders. Experience with sustainable design and construction standards, techniques, or methods. About Facilities Planning and Management Facilities Planning and Management (FPM) plays an essential role in maintaining, improving, and supporting Iowa State University's campus. With more than 450 full-time employees, along with student staff, our team provides a wide range of professional, technical, and skilled trades services that support the University's buildings, grounds, infrastructure, and utilities. Learn more about the department here Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Please Note: To receive full consideration, applications should be received by November 15, 2026. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS810 Original Posting Date: November 6, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20153 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Facilities-Construction-Manager-III_R20154": {
      "title": "Facilities Construction Manager III",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-06\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Facilities Construction Manager III Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 5 years of related experience Job Description: Facilities Planning and Management (FPM) is seeking a Facilities Construction Manager III . This position provides construction management services for moderate to large capital projects involving the renovation and new construction of campus facilities that support the University's teaching, research, and outreach mission. Responsibilities include serving as the University's Owner's Representative during the construction phase of assigned projects. This includes providing construction management, coordination, and construction administration services to ensure successful project delivery. The Facilities Construction Manager III works closely with contractors, project managers, consultants, and campus stakeholders to support project progress, resolve construction-related issues, and maintain effective communication throughout the construction process. Additionally, this position observes work in progress to ensure the installation of materials and equipment complies with contract documents, applicable codes, and university standards. The Facilities Construction Manager III oversees multiple projects simultaneously, with aggregate project budgets totaling up to $80 million. The successful candidate will possess strong communication, analytical, and organizational skills; be detail-oriented and proactive in problem solving; and have the ability to lead diverse project teams with differing interests, needs, and priorities while managing multiple projects concurrently. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in Construction Management, Engineering, Architecture, or a related field. Experience managing construction activities for commercial, institutional, or similarly complex building projects. Experience with construction administration, contractor coordination, and monitoring construction quality. Experience interpreting construction documents, building codes, and applicable construction standards. Experience with public sector construction projects, including procurement policies and regulations. About Facilities Planning and Management Facilities Planning and Management (FPM) plays an essential role in maintaining, improving, and supporting Iowa State University's campus. With more than 450 full-time employees, along with student staff, our team provides a wide range of professional, technical, and skilled trades services that support the University's buildings, grounds, infrastructure, and utilities. Learn more about the department here Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Please Note: To receive full consideration, applications should be received by November 15, 2026. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS811 Original Posting Date: November 6, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20154 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Department-Chair-of-Statistics_R20218": {
      "title": "Department Chair of Statistics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-09\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Department Chair of Statistics Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Statistics at Iowa State University seeks nominations and applications for the position of Professor and Chair. The department is jointly administered by the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences (LAS) and the College of Agriculture and Life Sciences (CALS). The Department of Statistics at Iowa State University is a nationally recognized leader in statistical education and research, with a graduate program highly ranked nationally. The department offers strong undergraduate and graduate programs and conducts innovative research in statistical theory, methodology, and applications, fostering interdisciplinary collaboration and providing statistical expertise to advance scientific discovery and address societal challenges.   Applications are sought for a visionary leader with demonstrated statistics and/or related experience. Candidates are expected to demonstrate a commitment to continued excellence in discipline-leading education of undergraduate and graduate students, and interdisciplinary and international research programs.   As leader of a jointly administered department, the Chair reports to the Dean of CALS and the Dean of LAS and serves as a collaborative member of both college leadership teams. The Chair works closely with faculty, staff, students, alumni, industry partners, community stakeholders, and university administrators to advance the department's strategic priorities and contribute to the missions of Iowa State University and both colleges.   Primary responsibilities of the department chair are to: Provide visionary leadership for the department to serve the needs of faculty, staff, students, stakeholders and citizens to fulfill the land-grant mission of the department, the college and university; Serve both the department and the dean’s office, including serving as a collaborative member of the colleges’ leadership teams; Communicate effectively the mission, vision and strengths of the department and colleges across Iowa State University and to external stakeholders and collaborators in the public and private sectors; Encourage and foster interdisciplinary collaboration with other departments, centers, and institutes within and external to the university; Foster a culture of collegiality, trust, empowerment, and shared responsibility that supports the success of all faculty, staff, and students, encourages individual initiative and professional growth, and promotes leadership development; Promote a culture of professionalism and accountability in achieving the department’s goals; Facilitate recruitment and retention of the best possible faculty and staff in all department positions; Stimulate and facilitate excellence and impact in all aspects of research, teaching, outreach, and service; Facilitate recruitment, retention, and enabling the academic and career success of students; Ensure sound fiscal and budgetary management of all departmental funds to achieve the mission of the department and comply with college and university-level policies and practices related to fiscal responsibility and management; Nurture and maintain good alumni relations and build alumni support; and Participate in activities on behalf of the department and the college, which may include after-hours events and travel.   Initial Department Chair appointment is for five years, with formal review during year four.  This appointment serves as an at-will position at the pleasure of the Deans.  This position will be filled as a 9-month appointment with two months of summer salary while serving as Chair.  Proposed start date July 1, 2027.   Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position.   Required Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. or academic equivalent in Statistics or a closely aligned field Must meet the university, college, and department requirements for appointment as tenured full professor   Preferred Qualifications: A clear vision and commitment for the growth and development of the department, including its contributions to the college and university mission, and appreciation of the broad spectrum of areas of statistical research and practice; Record of excellence in teaching, scholarship, and service consistent with a tenured faculty member, including evidence of generating sustained external funding; Evidence of effective and collaborative leadership, such as administrative experience in higher education and demonstrated ability to advance shared goals and priorities;  Capability for building and maintaining relationships with internal, external and international stakeholders and partners.   Department Unit/Website: https://www.stat.iastate.edu Proposed Start Date: July 1, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: 1) Resume/Curriculum Vitae 2) Letter of Application/Cover Letter 3) Contact Information for Three References For guaranteed consideration, please apply before January 15, 2027 . Position is open until filled. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: November 9, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20218 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Assistant-Director-Environmental-Health-and-Safety_R20208": {
      "title": "Assistant Director Environmental Health and Safety",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-09\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Director Environmental Health and Safety Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 5 years of related experience Job Description: Put your radiation safety expertise to work where innovation, research, and discovery happen every day! Iowa State University is seeking an Assistant Director of Environmental Health & Safety to serve as the university's Radiation Safety Officer (RSO) and lead its campus-wide Radiation Safety program. This is an exciting opportunity to take your technical expertise to the next level, lead a specialized safety program, and make a meaningful impact on the research, teaching, and veterinary medicine activities happening across campus. As a key member of the Environmental Health & Safety (EH&S) leadership team, you'll oversee radiation safety operations, ensure regulatory compliance, and collaborate with researchers, faculty, and staff to find practical solutions that support both safety and innovation.   Who We're Looking For: We're looking for a radiation safety professional who brings strong technical knowledge, enjoys solving complex challenges, and knows how to connect with people. The ideal candidate can evaluate radiological risks, explain technical information in a clear and approachable way, and help others understand not just what safety requirements are, but why they matter. We welcome professionals with backgrounds in health physics, radiation protection, research laboratories, government, military, healthcare, or other regulated environments. Whether you've managed a radiation safety program, led technical projects, mentored colleagues, or are ready to take the next step into leadership, we encourage you to explore this opportunity. Success in this role requires technical expertise, attention to detail, sound judgment, and the ability to build strong working relationships. Iowa State also values continued learning and professional growth, with opportunities for specialized Radiation Safety Officer training and leadership development.   What You'll Do: Lead the Radiation Safety Program: Oversee the safe use, handling, storage, and disposal of radioactive materials and radiation-producing equipment across campus. Manage Regulatory Compliance: Maintain the university's broad-scope radioactive materials license, oversee regulatory documentation, and coordinate inspections, audits, and reporting. Provide Technical Expertise: Evaluate radiological hazards, conduct or oversee radiation safety assessments and calculations, and recommend appropriate safety measures. Collaborate Across Campus: Partner with researchers, faculty, veterinary medicine professionals, and university leadership to provide practical guidance that supports safe teaching and research. Support Research and Veterinary Medicine: Provide radiation safety oversight for research laboratories, veterinary nuclear medicine, diagnostic X-ray systems, and other radiation-producing equipment. Develop and Improve Safety Programs: Create and maintain safety procedures, training programs, technical guidance, and documentation to support compliance and continuous improvement. Lead and Support Staff: Provide technical direction, coaching, and mentorship to radiation safety professionals while managing program priorities, resources, and daily operations. Promote Safety and Preparedness: Support radiation safety education, emergency response planning, and initiatives that strengthen safety awareness across the university.   About Environmental Health & Safety: Iowa State University's Environmental Health & Safety (EH&S) department plays an important role in supporting the university's research, teaching, and daily operations. Reporting to the Office of General Counsel, EH&S partners with the campus community to prevent injuries and illnesses, protect the environment, and promote a culture of safety and preparedness. Our Radiation Safety program supports more than 150 radioactive material users across approximately 80 laboratories, as well as specialized research and veterinary medicine operations. Through technical expertise, collaboration, and practical problem-solving, our team helps researchers, faculty, staff, and students carry out their work safely and successfully.       Preferred Qualifications Experience in radiation safety, health physics, radiation protection, or radioactive materials management. Experience interpreting and applying radiation safety regulations, including licensing, inspections, audits, or regulatory compliance. Experience evaluating radiological hazards, conducting radiation safety assessments, or implementing radiation protection measures. Experience developing safety procedures, technical documentation, training programs, or compliance initiatives. Experience leading technical projects, coordinating programs, mentoring colleagues, or supervising staff. Experience communicating technical information, providing safety guidance, or collaborating with stakeholders across different roles or disciplines.   Guaranteed Consideration Date: This position will remain open until filled. The last day to apply for full consideration is November 30, 2026 . Applications received after this date may be considered. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS812 Original Posting Date: November 9, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20208 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Academic-Advisor-II_R20164": {
      "title": "Academic Advisor II",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-09\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Academic Advisor II Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 2 years of related experience Job Description: The Department of Apparel, Events, and Hospitality Management in the College of Health and Human Services seeks an Academic Advisor II to provide comprehensive, student-centered academic advising services.   This position supports current and prospective students, as well as their families, by providing guidance on majors, minors, course planning, academic policies, and probation processes. The Academic Advisor II helps students navigate their academic pathways while connecting them with campus resources that promote student success and well-being, including academic support services, counseling, and financial aid. Through proactive outreach, individualized advising, and collaborative problem-solving, this role plays a vital part in fostering student achievement, a sense of belonging, and student retention. Example of Duties Advise current students in the Department of Apparel, Events, and Hospitality Management (AESHM). Meet individually with advisees and maintain accurate advising records. Provide guidance on degree requirements, course planning, academic policies, and university procedures. Review and approve course substitutions in coordination with AESHM Program Directors. Process change-of-major requests and approve minor declarations. Maintain transfer plans with community colleges. Monitor student success data and advising records in MapWorks, Navigate, and Workday. Conduct proactive outreach to support student success, retention, and engagement, and connect students with appropriate campus resources. Coordinate industry campus visits. Lead AESHM Learning Communities, including Common Threads and Directions, in collaboration with advising team members. Interpret university and departmental policies and procedures for students and families. Refer students to appropriate campus resources, including academic support services, counseling services, financial aid, and other student support programs. Collaborate with college staff, departmental faculty, and the AESHM advising team to develop and implement recruitment and outreach plans. Participate in student recruitment activities, campus visits, orientation programs, and other enrollment initiatives. Coordinate and lead orientation programs for new students and families. Teach orientation courses. Present at orientation sessions, open houses, visit days, and other departmental events. Advise student organizations and support student leadership development. Lead AESHM Learning Communities, including Common Threads and Directions, in collaboration with advising team members.   Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree in higher education, student affairs, counseling, fashion design and merchandising, hospitality management, event management, or a related field. Experience providing academic advising or student support services in a higher education setting. Experience teaching, facilitating workshops, or delivering presentations, including public speaking to student or professional audiences. Professional experience in the fashion design and merchandising, hospitality management, or event management industry. Experience collaborating with faculty, staff, and campus partners and using student information or advising systems to support student success. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS806 Original Posting Date: November 9, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 16, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20164 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Education-Extension-Specialist-III_R20185": {
      "title": "Education Extension Specialist III",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-09\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Education Extension Specialist III Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 5 years of related experience Job Description: Build the Future of Agriculture If you enjoy working with young people and want to help them discover the technologies, careers, and opportunities shaping the future of agriculture, this is the role for you. Who We Are The Digital Ag Innovation Lab at Iowa State University partners with leading agricultural companies to design, build, and deploy next-generation technologies for agriculture. Our team works at the intersection of applied engineering, industry collaboration, and the land-grant mission, moving ideas from concept to prototype to field deployment. Our vision is bold: to be the premier thought leader and partner in ag innovation . Our mission guides everything we do: Innovate. Educate. Outreach .   We operate with four core values: Passion. Innovation. Collaboration. Excellence . This is a place for builders, problem-solvers, and systems thinkers who want their work to move from idea → prototype → field → industry adoption. The Opportunity We are seeking a K-12 Agricultural Education & Outreach Specialist to bring ag technology to K-12 students across Iowa. Through school visits, FFA and 4-H programs, presentations, demonstrations, facility tours, and events, you will help students explore emerging agricultural technologies and the various career pathways available in agriculture. This is a highly visible, statewide role for someone who enjoys presenting, building relationships, traveling, and representing Digital Ag and Iowa State University Extension in communities across Iowa. What You'll Do Lead the development, coordination, and delivery of statewide K-12 agricultural technology education programs, including curriculum, presentations, demonstrations, and hands-on learning activities. Engage students, educators, FFA chapters, 4-H programs, school clubs, and other youth-focused organizations through educational presentations, school visits, facility tours, and events. Translate Digital Ag research and emerging technologies, including precision agriculture, artificial intelligence (AI), machine learning, data analytics, geographic information systems (GIS), robotics, drones, and automation, into engaging, age-appropriate educational content. Build relationships with educators, youth program leaders, and community partners to identify programming needs, expand engagement opportunities, and support ongoing collaboration. Collaborate with Digital Ag staff, Extension professionals, university partners, and K-12 educators to develop and maintain educational materials and programming. Represent Digital Ag, Iowa State University Extension, and the agricultural industry at school programs, career events, conferences, field days, and community activities. Develop and maintain a roadmap for current and future programs aligned with K-12 academic calendars, state and national conventions, and opportunities to reach target audiences across Iowa. Evaluate program participation, reach, feedback, and learning outcomes to document impact, inform continuous improvement, and guide future programming. Promote awareness of agricultural career pathways and connect students with educational and career opportunities available through Iowa State University and the agricultural industry. What You Bring Experience working with K-12 students, educators, or youth-focused educational programs. Knowledge of agriculture and an interest in agricultural technology, innovation, and career development. Experience developing educational programs or curriculum for K-12 audiences and evaluating program participation, outcomes, or impact. Strong presentation and communication skills with the ability to engage audiences of different ages and backgrounds. Ability to translate technical and scientific information into clear, engaging educational content. Strong organizational and relationship-building skills, with the ability to independently coordinate programs, manage multiple priorities, and collaborate with educators, university partners, and community stakeholders. Professionalism and confidence representing an organization in public settings, along with the ability and willingness to travel regularly throughout Iowa. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor's degree in agricultural education, agricultural communications, agriculture, education, Extension, agricultural business, agricultural engineering or technology, or a related field. Experience working with FFA, 4-H, agricultural education, Extension, or K-12 STEM programs. Familiarity with precision agriculture, agricultural equipment, artificial intelligence (AI), machine learning, data analytics, geographic information systems (GIS), robotics, drones, automation, or other emerging agricultural technologies. Experience coordinating educational or outreach programs across multiple schools, communities, or geographic regions. Experience developing partnerships with agricultural organizations, industry partners, or educational institutions to support youth programming or career exploration. This position involves in state travel and may include occasional out of state travel, as well as evening and weekend hours. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. This is a term position with the expectation of long-term renewal. The selected candidate will be hired as an Education Extension Specialist III. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular with Term Appointment (Fixed Term) Proposed End Date or Length of Term: December 13, 2029 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS808 Original Posting Date: November 9, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 29, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20185 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
