    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Industrial-Hygienist-I-II---Ames-National-Laboratory_R20199": {
      "title": "Industrial Hygienist I/II - Ames National Laboratory",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-06\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Industrial Hygienist I/II - Ames National Laboratory Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 2 years of related experience Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: Under general supervision of the Ames Laboratory Senior Industrial Hygienist, the Industrial Hygienist I performs foundational industrial hygiene activities that help anticipate, recognize, evaluate, and control occupational health hazards and confirm protection from risks from occupational health hazards in laboratories, shops, offices, field locations, construction/maintenance projects, and other assigned work areas. Builds technical competence under the guidance of a more experienced industrial hygienist. In addition to all of the duties listed above, the Industrial Hygienist II works independently to provide industrial hygiene services for an assigned portfolio of laboratory operations, facilities, research activities, or programs. Plans and executes routine and moderately complex exposure assessments, interprets results, recommends controls, and supports compliance decisions with applicable DOE, OSHA, state, and laboratory requirements. Industrial Hygienist I Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree Industrial Hygienist II Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree and 2 years related experience Preferred Qualifications: Graduate degree in a relevant science, engineering, industrial hygiene, or occupational/environmental health discipline or at least three years of related professional experience. Licensure in one or more of the following:  Certified Industrial Hygienist (CIH), Certified or Associate Safety Professional (CSP or ASP), Certified Hazardous Materials Manager (CHMM) Associate in Risk Management (ARM), Registered Environmental Manager. Credentials, relevant professional proficiency certifications, or documented continuing-education work in the field of occupational safety and health. Demonstrated experience in exposure assessment, workplace hazard evaluation, sampling equipment, technical reporting, and work planning/control in a research, industrial, or comparable setting. Working knowledge of applicable OSHA standards, 10 CFR Part 851, relevant DOE directives and laboratory procedures, and recognized IH methods. Ability to manage multiple assignments, explain technical findings, influence safe work practices, and maintain defensible records. Department/Program & College Description: Would you like to work for a National Laboratory that conducts world-renowned research? Would you enjoy working on a beautiful university campus? Can you imagine yourself in a mid-sized location that regularly ranks as one of the U.S. Best Places to Live ? If you answered yes to any of these questions, you should consider a career with Ames National Laboratory!   Ames Laboratory is a U.S. Department of Energy federally contracted National Laboratory located in Ames, Iowa, on the campus of Iowa State University. We are dedicated to translating foundational science through applied research to create technological innovations. We create materials, inspire minds to solve problems, and address some of the most challenging issues facing our world today. We promote and believe in a culture of civility and shared ownership in support of the Laboratory's collective success. Employees with appointment at Ames National Laboratory are subject to particular restrictions related to participation in Foreign Government Sponsored or Affiliated Activities, as defined and detailed in United States Department of Energy Order 486.1A. You will be asked to disclose any such participation during the recruitment phase for review by Ames National Laboratory.   Employment is contingent upon satisfying applicable requirements of Ames National Laboratory’s federal sponsor, the United States Department of Energy, and ISU requirements. These may include background checks and eligibility determinations related to access of facilities, information, or projects. This position requires the incumbent to obtain and maintain government access authorization for the duration of the appointment.  Department Unit/Website: www.ameslab.gov Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter List of Professional References Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS810 Original Posting Date: November 6, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 20, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20199 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Digital-Agriculture-Extension-Lead_R20184": {
      "title": "Digital Agriculture Extension Lead",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-06\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Digital Agriculture Extension Lead Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 5 years of related experience Job Description: Build the Future of Agriculture If you want to help farmers and agricultural professionals understand and adopt emerging technologies, this is the role for you. Who We Are The Digital Ag Innovation Lab at Iowa State University partners with leading agricultural companies to design, build, and deploy next-generation technologies for agriculture. Our team works at the intersection of applied engineering, industry collaboration, and the land-grant mission, moving ideas from concept to prototype to field deployment. Our vision is bold: to be the premier thought leader and partner in ag innovation . Our mission guides everything we do: Innovate. Educate. Outreach .   We operate with four core values: Passion. Innovation. Collaboration. Excellence . This is a place for builders, problem-solvers, and systems thinkers who want their work to move from idea → prototype → field → industry adoption. The Opportunity We are seeking a Digital Agriculture Extension Lead to lead the people, programs, and partnerships that deliver Iowa State University Extension programming on digital agriculture throughout Iowa and beyond. This role connects research and technology development with practical education for a wide range of audiences, from farmers to agricultural professionals. You will lead the strategy, roadmap planning, new program development and delivery of hands-on programs that translate emerging agricultural technologies and Digital Ag research into actionable outcomes that create direct and measurable on-farm value. Working with Digital Ag researchers, engineers, agronomists, Extension specialists, field staff, and industry partners, you will identify educational needs, develop programming, lead Extension staff, and expand the reach and impact of Iowa State University’s Extension and Outreach portfolio. What You'll Do Lead Digital Ag's Extension program, including strategy, roadmaps, staffing, partnerships, and annual programming. Develop and deliver new educational programs that translate research findings and emerging agricultural technologies into practical information for farmers and agricultural professionals.  Programs will focus on connecting agronomic research, technology and machinery implementation, systems thinking in crop production, and innovation through data and AI.  Identify producers and industry needs and use them to guide future programming and educational resources, ensuring content remains highly relevant. Lead and develop program staff, students, and other contributors involved in Iowa State Extension programming in Digital Ag. Build partnerships across Iowa State University Extension and Outreach, including field agronomists, agricultural engineers, campus specialists, and county and regional staff. Develop relationships with farmers, agribusinesses, commodity organizations, technology companies, and other partners to expand program reach and engage new audiences. Measure and communicate program participation, learning outcomes, adoption, and economic or operational impact. What You Bring Experience in Extension and outreach, professional education, agricultural training, technical education, product support, agronomy, precision agriculture, agricultural equipment, or a related field. Knowledge of production agriculture and technologies used in modern crop production systems. Experience developing and delivering high impact educational programs, technical training, demonstrations, field days, or similar programming. Ability to translate complex technical and research information into clear, practical guidance for farmers and agricultural professionals. Experience leading people, managing budgets and programs, and coordinating cross-functional teams. Experience building relationships with farmers, industry partners, researchers, and agricultural organizations. Strong communication, facilitation, and presentation skills. Preferred Qualifications Advanced degree in agricultural education, agricultural engineering, agronomy, agricultural systems technology, crop science, or a related field, or equivalent industry experience. Experience developing educational programs for farmers, agricultural professionals, or adult learners. Experience with digital agriculture, precision agriculture, agricultural equipment, application technology, or emerging agricultural technologies. Experience developing partnerships among universities, industry, and agricultural organizations. Experience managing multiple programs, events, budgets, and staff. Experience evaluating educational programs and documenting outcomes and impact. Experience developing externally funded Extension, educational, or industry-partnership programs.   This position involves in state travel and may include occasional out of state travel, as well as evening and weekend hours. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. This is a term position with the expectation of long-term renewal.   The selected candidate will be hired as a Manager Engineering. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular with Term Appointment (Fixed Term) Proposed End Date or Length of Term: December 13, 2029 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS812 Original Posting Date: November 6, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 29, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20184 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
