    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Postdoctoral-Researcher-in-Analysis-and-PDEs_R20197": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher in Analysis and PDEs",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-06\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Postdoctoral Researcher in Analysis and PDEs Appointment Type: Post Doc/Trainee Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Mathematics at Iowa State University invites applications for postdoctoral position(s) in analysis and partial differential equations (PDEs). This opening aligns with the research interests of Professor Pablo Raúl Stinga. The position is anticipated to be a two-year appointment, with the possibility of extension to a third year contingent upon the availability of funding. The position carries a 2-1 teaching load and includes mentoring undergraduate students in research through the Iowa State Math Research Teams (ISMaRT) program under the supervision of Professor Xuan Hien Nguyen. Required Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in Mathematics or a closely related discipline, completed prior to the start date. Demonstrated research interest in analysis and partial differential equations (PDEs). Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated research interest in regularity estimates, fractional PDEs, and free boundary problems. Research experience in numerical analysis and computational implementation of geometric PDEs. Demonstrated commitment to excellence in teaching, mentoring, and supporting student success. Department/Program & College Description: The Department of Mathematics at Iowa State University is a vibrant academic community with strengths in pure and applied mathematics, offering outstanding opportunities in research, teaching, and student mentorship. Faculty maintain active, externally funded research programs across a broad range of mathematical disciplines, while fostering a collaborative environment that supports innovation, interdisciplinary engagement, and student success. The department is committed to excellence in scholarship and education and provides opportunities for undergraduate and graduate students to participate in cutting-edge research Department Unit/Website: Department of Mathematics Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. To be guaranteed consideration, applications must be received by December 15th, 2026. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Research statement Teaching statement Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: Post Docs Original Posting Date: November 6, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20197 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
