    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Electrician-I_R20209": {
      "title": "Electrician I",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-06\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Electrician I Job Group: Merit Required Minimum Qualifications: • Requires State of Iowa Class A or B Journeyman Electrician license. • Must possess a valid driver’s license and meet University’s Fleet Safety Program. Job Description: Department Description – Utility Services Utility Services is a 24-hour, 365-day-a-year operation dedicated to meeting the energy needs of the Iowa State University community. The department operates and maintains four energy production facilities, as well as an extensive network of utility distribution systems that serve the entire Iowa State campus. Through a commitment to operational excellence, safety, and sustainability, Utility Services works to provide reliable, economical, and environmentally responsible utility services that support the university's teaching, research, and outreach mission. Its primary goal is to safely deliver dependable utility services while continuously advancing sustainability and efficiency across campus operations. Preferred Qualifications Experience reading blueprints and electrical schematics Experience installing, maintaining, and repairing Utility electrical systems.  Experience working electrical maintenance in utility plant or process plant environment. Click below to learn more about our team! Utilities Characteristic Duties and Responsibilities • Installs, maintains, troubleshoots, repairs and replaces electrical systems and electrical operated equipment (generally less than 600V), including but not limited to circuit breakers, relays, switches, wiring, conduit, receptacles, and magnetic starters and controls. • Installs, maintains, troubleshoots, repairs and replaces electrical equipment, including but not limited to electric motors, transformers, generators, lights, fixtures, bulbs, tubes, motor control systems and meters. • Draws layouts, reads and interprets blueprints, schematics and other drawings. • As required, estimates materials needed and records time and materials expended on each work order. • Performs preventive maintenance on electrical equipment and systems. • Requires the knowledge of and ability to interpret local, state and national electrical codes. • Requires the ability to interpret instructions, design specifications and blueprints. • Perform other related duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities • Knowledge of the principles, methods and techniques used in the electrical trade. • Knowledge of the tools and equipment of the electrical trade and skill in their safe use. • Knowledge of the occupational hazards and safety precautions of the trade. • Knowledge of safety precautions mandated by OSHA, NFPA, NEC, and the EPA. • Knowledge of and ability to interpret local, state and national electrical codes. • Ability to interpret instructions, specifications and blueprints. • Ability to plan and perform work involving the installation, modification, troubleshooting and repair of new and existing electrical systems, and related equipment. • Ability to communicate effectively orally and in writing. • Ability to work outdoors in all types of weather conditions or in areas where there is exposure to excessive noise, dirt and fumes and at elevated heights from ladders, scaffolds, or hydraulic lifts. • Ability to work independently during normal work hours and after hours. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: 5071a Original Posting Date: November 6, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 29, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20209 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Postdoctoral-Research-Associate-in-Mathematical-Biology_R20202": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate in Mathematical Biology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-06\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Postdoctoral Research Associate in Mathematical Biology Appointment Type: Post Doc/Trainee Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Department of Mathematics at Iowa State University invites applications for a two-year Postdoctoral Research Associate position, with the possibility of extension to a third year contingent upon available funding. The postdoctoral researcher will join Professor Claus Kadelka's research program in mathematical biology. Candidates should have defined research interests in mathematical biology. Research areas include systems biology, gene regulatory networks, infectious disease modeling, and behavioral epidemiology. Current projects examine how the structure and dynamics of biological regulatory networks shape biological function, including the NSF-funded projects Canalization and Other Design Principles of Gene Regulatory Network Models and A Mathematical Theory for the Biological Concept of Modularity . Additional projects focus on developing mathematical and computational models that account for heterogeneity in human behavior, contact patterns, and other individual-level characteristics and studying their effects on population-level disease dynamics. The specific research direction will be determined based on the successful candidate's expertise and interests, with flexibility to pursue new questions within these areas. The position includes a 2-1 teaching load and involvement in mentoring undergraduate students in research through Iowa State Math Research Teams (ISMaRT). Required Minimum Qualifications: PhD in Mathematics or a closely related discipline by the appointment start date. Preferred Qualifications: Strong research record in areas aligned with Professor Claus Kadelka's research interests, including discrete dynamical systems, network science, computational systems biology, infectious disease modeling, or related fields. Demonstrated ability to conduct independent research and collaborate effectively in an interdisciplinary research environment. Experience teaching undergraduate mathematics courses and mentoring students in research. Experience publishing scholarly research and communicating research findings to scientific audiences. Experience programming in Python. Department/Program & College Description: The Department of Mathematics at Iowa State University is a vibrant academic community with strengths in pure and applied mathematics, offering outstanding opportunities in research, teaching, and student mentorship.   Faculty maintain active, externally funded research programs across a broad range of mathematical disciplines, while fostering a collaborative environment that supports innovation, interdisciplinary engagement, and student success.   The department is committed to excellence in scholarship and education and provides opportunities for undergraduate and graduate students to participate in cutting-edge research Department Unit/Website: Department of Mathematics Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Research statement Teaching statement Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Proposed Start Date: August 16, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: Post Docs Original Posting Date: November 6, 2026 Posting Close Date: December 15, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20202 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Research-Technician-II_R20042": {
      "title": "Research Technician II",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-10\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Research Technician II Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent and 3 years of related experience Job Description: The Department of Animal Science at Iowa State University is seeking a Research Technician II to support innovative research investigating how environmental exposures, including per- and polyfluoroalkyl substances (PFAS), affect ovarian function and reproductive health. This is a unique opportunity to contribute to research with potential implications for human health, addressing important questions in reproductive health that affect roughly half of the population, while developing expertise across animal research, molecular and cellular laboratory techniques, and research data analysis. You'll join a team that invests in professional development, provides opportunities to work with researchers across Iowa State and other universities, and supports individual career goals. You'll be part of a collaborative environment where strong organization, communication, and teamwork are essential to keeping research moving forward. What You'll Do Coordinate laboratory activities, prepare reagents and experimental materials, and maintain accurate research records and inventories. Perform animal research procedures, including dosing, breeding colony management, tissue collection, necropsy support, and biological sample processing in accordance with approved research protocols. Conduct molecular and cellular laboratory techniques such as RNA isolation, protein extraction, Western blotting, immunohistochemistry, histological processing, microscopy, and follicle quantification. Collect, organize, analyze, and maintain research data from animal studies and laboratory experiments, ensuring data quality, accuracy, and integrity. Prepare datasets, summaries, figures, and reports to support research publications, presentations, grant reporting, and other project needs. Operate, calibrate, maintain, and troubleshoot laboratory instrumentation and specialized research equipment, addressing technical issues that may affect experimental outcomes. Assist with developing, optimizing, and validating laboratory protocols and research methods and recommend improvements to laboratory processes. Train and provide technical guidance to undergraduate researchers, graduate students, and other laboratory personnel on research techniques, laboratory procedures, and safety practices. Communicate research findings, technical concerns, and recommendations with the principal investigator and research team. Preferred Qualifications : Bachelor's degree in biology, animal science, biochemistry, molecular biology, reproductive physiology, or a related field. Experience with molecular or cellular laboratory techniques such as RNA isolation, protein extraction, Western blotting, immunohistochemistry, histology, or microscopy. Experience with animal handling, dosing, tissue collection, or other animal-based research procedures. Experience collecting, organizing, analyzing, or interpreting research data. Experience troubleshooting laboratory procedures, assays, or research equipment. Experience training or providing technical guidance to students or other laboratory personnel. This is a term appointment that may have opportunity for renewal. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular with Term Appointment (Fixed Term) Proposed End Date or Length of Term: November 15, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS805 Original Posting Date: October 8, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 22, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20042 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Department-Chair-of-Industrial-Design_R20222": {
      "title": "Department Chair of Industrial Design",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-10\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Department Chair of Industrial Design Appointment Type: Faculty Job Description: The Department of Industrial Design in the College of Design at Iowa State University is seeking a dynamic and accomplished leader, with an interest in collaborative and interdisciplinary design education, to join the faculty in the role of Department Chair at the rank of associate professor or professor with tenure. This position is a full-time appointment (9-month with summer support). The anticipated start date is July 1, 2027. The Chair is the designated executive officer of the department and is responsible for leadership and oversight of central departmental administrative operations. In this capacity, the Chair serves at the pleasure of the Dean of the College of Design. We are looking for someone with a passion for design education, a commitment to excellence, and the ability to advance all three dimensions of the land-grant mission: education, research/creative inquiry, and outreach. Founded in 2010, our department is young, growing, and open to new ideas. The next Chair will have the chance to shape what it becomes: its curriculum, its research and industry partnerships, and its culture. We want a collaborative, open communicator who enjoys helping faculty and students do their best work. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Position Responsibilities: Articulate and advocate for the department’s mission, values and priorities within the University and beyond; Lead strategic planning with faculty, setting clear goals for the department’s growth and direction; Oversee curriculum development, course scheduling and teaching assignments, program assessment and accreditation; Manage the departmental budget and shared governance, and supervise departmental faculty; Recruit, hire, and retain excellent faculty, conduct annual reviews, and support faculty development at every career stage; Strengthen inter-disciplinary connections with programs across the College and University, and build relationships with communities, professionals, alumni, donors and industry partners; Support department, college and university efforts in student recruitment, marketing, communication, and fundraising; Actively promote and expand the reach of industrial design across the state, increasing national recognition of the program and our graduates; Represent department and college at professional organizations and/or academic symposia; Foster a welcoming, respectful, and supportive environment for all students and faculty; Guide faculty through promotion and tenure and term-faculty advancement reviews, in line with college and university policies. Maintain an active program of research, creative work, or professional practice, and teach as appropriate to the appointment;   Required Minimum Qualifications: Terminal degree (MFA, MID, or PhD) in industrial design, product design or a closely related field; Record of scholarship, creative work, and/or professional accomplishment that qualifies for appointment at the rank of associate professor or full professor with tenure at Iowa State University;   Preferred Qualifications: PhD in product/industrial design or design-related fields; Demonstrated experience in academic administration and/or supervisory experience, including fiscal and personnel management; Experience building industry partnerships; Record of successful funded research or recognized professional accomplishment in industrial design practice; Active engagement in interdisciplinary or transdisciplinary collaborations.     Department/Program & College Description: The Department of Industrial Design was formed in 2010 as part of the College’s expansion plan and endeavor to create the most comprehensive college of design in the region. The department was formed with a vision to bridge the intersections between design academics, practitioners and end-users, by exploring new models, tools and modes of working that strengthen design practice, support social and growth development and build a world-class learning environment. The department includes 11 faculty members, and approximately 210 undergraduate and 13 graduate students. The Industrial Design department offers a Bachelor of Industrial Design (BID) and a Master of Industrial Design (MID). Both the undergraduate and graduate programs are accredited by the National Association of Schools of Art and Design (NASAD). The undergraduate program includes cross-disciplinary studios, minors, industry-sponsored projects, study abroad and internships. The department has built strategic collaborations with highly ranked programs across campus, including mechanical engineering, apparel design and business, and we offer a concurrent degree that leads to both a BID and a Master of Business Administration (MBA). Our faculty also teach alongside Graphic Design faculty in the newly established undergraduate Minor in User Experience Design and the online Master of Arts in User Experience Design.   The College of Design brings together architecture, art and visual culture, graphic design, industrial design, interior design, landscape architecture, and urban planning and development so working across disciplines is part of everyday life. Iowa State is located in Ames, a friendly and affordable college town about 30 miles north of Des Moines.   Department Unit/Website: https://www.design.iastate.edu /  Proposed Start Date: July 1, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 09 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: (1) a letter of interest describing your leadership approach and your vision for the department, (2) a curriculum vitae, (3) a portfolio or summary of your research, creative work, or professional practice, and (4) contact information for [three to five] references.   Review of applications will begin on January 15 and will continue until the position is filled. Questions about the search can be sent to Search Committee Chair Paul Bruski, Department Chair of Graphic Design, bruski@iastate.edu . Why Choose ISU? Iowa State Faculty enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental; as well as: • Retirement benefits, including defined benefit and defined contribution plans • Generous leave plans • Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) • Life insurance and long-term disability • Flexible Spending Accounts • Various voluntary benefits and discounts • Employee Assistance Program • Wellbeing program Original Posting Date: November 10, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20222 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Part-time-Administrative-Assistant-II_R20207": {
      "title": "Part-time Administrative Assistant II",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-10\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Part-time Administrative Assistant II Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent and 3 years of related experience Job Description: The Department of Political Science within the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences at Iowa State University is seeking a Part-Time Administrative Assistant II to support the department's daily front-office operations.   This position will greet and assist walk-in visitors, directing individuals to appropriate campus services, and responding to telephone, email, and written inquiries from faculty, staff, students, patrons, and alumni. Examples of Duties: Manage daily front-office operations, including reception, telephone and email inquiries, and visitor assistance. Coordinate department calendars, room reservations, meetings, and events. Maintain departmental files, directories, listservs, website content, and office supplies. Process purchasing, financial transactions, travel arrangements, reimbursements, and purchasing card expenses. Coordinate departmental IT and key requests, distribution, and returns. Provide administrative support to the department chair, faculty, staff, and students. Support faculty reviews, student employment, hiring, onboarding, and payroll-related processes. Coordinate student recruitment activities, campus visits, student ambassadors, scholarships, and student opportunities. Assist with departmental events, guest speakers, faculty recruitment, and special projects. Provide backup administrative support to other departments as needed. Coordinate course scheduling, registration updates, faculty assignments, room reservations, and enrollment tracking through Workday. Support the graduate program, including admissions and processing assistantships for graduate students. Preferred Qualifications: Experience serving as a primary point of contact and providing administrative support in a professional office environment. Strong organizational skills, including managing calendars, coordinating schedules, and balancing multiple administrative responsibilities. Ability to prioritize tasks, manage competing deadlines, and ensure timely completion of assignments. Strong attention to detail and accuracy in completing administrative tasks and maintaining records. This is a 10-month, 30-hour-per-week appointment, with an expected work schedule of Monday through Friday. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position . Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 10 Month Work Period Time Type: Part time Pay Grade: PS806 Original Posting Date: November 10, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 17, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20207 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Budget-and-Finance-Specialist-III_R20223": {
      "title": "Budget and Finance Specialist III",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-09\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Budget and Finance Specialist III Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 5 years of related experience Job Description: The Iowa State University Budget Office seeks qualified candidates for a Budget and Finance Specialist III position supporting the President’s Division. The Budget Office provides financial planning, analysis, budgeting, forecasting, and reporting services that support sound financial stewardship and informed decision-making across the university. This position serves as a strategic financial partner to divisional and senior leadership, providing leadership and direction for budget development, financial planning, forecasting, and resource management activities. The position works across multiple university units and funds to develop meaningful financial insights, identify risks and opportunities, and support decisions that advance Iowa State University’s mission and strategic priorities. Some key responsibilities for this role include the following: Providing strategic financial analysis and recommendations to leadership. Providing leadership and direction for budget development and financial planning. Developing multi-fund, multi-year forecasting and budget projections. Conducting financial analysis, scenario modeling, and data analytics. Identifying financial risks, opportunities, and potential efficiencies. Ensuring responsible use of resources and compliance with financial policies. Supporting effective use of Workday Finance and Planning systems and related processes. Providing financial guidance and training to divisional fiscal staff. Serving as the financial representative for the President’s Division on central finance committees and teams. Providing leadership and coordination across divisional fiscal operations. Serving as backup for institutional financial planning, analysis, and reporting. The ideal candidate should possess strong analytical, critical-thinking, time-management, and organizational skills, along with the ability to excel in a complex and dynamic environment. Effective verbal and written communication skills are essential. Additionally, the successful candidate will demonstrate sound professional judgment, strong problem-solving skills, and the ability to translate complex financial information into clear, actionable insights. The candidate should thrive in a collaborative setting and demonstrate a commitment to service, integrity, ethical conduct, and continuous improvement. Preferred Qualifications Experience providing financial analysis, planning, recommendations, and business partner support to senior or executive leadership. Experience executing financial forecasting, budget development, and multi-year financial planning. Experience developing and executing financial analytics, modeling, and using data to inform business and resource decisions. Experience operating within enterprise financial planning, budgeting, or reporting systems and processes. Experience implementing AI or automation related to financial planning, analysis, reporting, or process improvement is a plus. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Please Note: To receive full consideration, applications should be received by November 22, 2026. Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS810 Original Posting Date: November 9, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20223 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Business-Administrator-II_R20151": {
      "title": "Business Administrator II",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-09\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Business Administrator II Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 2 years of related experience Job Description: The College of Design seeks a qualified Business Administrator II to oversee the business affairs and operations of assigned departments.   The Departmental Partner plays a pivotal role within the Administrative Services Office (ASO) of the College of Design. This position provides a unique opportunity to apply a variety set of skills and significantly influences the operation of our departments. The ASO values the unique contributions of each team member and encourages an atmosphere that nurtures growth and professional development.     This role reports to the college's Fiscal Officer and collaborates closely with chairs, faculty, and students. It involves a range of administrative duties crucial to the success of our academic efforts. It requires an adaptable, collaborative, and communicative individual proficient in multitasking.   Examples of Duties: Budget and Financial Management Manage departmental cost centers, budgets, and financial transactions using Workday, including state, course fee, and foundation funds. Prepare and analyze budgets and financial reports; advise department chairs on expenditures tracking, budget comparison, and financial decisions. Approve expenses, reconcile accounts, and ensure compliance with university financial policies and procedures. Administrative and Departmental Support Coordinate course scheduling, room assignments, and faculty/instructor records in Workday Student. Support department chairs with meeting coordination and follow-up on departmental matters. Facilitate departmental voting and provide guidance on college and university policies and procedures. Process graduate student hiring, assistantship appointments, scholarships. Support Department faculty searches through job postings, candidate travel, scheduling, and logistics. Faculty and Student Support Serve as a resource for faculty regarding departmental policies, procedures, and administrative matters. Coordinate faculty promotion and tenure documentation.   Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, Business Administration, or a closely related field. Experience in financial management, including monthly account reconciliations, budget oversight, expense monitoring, and financial reporting. Proven ability to ability to explain and interpret financial information, policies, and procedures to faculty, staff, and other stakeholders to support informed decision-making. Experience in a higher education or similarly complex organizational environment, with the ability to learn and navigate financial, academic, and administrative policies and procedures. Experience providing administrative support in an academic or organizational setting, including personnel and student employment processes, scheduling and course coordination, scholarship or financial assistance administration, and faculty support. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS808 Original Posting Date: November 9, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 19, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20151 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
