    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Postdoctoral-Research-Associate--4-month-TERM----Ames-National-Laboratory_R20238": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate (4-month TERM) - Ames National Laboratory",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-11\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Postdoctoral Research Associate (4-month TERM) - Ames National Laboratory Appointment Type: Post Doc/Trainee Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: The Division of Materials Science and Engineering at Ames National Laboratory seeks a Postdoctoral Research Associate to conduct high magnetic field characterization, heat capacity, and magnetotransport measurements of kagome metals.  The candidate must have experience in preparing single-crystal samples and conducting measurements in high-field environments, including pulsed fields.  This will be a 4-month term position. Required Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in experimental condensed-matter physics, applied physics, materials science and engineering, or a closely related field. Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated hands-on experience with low-temperature experimental techniques, cryogenic systems, focused ion-beam sample preparation, high magnetic fields and pulsed fields.  Experience conducting experiments at the National High Magnetic Field Laboratory is highly valued. Background in magnetism, topological materials, and familiarity with conventional characterization (transport, PPMS/MPMS). Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively in written reports, oral presentations, manuscripts, and interdisciplinary team discussions; collaborate with others; maintain accurate laboratory records; and meet project milestones. Department/Program & College Description: Would you like to work for a National Laboratory that conducts world-renowned research? Would you enjoy working on a beautiful university campus? Can you imagine yourself in a mid-sized location that regularly ranks as one of the U.S. Best Places to Live ? If you answered yes to any of these questions, you should consider a career with Ames National Laboratory!   Ames Laboratory is a U.S. Department of Energy federally contracted National Laboratory located in Ames, Iowa, on the campus of Iowa State University. We are dedicated to translating foundational science through applied research to create technological innovations. We create materials, inspire minds to solve problems, and address some of the most challenging issues facing our world today. We promote and believe in a culture of civility and shared ownership in support of the Laboratory's collective success. Employment is with Iowa State University with appointment at Ames National Laboratory. Your appointment is contingent, at the time of hire and throughout your employment, on satisfying applicable requirements of Ames National Laboratory’s f ederal sponsor, the United States Department of Energy, and ISU requirements. These may include background checks, required disclosures of certain activities or affiliations, and eligibility determinations related to access of facilities, information, or projects. All positions require obtaining and maintaining federal government-issued access authorizations or meeting additional compliance requirements. If you do not meet or maintain applicable requirements or authorizations, or are deemed ineligible to participate in Laboratory activities, ISU may withdraw this offer or take appropriate employment action, up to and including termination. Department Unit/Website (if applicable): www.ameslab.gov Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter List of Professional References Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Proposed Start Date: January 1, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: Post Docs Original Posting Date: November 11, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 17, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20238 Employees with appointment at Ames National Laboratory are subject to particular restrictions related to participation in Foreign Government Sponsored or Affiliated Activities, as defined and detailed in United States Department of Energy Order 486.1A. You will be asked to disclose any such participation during the recruitment phase for review by Ames National Laboratory.   Employment is contingent upon satisfying applicable requirements of Ames National Laboratory’s federal sponsor, the United States Department of Energy, and ISU requirements. These may include background checks and eligibility determinations related to access of facilities, information, or projects. This position requires the incumbent to obtain and maintain government access authorization for the duration of the appointment.  Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Secretary-II_R20228": {
      "title": "Secretary II",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-10\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Secretary II Job Group: Merit Required Minimum Qualifications: • Any combination of related clerical office experience, related undergraduate education and/or post high school clerical training that is the equivalent to two years of full-time employment and includes the use of word processing. Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: Are you an organized, customer-focused professional who enjoys helping others and keeping operations running smoothly? Join Iowa State University's Department of Residence Life as a Secretary II and play a key role in supporting a vibrant residential community. In this position, you will serve as a primary resource for students, families, staff, and campus partners, helping to ensure the efficient operation of one of Iowa State's residential communities. You will provide administrative support, coordinate communications and events, assist with financial and personnel processes, and contribute to a welcoming environment where students can live, learn, and thrive. This role is ideal for someone who enjoys variety in their work, excels at organization and customer service, and takes pride in supporting both people and processes in a fast-paced environment. What You'll Do Serve as a welcoming first point of contact for students, families, staff, and visitors. Support daily office operations and maintain accurate records, files, and documentation. Process purchasing, personnel, budgeting, and other administrative transactions. Monitor expenditures and assist with account reconciliation and budget tracking. Coordinate meetings, training sessions, programs, and departmental events. Prepare correspondence, reports, schedules, and communications for a variety of audiences. Generate reports and maintain data using university systems and office software. Partner with Residence Life staff to support programs, services, and initiatives that enhance the student experience. Help foster a welcoming and supportive environment where students can live, learn, and thrive. Preferred Qualifications: Experience providing administrative or office support in a professional, higher education, student affairs, or customer-service-focused environment. Demonstrated ability to provide exceptional customer service and effectively communicate with diverse audiences. Experience coordinating calendars, meetings, events, training sessions, or departmental activities. Experience processing financial, purchasing, payroll, personnel, or budget-related transactions. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications and experience maintaining records, reports, and data systems. Department/Program & College Description: The Department of Residence is one of the largest non-academic departments at Iowa State University, employing more than 400 full-time, part-time, and student staff members. Through its residence life, facilities, business, marketing, conference, and technology teams, the department provides supportive living and learning communities that help students thrive, succeed academically, and fully engage in the Iowa State experience. Department Unit/Website: Home - Department of Residence Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: 08 Original Posting Date: November 10, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 20, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20228 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Manager-Customer-Relations_R20241": {
      "title": "Manager Customer Relations",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-11\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Manager Customer Relations Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent and 5 years of related experience Job Description: The Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center, part of Iowa State University’s College of Veterinary Medicine, is a full-service teaching hospital offering advanced diagnostic, medical, and surgical care for small and large animals while supporting the education and training of future veterinarians. About the Role The Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center is seeking a Manager of Customer Relations with management experience and extensive patient or client service experience. This opportunity is well suited to a leader from patient access, patient relations, hospital registration, or medical practice operations who wants to apply those skills in a veterinary teaching hospital. You will lead Veterinary Teaching Hospital Assistants supporting reception, client communication, and patient flow across the Small Animal and Large Animal Hospitals. In this role, you will oversee staffing, scheduling, employee development, and client service operations in a fast-paced, 24/7 hospital. You will help staff navigate sensitive conversations, resolve concerns, and provide clear, compassionate communication to clients seeking care for their animals. Your experience coordinating service teams and working with clinical departments will help improve the client experience while supporting hospital operations and veterinary education. Key Responsibilities Lead and develop Veterinary Teaching Hospital Assistant teams across small and large animal hospital services, including hiring, onboarding, coaching, performance management, and employee development. Develop, implement, and maintain standard operating procedures and training programs that support consistent reception, client communication, and service delivery. Support hospital operations through data review, process improvement initiatives, and special projects, using available information and feedback to identify service gaps and evaluate improvements. Partner with service leaders and hospital administration to coordinate client-facing workflows, address operational barriers, and improve communication between reception and clinical teams. Serve as a resource for complex client concerns, coach staff in service recovery and de-escalation, and coordinate follow-up with clinical teams and hospital leadership. Establish clear service expectations and provide timely feedback, recognition, and training to strengthen team performance and the client experience. Monitor departmental supply and operational needs and support financial and purchasing processes. Oversee staffing plans, scheduling processes, and workforce management systems to coordinate coverage across shifts and support continuous 24/7 hospital operations. The primary work hours are 11:00 a.m. to 8:00 p.m. Flexibility is required to adjust the schedule to meet with, coach, and support employees working day, evening, and overnight shifts in a 24/7 hospital. Occasional morning meetings, weekend or holiday work, and coverage outside the primary schedule may be required to meet operational needs. Additional Details This is an on-site position within a veterinary teaching hospital. Work environment includes interaction with clinical areas and animal patients. Occasional coverage outside standard work hours may be required to support hospital operations. Position requires frequent movement throughout the hospital, including walking between service areas, standing for extended periods, and responding to operational needs across the facility. Ability to navigate both Small Animal and Large Animal Hospital areas while supporting staff, clients, and hospital operations. Why Join Us? Bring your management experience to a setting where skilled client service helps families navigate complex and often emotional decisions about their animals. Work alongside clinicians, faculty, students, and staff to connect compassionate service with advanced veterinary care and education. Shape reception workflows, strengthen communication, and help your team deliver a consistent client experience across hospital services. Make a direct impact through employee coaching, team development, and practical improvements to daily hospital operations. Preferred Qualifications: Experience managing teams in human healthcare, veterinary healthcare, higher education, hospitality, or other service-focused environments. Experience supervising, coaching, and developing employees, including performance management responsibilities. Experience interpreting and implementing workplace policies and procedures. Experience using scheduling, workforce management, electronic health record, or enterprise systems. Experience overseeing staffing, scheduling, and workforce coordination in a multi-shift or 24/7 environment. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Consideration Date: Applications received by November 20th, 2026 will be given full consideration. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS808 Original Posting Date: November 11, 2026 Posting Close Date: December 3, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20241 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Manager-Clinical-Support_R20242": {
      "title": "Manager Clinical Support",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-11\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Manager Clinical Support Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Associate’s degree and 5 years of related experience Job Description: The Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center, part of Iowa State University’s College of Veterinary Medicine, is a full service teaching hospital offering advanced diagnostic, medical, and surgical care for small and large animals while supporting the education and training of future veterinarians. The Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center (LVMC) within Iowa State University's College of Veterinary Medicine is seeking an experienced, collaborative, and people-focused leader to serve as the Manager, Clinical Support - Large Animal Hospital . This position provides leadership for a dynamic clinical support team and plays a critical role in advancing the hospital's mission of exceptional patient care, veterinary education, and clinical excellence. In this role, you will partner closely with clinicians, house officers, and hospital leadership to oversee daily operations within the Large Animal Hospital while supporting a team of veterinary technicians, animal caretakers, veterinary technician interns, and student employees. The successful candidate will be responsible for fostering a positive and inclusive workplace culture, developing employees, optimizing hospital operations, and ensuring high-quality patient care in a complex veterinary teaching environment. As a leader within our 24-hour teaching hospital, you will coordinate staffing across multiple shifts, support workforce planning efforts, drive continuous improvement initiatives, and help create an outstanding learning experience for veterinary students, interns, residents, and clinical support staff. This position offers a unique opportunity to influence the future of veterinary medicine through leadership, mentorship, and operational excellence. If you are passionate about developing people, strengthening teams, improving processes, and supporting exceptional patient care, we encourage you to apply. Key Responsibilities: Provide operational leadership and oversight for the Large Animal Hospital clinical support team. Supervise, coach, mentor, and develop veterinary technicians, veterinary technician interns, animal caretakers, and student employees, including hiring, onboarding, scheduling, performance management, and professional development. Coordinate staffing and employee schedules across multiple shifts to ensure appropriate coverage while supporting patient care, employee well-being, and operational needs. Oversee veterinary technician internship programs, including recruitment, selection, scheduling, orientation, mentorship, competency development, performance evaluation, and professional growth. Collaborate with faculty, house officers, clinical services, and hospital leadership to coordinate medical, diagnostic, and surgical procedures and ensure efficient hospital operations. Evaluate staffing, equipment, inventory, and facility needs and implement solutions to enhance operational efficiency, patient care, and employee effectiveness. Oversee inventory management, equipment maintenance, preventative maintenance programs, facility-related operational needs, and capital equipment planning. Support the teaching mission by partnering with clinical staff in training veterinary students and providing feedback regarding student performance during clinical rotations. Promote a collaborative, service-oriented culture focused on communication, accountability, continuous improvement, employee engagement, and exceptional client service. Develop, review, and maintain standard operating procedures and lead process improvement initiatives that enhance patient care, safety, efficiency, and regulatory compliance. Ensure compliance with hospital policies, university procedures, workplace safety standards, and applicable regulatory requirements. Serve as a key resource for communication, problem-solving, and relationship management among clinicians, staff, students, clients, and referring veterinarians. This position works both independently and collaboratively with hospital leadership, clinical services, and Veterinary Clinical Sciences within a large animal veterinary teaching hospital environment. Standard hours would be Monday - Friday 8:00AM to 5:00PM, some flexibility to work off scheduled hours to meet with employees who work different shifts. The Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center provides patient care 24 hours a day, 7 days a week, the manager must be available to support operational needs outside of normal business hours when necessary. This may include responding to urgent staffing issues, answering employee questions, and occasionally working evenings, weekends, holidays, or on-call shifts to ensure continuity of patient care. Additional Details: This is an on-site position within a veterinary teaching hospital. Work environment includes interaction with clinical areas and animal patients. Occasional coverage outside standard work hours may be required to support hospital operations. Position requires frequent movement throughout the hospital, including walking between service areas, standing for extended periods, and responding to operational needs across the facility. Ability to navigate both Small Animal and Large Animal Hospital areas while supporting staff, clients, and hospital operations. Why Join Us? At the Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center, you will have the opportunity to lead talented professionals, support the development of future veterinary practitioners, and contribute to one of the nation's leading veterinary teaching hospitals. This role offers the chance to make a lasting impact on patient care, employee development, hospital operations, and veterinary education. Preferred Qualifications Leadership or management experience in a veterinary, healthcare, agricultural, or related clinical environment, including supervision of staff, performance management, and employee development. Experience working in a veterinary teaching hospital, academic medical center, specialty referral practice, or similarly complex healthcare setting. Experience supporting veterinary technician, intern, resident, student, or clinical training programs within a teaching environment. Experience managing inventory, equipment, facilities-related operations, budgets, or operational resources. Experience leading teams within a 24/7 operational environment requiring complex staffing and scheduling. Licensed Veterinary Technician (RVT, CVT, or LVT) Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Consideration Date: Applications received by November 28th, 2026 will be given full consideration. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS808 Original Posting Date: November 11, 2026 Posting Close Date: December 4, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20242 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Residence-Hall-Coordinator_R20232": {
      "title": "Residence Hall Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-11\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Residence Hall Coordinator Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: Are you passionate about student success, leadership development, and building community? Iowa State University's Department of Residence Life is seeking a passionate student affairs professional to join our team as a Residence Hall Coordinator. This is an opportunity to do more than manage a residence hall. It is a chance to help students navigate one of the most transformative periods of their lives while building a community where they can learn, connect, and succeed.   As a live-in leader, you will play a central role in creating a residential experience grounded in our KCE model: Knowledge, Connection, and Empowerment. Every day brings opportunities to mentor student leaders, support residents through challenges and successes, foster a strong sense of belonging, and help students develop the skills and confidence they need to thrive both at Iowa State and beyond.   This live-in position includes a furnished apartment, meal plan, laundry, and parking accommodations. Most importantly, it offers the opportunity to build lasting relationships with students while contributing to a supportive campus environment.   If you are energized by student development, leadership education, community building, and helping students succeed, we encourage you to explore this exciting opportunity with Iowa State University's Residence Life team. What You'll Do Lead and manage the day-to-day operations of a residence hall community. Recruit, train, supervise, and develop undergraduate Community Advisor staff. Support students through academic, personal, and community-related concerns. Design and implement educational, leadership, and community engagement initiatives. Administer residence hall and university policies, including student conduct processes. Collaborate with Learning Communities, faculty, and campus partners to enhance the student experience. Coordinate key housing operations, including hall openings, closings, occupancy, and break periods. Partner with dining, facilities, maintenance, and custodial teams to support residential operations. Maintain records, prepare reports, and contribute to departmental goals and initiatives. Participate in an on-call rotation and respond to student and facility emergencies. Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated leadership experience in a college or university setting. Experience as a Resident Assistant (RA), Graduate Assistant (GA), or in a comparable student leadership role. Experience supervising staff or student employees, including hiring, training, and performance management. Demonstrated experience creating and facilitating student development initiatives aligned with the Knowledge, Connection, and Empowerment (KCE) framework, including student learning, engagement, leadership development, mentoring, or co-curricular programming. Experience with crisis response, conflict resolution, student conduct processes, and serving as a first-line responder to student incidents. Department/Program & College Description: The Department of Residence is one of the largest non-academic departments at Iowa State University, employing more than 400 full-time, part-time, and student staff members. Through its residence life, facilities, business, marketing, conference, and technology teams, the department provides supportive living and learning communities that help students thrive, succeed academically, and fully engage in the Iowa State experience. Department Unit/Website: Home - Department of Residence Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. This position is currently funded through June 30, 2027. Continued funding is anticipated, with the position eligible for renewal pending the availability of funding. This posting will be open until filled. However, to receive full consideration, applications need to be submitted before November 23rd, 2026. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular with Term Appointment (Fixed Term) Proposed End Date or Length of Term: June 30, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS805 Original Posting Date: November 11, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20232 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Administrative-Assistant-II_R20236": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant II",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-13\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Administrative Assistant II Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent and 3 years of related experience Job Description: The Department of History within the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences at Iowa State University is seeking a Part-Time Administrative Assistant II to support the department's daily front-office operations.   The successful administrative candidate will be highly organized, detail-oriented, and professional, with strong communication and interpersonal skills. They will be proactive, dependable, and able to serve as a primary point of contact while managing multiple responsibilities, coordinating schedules, and meeting important deadlines. They should be adaptable, resourceful, and comfortable working independently while providing excellent customer service and support to faculty, staff, students, and visitors.   Examples of Duties: Oversee daily front office operations, serve as the primary receptionist, greet visitors, answer phone calls and emails, and direct inquiries to appropriate campus resources. Manage department room reservations, faculty and staff meetings, departmental calendars, and important university deadlines. Process financial transactions, including purchasing cards, requisitions, travel arrangements, reimbursements, expense reports, and supply purchases. Maintain organized electronic and paper files, departmental directories, listservs, website information, and office supplies. Coordinate maintenance requests, copier services, key distribution, IT needs, and excess property disposal. Coordinate departmental events, invitations, RSVPs, catering, publicity materials, and campus recruitment activities. Assist with student hiring, onboarding, timekeeping, contract renewals, compensation changes, and employee separations. Provide administrative support for faculty reviews, scholarship coordination, student inquiries, recruitment, and academic program activities. Assist the department chair with correspondence, scheduling, special reports, deadlines, and administrative projects. Provide administrative support for African and African American Studies and backup support for the Department of Political Science. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's degree. Experience with Workday or similar administrative and financial management systems. Experience serving as a primary point of contact and providing administrative support in a professional office environment. Strong organizational skills, including managing calendars, coordinating schedules, and balancing multiple administrative responsibilities. Ability to prioritize tasks, manage competing deadlines, and ensure timely completion of assignments. This 20-hour-per-week appointment, with an expected work schedule of Monday through Friday. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Part time Pay Grade: PS806 Original Posting Date: November 13, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 23, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20236 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Program-Specialist-II_R20235": {
      "title": "Program Specialist II",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-13\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Program Specialist II Job Group: Professional & Scientific Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and 2 years of related experience Job Description: The Department of Food Science and Human Nutrition at Iowa State University is seeking a Program Specialist II to support research and development activities within the Polymer and Food Protection Consortium (PFPC). This position plays a key role supporting applied research projects, managing research projects, and communication with industry partners and PFPC faculty and staff.   The successful candidate will be highly organized, detail-oriented, and professional, with strong critical-thinking and problem-solving skills. They must be adaptable and able to thrive in a fast-paced environment, effectively manage multiple responsibilities, and adjust to changing priorities while maintaining productivity, accuracy, and attention to detail. Examples of Duties: Coordinate and monitor research projects to ensure objectives, deliverables, and timelines are met. Manage databases and documentation for major research initiatives, including total fluorine, packaging legislation, and post-consumer recycled materials. Collaborate with faculty, staff, and industry partners to develop and coordinate research projects. Serve as the primary liaison between research teams and industry partners. Prepare research reports, scholarly manuscripts, and industry presentations/webinars. Manage PFPC documentation, publications, grants, presentations, and membership records in CyBox. Monitor and coordinate day-to-day PFPC lab operations. Support personnel administration, including student hiring, timekeeping, and scheduling. Develop and implement marketing, promotional, and communication strategies. Manage internal and external communications, public relations, and outreach to inform university and industry stakeholders. Support the PFPC Director with communication planning and development. Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree in Business Administration (MBA) or a related field. Knowledge of packaging guidelines, standards, terminology, and industry practices. Experience in customer relations and building collaborative relationships with industry partners. Professional experience within the packaging industry. Why Join Us? At Iowa State University, you'll have the opportunity to contribute to innovative research focused on sustainability, recycling technologies, and advanced materials. You'll work alongside researchers, students, and industry partners while gaining experience with specialized processing equipment and applied research projects that have real-world impact. This is a one-year term position with opportunity for renewal. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program Iowa State offers WorkFlex options for some positions. WorkFlex offers flexibility on when, where, and how you do your work. For more information, please speak with the Hiring Manager. If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular with Term Appointment (Fixed Term) Proposed End Date or Length of Term: November 30, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: PS807 Original Posting Date: November 13, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 20, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20235 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Dairy-Farm-Custodian---Temporary_R20246": {
      "title": "Dairy Farm Custodian – Temporary",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-13\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Dairy Farm Custodian – Temporary Job Group: Merit Required Minimum Qualifications: • Ability to read, write, and follow instructions. Job Description: Summary of Duties and Responsibilities: Under direct supervision, performs custodial work required for the general maintenance of buildings at the ISU Dairy Farm. The successful candidate will perform these duties 12 – 18 hours per week on a flexible schedule determined by the successful candidate and the supervisor. Flexibility includes days of the week, time of day (morning/afternoon/evening), weekends, etc. Characteristic Duties and Responsibilities   • Performs cleaning in all areas of a building. • Performs cleaning of all floor areas such as vacuuming, shampooing, sweeping, mopping, stripping, scrubbing, waxing, and buffing. • Cleans and polishes all bathroom fixtures. • Cleans and washes all glass surfaces, ceilings and walls. • The use of a ladder up to 12 feet in height may be required. • Replaces light bulbs and cleans light fixtures, using a ladder as required. • Makes beds and handles both clean and soiled linens. • Refills holder of disposable items, such as soap, bathroom tissue, paper towels, etc. Cleans and disinfects beds, bedside tables, overbed tables, etc., and other equipment and areas. • Reports breakage and needed repairs. • Moves furniture, supplies and miscellaneous equipment; removes draperies and rugs periodically for cleaning; delivers supplies to various areas. • Collects trash from receptacles throughout the building and empties it into various areas. • Performs duties in the immediate exterior of building such as sweeping sidewalks, snow and ice removal at entrances, cleaning ash pits, cleaning debris from grounds and window wells, and cleaning exterior windows. • Locks and unlocks doors as required. • Assists in unloading trucks, unpacking, assembling, and moving equipment and furniture. • Picks up and returns equipment for repair by maintenance. • Delivers housekeeping supplies to designated areas. • Operates high pressure, water-cleaning apparatus to clean and disinfect rug runners, hospital equipment and showers. • Maintains inventory of linen and record of lined laundering; maintains inventory of custodial supplies, and keeps and prepares other records and reports as directed. Required Minimum Qualifications: - Ability to read, write, and follow instructions. Preferred Qualifications: - Prior custodial, janitorial, or commercial cleaning experience. - Experience with commercial cleaning equipment. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Temporary (Fixed Term) Proposed End Date or Length of Term: June 30, 2027 Number of Months Employed Per Year: Time Type: Part time Pay Grade: 0003a Original Posting Date: November 13, 2026 Posting Close Date: Job Requisition Number: R20246 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    },
    "https://isu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/IowaStateJobs/job/Ames-IA/Animal-Caretaker-III_R20210": {
      "title": "Animal Caretaker III",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-12\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Animal Caretaker III Job Group: Merit Required Minimum Qualifications: • Ability to read, write, and follow instructions. • Four years experience and/or education in animal care work, with demonstrated ability in the required skills, or American Association of Laboratory Animal Science full certification as a Laboratory Animal Technician with a minimum of three years applicable work experience. • Possession of a valid state or commercial driver's license, as required. Job Description: Want to take the next step in your veterinary career? The Hixson-Lied Small Animal Hospital at the Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center (LVMC) is seeking Animal Caretaker III to join our Small Animal Emergency & Critical Care (ECC) team. This fast-paced department provides advanced patient care 24 hours a day, 365 days a year, supporting animals with critical and emergency medical needs. This position serves as a frontline leader within the ECC team, providing guidance and support to Animal Caretakers while helping ensure exceptional patient care and efficient hospital operations. The successful candidate will coordinate daily work activities, assist with staff development and training, and work closely with veterinarians and veterinary technicians to maintain a safe, clean, and well-functioning clinical environment. What You'll Do: Provide day-to-day leadership, guidance, and support to Animal Caretakers I and II. Assist with hiring, onboarding, training, scheduling, and staff coverage coordination. Assign and prioritize work based on patient care needs and department workflow. Monitor task completion and provide coaching, instruction, and constructive feedback to team members. Support the daily operation of the ICU and Emergency & Critical Care service. Maintain inventory of medical supplies and coordinate equipment maintenance and facility-related requests. Ensure compliance with hospital cleaning, disinfection, and biosecurity protocols. Promote a safe, organized, and sanitary environment for patients, clients, and staff. Collaborate with veterinarians, veterinary technicians, and other hospital personnel to support high-quality patient care and infection prevention efforts. Help identify opportunities to improve efficiency, workflow, and service delivery within the department. Why Join Us? As part of a nationally recognized veterinary teaching hospital, you'll have the opportunity to work alongside highly skilled veterinary professionals while contributing to the care of complex and critical cases. This role offers the chance to combine hands-on animal care experience with leadership responsibilities in a collaborative, team-oriented environment.  Schedule: This position is expected to work a swing shift and will include evenings, weekends, and holidays. Flexibility is required to meet departmental staffing, workflow, and training needs. Department Unit/Website: https://vetmed.iastate.edu/vmc/ Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. Immigration sponsorship is not available for this position. Application Instructions: To apply for this position, please click on “Apply” and complete the Employment Application. Please be prepared to enter or attach the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Application/Cover Letter Why Choose Iowa State University? Iowa State Employees enjoy comprehensive health and work-life benefits, including medical and dental, as well as: Retirement benefits including defined benefit and defined contribution plans Generous vacation, holiday, and sick time and leave plans Onsite childcare (Ames, Iowa) Life insurance and long-term disability Flexible Spending Accounts Various voluntary benefits and discounts Employee Assistance Program Wellbeing program If you have questions regarding this application process, please email employment@iastate.edu, or call 515-294-4800 or Toll Free: 1-877-477-7485. Appointment Type: Regular Number of Months Employed Per Year: 12 Month Work Period Time Type: Full time Pay Grade: 7613a Original Posting Date: November 12, 2026 Posting Close Date: November 26, 2026 Job Requisition Number: R20210 Iowa State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, age, ethnicity, religion, national origin, pregnancy, sexual orientation, genetic information, sex, marital status, disability, or status as a U.S. Veteran. Inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies may be directed to Office of Equal Opportunity, 2680 Beardshear Hall, 515 Morrill Road, Ames, Iowa 50011, Tel. 515-294-7612, email eooffice@iastate.edu .   General ISU compensation information can be found on the University Human Resources website. Please note that this is only a list of ranges and individuals will be paid commensurate with qualifications."
    }
